(window.PF_CAT_SHARD=window.PF_CAT_SHARD||{})["76456"]={"2519":{"i":"2519","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Master of Applied Management is one of the following: an NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) in the Business or Management field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B average (as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system); or a Bachelor Honours or Postgraduate degree in the Business or Management field with 120 credits at Level 8; or a degree or equivalent professional qualification in a related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a -B average (as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system) and evidence of management experience at degree level, and assessment from the programme coordinator; Or at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. [A Master of Applied Management applicant who does not meet the entry criteria above may be admitted to the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management and, upon successful completion of four courses (with a minimum B average) from the Schedule to the Regulations, be admitted to the Master of Applied Management.] Applicants from countries in which English is not the primary spoken language must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in the programme. Ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include (i) completion of a programme of study in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply*), and (ii) approved scores on IELTS tests, namely an Academic score of 6.5 with no band lower than 6 (or accepted international equivalents). An international student must be in possession of an appropriate visa for the duration of the Programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The degree may be taken by coursework, thesis and coursework or thesis. The Master of Applied Management is designed to apply an advanced and discursive body of knowledge to a graduate's applied management knowledge and skills within the aims of the postgraduate programmes. A student undertaking a Master of Applied Management is required to complete courses across a range of areas of professional competence as approved by the Programme Coordinator. This requirement ensures that graduates in the Master of Applied Management gain breadth and depth of professional competence in their postgraduate studies consistent with the philosophy of the programmes. Selection of courses will take into account individual level of competency, together with the attainment of all graduate attributes.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Management will: show evidence of advanced knowledge and mastery of sophisticated theoretical subject matter in the areas of professional competence demonstrate evidence of leadership skills in a business context Graduates will be able to demonstrate the following professional attributes in a business context: Critical thinking and problem solving apply independent rigorous intellectual analysis to management decisions critically and effectively diagnose existing and emerging business problems in order to produce optimal solutions Planning and change management skills work both independently and co-operatively to make, and implement, strategic and operational business plans apply advanced knowledge to new situations and generate new solutions adapt to emerging paradigms within the profession Research and informational skills critically evaluate findings and discussions in applied management literature apply business and/or management research in industry research, analyse, and argue from evidence Communication skills effectively communicate business decisions and information both written and orally communicate across cultures within a business context.","educationPathway":"The Master's Degree achieved to an appropriate standard may provide a pathway to a programme of advanced study and/or original research leading to a doctoral degree such as PhD, DBA or other professional doctoral qualifications. The offering institute may require the student to first complete some additional study or research before allowing provisional entry or direct entry.\"","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2519"},"2520":{"i":"2520","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Postgraduate Certificate and Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management is one of the following: * an NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) in Business or Management; or * an undergraduate degree in a related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- average (as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system), subject to assessment by the programme coordinator; or * Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management deepens and broadens applied knowledge well beyond initial undergraduate level. The programme enables completion of a comprehensive body of knowledge in management relevant to specific individual's aspirations and is likely to align closely to the context of a small to medium-sized enterprise. Individuals are prepared for research, and its application to management improvement initiatives. The programme aims to develop scholarship, problem-solving and critical thinking to advanced levels.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management will show evidence of advanced technical and theoretical knowledge in the areas of professional competence. Graduates will also be able to demonstrate the following professional attributes in a business context: Critical thinking and problem solving engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism, and problem-solving in a business context diagnose business problems critically and logically in order to arrive at optimal solutions Planning and change management skills devise, and implement, strategic and operational business plans apply technical and theoretical knowledge to manage and control complex situations and to generate new solutions Research and informational skills find and use information to extend research work and consolidate knowledge in business practice apply business and/or management research in industry Communication skills effectively communicate business decisions and information both written and orally demonstrate understanding of communication issues across cultures within a business context.","educationPathway":"* The Postgraduate Diploma achieved to an appropriate standard provides a pathway to enrol in a Master's Degree.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2520"},"2527":{"i":"2527","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Postgraduate Certificate and Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management is one of the following: \n\r\nan NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) in Business or Management; \n\r\nor \n\r\nan undergraduate degree in a related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- average (as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system), subject to assessment by the programme coordinator; \n\r\nor \n\r\nDean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management stimulates initial development of critical thinking in applied management through extending undergraduate achievement in areas related to their original accomplishment. The programme enables recent graduates opportunities for academic achievement in advance of their undergraduate qualifications and to make a solid start in higher level, constructive and functional applications of knowledge and initial management experience. The programme enables people already working in management roles to commence applied professional development related to their employment context and potentially of direct improvement impact on those businesses. This qualification is suitable for students who want to enter the Master Programme, but who do not meet the entry requirements, or students who only want to obtain a specific body of knowledge without a research project. All courses in the Master of Applied Management programme at level eight are available to students enrolled in the Postgraduate Certificate and Diploma in Applied Management.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management will show evidence of advanced knowledge in the areas of professional competence as identified in the philosophy of the programmes. Graduates will also be able to demonstrate the following professional attributes in a business context: Critical thinking and problem solving think clearly, rationally, and independently when making applied management decisions diagnose and analyse business problems logically in order to produce optimal solutions Planning and change management skills contribute to the development and implementation of strategic and operational business plans Research and informational skills find, and use, information to extend research work and consolidate knowledge in business practice Communication skills communicate management decisions and information both written and orally demonstrate awareness of communication issues across cultures within a business context.","educationPathway":"Further Postgraduate study","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2527"},"2566":{"i":"2566","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree (or equivalent) in business or related subject. International students: IELTS 6.5 (with no band below 6.0), or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Management Students enables students to advance and deepen their knowledge of management and extend their interpersonal and technical skills.  As a result, they may be able to obtain employment at a higher level than their previous qualifications and experience made possible. Graduates will be able to use their enhanced knowledge, skills and capabilities to obtain employment in positions of responsibility that relate to the electives they choose and/or to proceed to further studies, such as a Postgraduate Diploma or Master's degree in Management.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Management programme will be able to:  \n\r\n* acknowledge that the world views of leaders and managers impact how values and philosophies shape leadership and management decision making   \n\r\n* work effectively in bicultural and multicultural teams and exercise leadership as required  \n\r\n* engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving  \n\r\n* learn independently and appreciate the need for continued learning  \n\r\n* apply advanced knowledge and interpersonal and technical skills to practical situations  \n\r\n* critically evaluate research literature and research findings in management studies and their application in organisations  \n\r\n* identify, analyse and address ethical issues in leadership and management in practical and applied situations  \n\r\n* analyse and argue from evidence  \n\r\n* undertake further postgraduate study","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Management may be admitted into the Whitireia Postgraduate Diploma in Management (with credit) or the Whitireia Master of Management (with credit) or into other master's programmes in New Zealand or overseas.","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2566"},"2567":{"i":"2567","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree (or equivalent) in business or related subject  \n\n\n\r\nWork experience deemed equivalent means at least three years in a Manager or Senior Manager role in accounting, finance, marketing, hospitality, information systems, general management or similar. \n\n\n\r\nApplicants with a degree in a discipline or subject area other than business may be accepted subject to Programme Manager approval, based on evidence of the applicant's additional skills and knowledge through relevant work experience equivalent to the above.  \n\n\n\r\nInternational students: IELTS 6.5 (with no band below 6.0), or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the postgraduate programmes is to enable students to gain internationally recognised skills and knowledge in management with an area of specialisation to assist New Zealand in its drive toward a knowledge-based economy. The Postgraduate Diploma allows students to gain a deep understanding of management topics and associated specialisations and prepares them for undertaking further independent research and scholarship in management studies. Students have an opportunity to enrol in elective courses that allow them to apply learned skills to real life examples, projects and scenarios. Graduates are able to use their enhanced knowledge, skills and capabilities to obtain employment in positions of responsibility that relate to the electives they choose and/or to proceed to further studies, such as a master's degree in management.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Management programme will be able to:  \n\r\n* acknowledge that the world views of leaders and managers impact how values and philosophies shape leadership and management decision making   \n\r\n* communicate effectively (orally, visually and in writing) with people of different cultures  \n\r\n* work effectively in bicultural and multicultural teams and exercise leadership as required  \n\r\n* engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving  \n\r\n* learn independently and appreciate the need for continued learning  \n\r\n* apply advanced knowledge and professional and managerial skills to practical and new situations  \n\r\n* critically evaluate research literature and research findings in management studies and their application in organisations  \n\r\n* identify, analyse and address ethical issues in leadership and management in practical and applied situations  \n\r\n* plan, conduct and report on small-scale research projects  \n\r\n* analyse and argue from evidence  \n\r\n* undertake further postgraduate study","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Management may be admitted into the Whitireia Master of Management with credit or into other master's programmes in New Zealand or overseas.","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2567"},"2568":{"i":"2568","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree (or equivalent) in business or related subject with at least a B grade average at level 7 (or 8) Work experience deemed equivalent means at least three years in a Manager or Senior Manager role in accounting, finance, marketing, hospitality, information systems, general management or similar. Applicants with a degree in a discipline or subject area other than business may be accepted subject to Programme Manager approval, based on evidence of the applicant's additional skills and knowledge through relevant work experience equivalent to the above. International students: IELTS 6.5 (with no band below 6.0), or equivalent To enrol in BUS9502 Thesis or BUS9503 Dissertation requires a B average in Level 8 courses.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The primary aim of this programme is to enable students to gain internationally recognised skills and knowledge in management with an area of specialisation to assist New Zealand in its drive toward a knowledge-based economy. Students have an opportunity to enrol in elective papers that allow them to apply learned skills to real life examples, projects and scenarios. Students gain skills to apply an advanced body of knowledge in Management studies and associated specialisations in a range of contexts for research, further learning and professional practice. Graduates are able to use their enhanced knowledge, skills and capabilities to obtain employment in positions of responsibility that relate to the electives they choose and/or to proceed to further studies, such as a doctorate degree.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Management programme will be able to:    \n\r\n* acknowledge that the world views of managers impact how values and philosophies shape management and leadership decision making    \n\r\n* communicate effectively (orally, visually and in writing) with people of different cultures    \n\r\n* work effectively in bicultural and multicultural teams and exercise leadership as required    \n\r\n* engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving    \n\r\n* learn independently and appreciate the need for continued learning    \n\r\n* apply advanced knowledge in management studies and associated skills to practical and new situations    \n\r\n* critically evaluate current literature and research findings in Management Studies and their application in organisations    \n\r\n* research, analyse and argue from evidence    \n\r\n* identify, analyse and address ethical issues in management in practical and applied situations    \n\r\n* plan, execute and complete a piece of original research or an applied research project, relevant to industry stakeholders    \n\r\n* undertake further postgraduate study","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Master of Management who have completed a 90 credit thesis with a good grade and obtained good grades across their level 8 papers, usually a B+ average, may be admitted to doctoral programmes in New Zealand or overseas, or other postgraduate programmes.","developedBy":"New Zealand Institute of Skills and Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2568"},"2830":{"i":"2830","entryRequirements":"Entry Requirements Applicants require a Bachelor's degree (or equivalent) in business, management or a related hospitality area, with at least a B- grade average at level 7 (or higher). Degrees in other disciplines may be considered if the applicant has at least three years' relevant hospitality experience at a supervisory level, or equivalent. In addition, applicants for whom English is not their first language require an IELTS score of 6.5, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Master of Hotel Management programme is to enhance students' abilities to a) Manage job related activities at operational levels such as food and beverage, front office, housekeeping, materials management, b) Interact and deal effectively with employees, guests, peers and superiors, c) Undertake project development and conduct needs analyses and feasibility studies, d) Visualise long term goals for the property, e) Assist in new product and services development, f) Conceptualise multifarious problems and provide appropriate solutions, g) Develop and formulate strategic concepts in relation to all available resources and the company's objectives, h) Conceptualise the structure and nature of the hospitality industry in a national and international context, i) Display professional attitudes in developing and maintaining effective interpersonal skills, j) Develop quality standards in service delivery in the hospitality industry and design evaluation methodologies to maintain these standards, k) Develop policies and procedures to evaluate technical competencies in the major areas of the hospitality industry, l) Manage computer based management and information systems for financial control, budget and planning, materials management, marketing, sales and personnel, m) Promote and market the activities within a hospitality organisation, n) Apply analytical, problem solving and creative thinking skills to manage change and to further diagnose and appraise project design, review and management, o) Organise appropriate productivity evaluators which will produce pre determined profit levels to the organisation, and p) Promote moral and ethical guidelines relevant to management roles. The Master of Hotel Management programme will produce graduates who will be able to 1) Formulate a research proposal, critically review the relevant literature, gather and analyse appropriate data, and present results and recommendations in a professional manner in both written and oral forms, 2) Reflect on the foundations of good management and leadership, and relate academic and operational learning to implement the requirements of a supervisory role, 3) Apply key accounting performance indicators with an understanding of the outcomes of these components and what they mean to the hospitality manger, 4) Critically evaluate the impact of hospitality and contemporary tourism marketing on a hospitality enterprise, 5) Evaluate Human Resources Management practices and synthesise strategies to improve company employee relations and productivity, 6) Communicate effectively with customers, suppliers, and co workers at various levels, 7) Either evaluate all aspects of food and beverage management with the view to maximize guest satisfaction and financial returns, develop strategies and integrate food and beverage into the wider hotel operation or develop strategies both operationally and technically to optimize the utilization of Rooms Division resources, customer satisfaction and reduction of risk. As required by NZQA (see Appendix 7), the programme and individual courses have been designed to ensure that graduates will demonstrate the outcomes of a Master's degree, namely, a) Show evidence of advanced knowledge about a specialist field of enquiry or professional practice, b) Engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem solving, c) Demonstrate mastery of sophisticated theoretical subject matter, d) Evaluate critically the finding and discussions in the literature, e) Work independently and apply knowledge to new situations, f) Research, analyse and argue from evidence.","graduateProfile":"Educational Pathways Students who have successfully completed the Master of Hotel Management may seek admission to research master's or doctoral programmes in New Zealand or overseas. Employment Pathways Students who have successfully completed the Master of Hotel Management and have (or gain) appropriate practical experience may obtain employment in a wide range of managerial positions in the hospitality and tourism industry, including Facilities and Logistics Manager, Food and Beverage Manager, Front Office Manager, General Manager, Hotel Manager, Housekeeping Manager, Human Resources Manager, International Manager, Marketing and Sales Manager, Regional Manager, Rooms Division Manager, Training Manager.","developedBy":"Pacific International Hotel Management School Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=2830"},"3015":{"i":"3015","entryRequirements":"Academic: Applicants must have a Bachelor's degree or a Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a similar subject, OR relevant skills and knowledge acquired through appropriate work or professional experience. \n\r\nAlternative: Applicants who are unable to evidence that they meet Academic Entry Requirements, but who can demonstrate acquired skills for tertiary study gained through study, work and/or life experience, may be approved for alternative entry. This may include Recognition of Prior Learning.  \n\r\nEnglish language: If English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency Outcomes Table: IELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.0 in each band). Note: Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact NMIT for an assessment. Note: Applicants who have achieved NCEA Level 3 University Entrance requirements are not required to provide evidence of English language skills.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the PGDipIB states that the programme will produce work-ready graduates with the personal attributes, advanced specialised knowledge and practical skills necessary to make an immediate and innovative contribution to organisations engaged in or wishing to engage in, international business whether locally, nationally or internationally.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will demonstrate a critical understanding of the key principles underpinning the international business environment and the place of New Zealand within that environment.","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"Nelson Marlborough Institute of Technology (NMIT)","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3015"},"3191":{"i":"3191","entryRequirements":"Application and Selection Criteria \n\r\nApplication and selection criteria for the postgraduate applied management programme are as follows: \n\r\nStudents will have completed all requirements of a relevant bachelor's degree or graduate diploma or postgraduate certificate with at least a B grade average at level 7 or higher. \n\r\nSpecial Admission \n\r\nNotwithstanding the above admission criteria, in exceptional circumstances, a mature aged applicant who can show evidence of ability to succeed in the programmes may be considered for admission, provided the applicant has successfully completed an approved course or programme, or has relevant work experience, which is deemed to meet the required standard for entry. \n\r\nProvisional Part-time Admission \n\r\nAn applicant, who does not meet academic criteria, may be provisionally admitted to enrol in one or more papers. Upon successful completion of the paper(s), the student may apply for special admission or admission by mature entry. \n\r\nAdditional Criteria \n\r\nIn addition, the following requirements also apply to all applicants in all admission categories. \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate of at least 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English, are required to provide evidence of having passed an NZQA English Proficiency Assessment, or one of the following tests of English language competence in accordance with the NZQA rules below: \n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6 \n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE) \n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21) \n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill. \n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement \n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58) \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42 \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate below 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English must provide evidence that they: \n\r\na) Have gained NCEA Level 3 and met New Zealand University Entrancerequirements or \n\r\nb) Hold a bachelor's degree of at least 3 years from New Zealand, Australia, Canada, The Republic of Ireland, South Africa, United Kingdom or United States of America or \n\r\nc) Have achieved a Certificate in English Language Teaching to Adults, CELTA or \n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6 \n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE) \n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21) \n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of \n\r\n176. No less than 169 in each skill. \n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement \n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58) \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42 \n\r\nAll enrolments in the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management are approved at the discretion of the Programme Manager in consultation with the Head of Faculty and teaching staff as required. \n\r\nSelection Criteria \n\r\nRight of entry into programmes of study is restricted by SIT and apparent eligibility may not lead to automatic acceptance. Applicants must demonstrate attributes that, in the assessment of SIT, should lead to success. \n\r\nWhere SIT is satisfied that it is necessary to do so because of insufficiency of staff, accommodation, or equipment it may determine the maximum number of students who may be enrolled in a particular course of study. Where the number of applications for enrolment exceeds the number of places in any case where such a limitation applies, the criteria for selection shall be academic merit and suitability for admission to that course of study. Eligible students not admitted to their chosen course of study will be placed on a waiting list and/or referred to another programme. Applications should be received by SIT no later than the due date. Late applications may be considered, subject to availability of places. \n\r\nApplicants may be required to attend an interview, or if they live at some distance from the campus, complete a telephone interview. Applicants may be required to provide copies of applicable certificates and evidence of previous achievements prior to the interview date.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management is aimed at management practitioners wishing to undertake a short programme of study in order to extend and update their management knowledge and skills. Public and private sector organisations employing graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management will benefit from the knowledge and skills that the graduates have acquired during their programme of study.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management will be able to:  \n\r\n* assess corporate social responsibility issues and determine appropriate responses  \n\r\n* apply acquired knowledge and skills in practical management situations  \n\r\n* evaluate evidence in order to support a management course of action  \n\r\n* show evidence of advanced knowledge about management practice  \n\r\n* work effectively in teams","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate will be able to pathway to further postgraduate programmes, such as the Postgraduate Diploma  in Applied Management or the Master of Applied Management.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3191"},"3192":{"i":"3192","entryRequirements":"Application and Selection Criteria\n\r\nApplication and selection criteria for the postgraduate applied management programme are as follows:\n\r\nStudents will have completed all requirements of a relevant bachelor's degree or graduate diploma or postgraduate certificate with at least a B grade average at level 7 or higher.\n\r\nSpecial Admission\n\r\nNotwithstanding the above admission criteria, in exceptional circumstances, a mature aged applicant who can show evidence of ability to succeed in the programmes may be considered for admission, provided the applicant has successfully completed an approved course or programme, or has relevant work experience, which is deemed to meet the required standard for entry.\n\r\nProvisional Part-time Admission\n\r\nAn applicant, who does not meet academic criteria, may be provisionally admitted to enrol in one or more papers. Upon successful completion of the paper(s), the student may apply for special admission or admission by mature entry.\n\r\nAdditional Criteria\n\r\nIn addition, the following requirements also apply to all applicants in all admission categories.\n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate of at least 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English, are required to provide evidence of having passed an NZQA English Proficiency Assessment, or one of the following tests of English language competence in accordance with the NZQA rules below:\n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6\n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE)\n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21)\n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill.\n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement\n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58)\n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42\n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate below 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English must provide evidence that they:\n\r\na) Have gained NCEA Level 3 and met New Zealand University Entrancerequirements or\n\r\nb) Hold a bachelor's degree of at least 3 years from New Zealand, Australia, Canada, The Republic of Ireland, South Africa, United Kingdom or United States of America or\n\r\nc) Have achieved a Certificate in English Language Teaching to Adults, CELTA or\n\r\nIELTS test - Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6\n\r\nTOEFL Paper based test (pBT) - Score of 590 (with an essay score 5.5 TWE)\n\r\nTOEFL Internet- based test (iBT) - Score of 79 (with a writing score of 21)\n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations - CAE or CPE with a score of\n\r\n176. No less than 169 in each skill.\n\r\nNZCEL - Level 5 with the Academic endorsement\n\r\nPearson Test of English (Academic) - PToE (Academic score of 58)\n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL - C1 Expert with a score of 42\n\r\nAll enrolments in the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management are approved at the discretion of the Programme Manager in consultation with the Head of Faculty and teaching staff as required.\n\r\nSelection Criteria\n\r\nRight of entry into programmes of study is restricted by SIT and apparent eligibility may not lead to automatic acceptance. Applicants must demonstrate attributes that, in the assessment of SIT, should lead to success.\n\r\nWhere SIT is satisfied that it is necessary to do so because of insufficiency of staff, accommodation, or equipment it may determine the maximum number of students who may be enrolled in a particular course of study. Where the number of applications for enrolment exceeds the number of places in any case where such a limitation applies, the criteria for selection shall be academic merit and suitability for admission to that course of study. Eligible students not admitted to their chosen course of study will be placed on a waiting list and/or referred to another programme. Applications should be received by SIT no later than the due date. Late applications may be considered, subject to availability of places.\n\r\nApplicants may be required to attend an interview, or if they live at some distance from the campus, complete a telephone interview. Applicants may be required to provide copies of applicable certificates and evidence of previous achievements prior to the interview date.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management is aimed at management practitioners and recent graduates (domestic and international) wishing to undertake a comprehensive programme of study in order to upgrade their qualifications and extend their management knowledge and skills with the objective of obtaining employment or advancing their careers. Public and private sector organisations employing graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management will benefit from the broad knowledge and skill set (including problem-solving and team work) that the graduates have acquired during their programme of study.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management will be able to: \n\r\n* contribute effectively to multi-person projects and teamwork in an organisation, including as a team leader \n\r\n* show evidence of advanced knowledge about specialist areas of management \n\r\n* recognise, evaluate and address management-related ethical issues  \n\r\n* apply theoretical concepts to solve practical management problems \n\r\n* gather, evaluate and analyse information from a variety of sources \n\r\n* demonstrate the capacity for critical thinking","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma will be able to pathway on to the Master of Applied Management.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3192"},"3193":{"i":"3193","entryRequirements":"Application and Selection Criteria Application and selection criteria for the postgraduate applied management programme are as follows: Students will have completed all requirements of a relevant bachelors degree or graduate diploma or postgraduate certificate or postgraduate diploma with at least a B grade average at level 7 or higher.   \n\r\nSpecial Admission   \n\r\nNotwithstanding the above admission criteria, in exceptional circumstances, a mature aged applicant who can show evidence of ability to succeed in the programmes may be considered for admission, provided the applicant has successfully completed an approved course or programme, or has relevant work experience, which is deemed to meet the required standard for entry.   \n\r\nProvisional Part time Admission   \n\r\nAn applicant, who does not meet academic criteria, may be provisionally admitted to enrol in one or more papers. Upon successful completion of the papers, the student may apply for special admission or admission by mature entry.   \n\r\nAdditional Criteria  \n\r\nIn addition, the following requirements also apply to all applicants in all admission categories.   \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate of at least 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English, are required to provide evidence of having passed an NZQA approved English Proficiency Assessment, or one of the following tests of English language competence in accordance with the NZQA rules below  \n\r\nIELTS test Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6; TOEFL Paper based test pBT Score of 590 with an essay score 5.5; TWE TOEFL Internet based test iBT Score of 79 with a writing score of 21;   \n\r\nUniversity of Cambridge ESOL Examinations CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill;   \n\r\nNZCEL Level 5 with the Academic endorsement;   \n\r\nPearson Test of English Academic PToE Academic score of 58;   \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL C1 Expert with a score of 42.   \n\r\nApplicants from countries with an annual student visa approval rate below 80 per cent, whose first language is not English, or who come from a country where the language of instruction in schools is not English must provide evidence that they:   \n\r\nHave gained NCEA Level 3 and met New Zealand University Entrance requirements; or   \n\r\nHold a bachelors degree of at least 3 years from New Zealand, Australia, Canada, The Republic of Ireland, South Africa, United Kingdom or United States of America; or   \n\r\nHave achieved a Certificate in English Language Teaching to Adults, CELTA; or   \n\r\nIELTS test Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6; TOEFL Paper based test pBT Score of 590 with an essay score 5.5; TTOEFL Internet based test iBT Score of 79 with a writing score of 21; University of Cambridge ESOL Examinations CAE or CPE with a score of 176. No less than 169 in each skill;   \n\r\nNZCEL Level 5 with the Academic endorsement Pearson Test of English Academic PToE Academic score of 58;   \n\r\nCity of Guilds IESOL C1 Expert with a score of 42.   \n\r\nAll enrolments in the Master of Applied Management are approved at the discretion of the Programme Manager in consultation with the Head of Faculty and teaching staff as required.  \n\r\nSelection Criteria   \n\r\nRight of entry into programmes of study is restricted by SIT and apparent eligibility may not lead to automatic acceptance. Applicants must demonstrate attributes that, in the assessment of SIT, should lead to success. Where SIT is satisfied that it is necessary to do so because of insufficiency of staff, accommodation, or equipment it may determine the maximum number of students who may be enrolled in a particular course of study. Where the number of applications for enrolment exceeds the number of places in any case where such a limitation applies, the criteria for selection shall be academic merit and suitability for admission to that course of study. Eligible students not admitted to their chosen course of study will be placed on a waiting list and/or referred to another programme. Applications should be received by SIT no later than the due date. Late applications may be considered, subject to availability of places. Applicants may be required to attend an interview, or if they live at some distance from the campus, complete a telephone interview. Applicants may be required to provide copies of applicable certificates and evidence of previous achievements prior to the interview date.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Applied Management is aimed at management practitioners and recent graduates (domestic and international) wishing to undertake an advanced programme of study in order to prepare for further study or to assist with obtaining a more senior position. Public and private sector organisations employing graduates of the Master of Applied Management will benefit from the advanced knowledge and capabilities (including analytical, managerial and research) that the graduates have acquired during their programme of study.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Management will be able to: design, carry out and communicate the results of significant research projects in the field of management studies and relate the findings to the professional and research literature; analyse and critique professional and research publications in management studies and related subject areas, identify practical applications and relate findings to their own research; evaluate the positive and negative impacts of business and management practices on society and address related ethical and professional issues; demonstrate mastery of complex concepts and theories in the field of management studies and their application in solving practical problems; apply their analytical, managerial and research capabilities to unfamiliar situations involving the application of management practices; think critically and act responsibly when confronted with academic or professional challenges; demonstrate high levels of skill in a management or research role in an organisation.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Management will be able to: design, carry out and communicate the results of significant research projects in the field of management studies and relate the findings to the professional and research literature; analyse and critique professional and research publications in management studies and related subject areas, identify practical applications and relate findings to their own research; evaluate the positive and negative impacts of business and management practices on society and address related ethical and professional issues; demonstrate mastery of complex concepts and theories in the field of management studies and their application in solving practical problems; apply their analytical, managerial and research capabilities to unfamiliar situations involving the application of management practices; think critically and act responsibly when confronted with academic or professional challenges; demonstrate high levels of skill in a management or research role in an organisation.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3193"},"3337":{"i":"3337","entryRequirements":"Academic entry and admission requirements are in accordance with Waiariki's Academic Regulations and the following criteria: \n\r\nApplicants will be required to submit a 400-word statement about their professional goals and rationale for seeking entry into this programme. Applicants may be interviewed in person or via Skype to evaluate their suitability to enter the programme. \n\r\nAll applicants must possess: \n\r\n* a graduate diploma at NZQA Level 7 or equivalent; or \n\r\n* an undergraduate degree or equivalent; or  \n\r\n* a bachelor's honours degree, or a postgraduate certificate, or the equivalent at Level 8. \n\r\nProvisional Entry: Applicants who do not meet the standard entry above in a relevant field for the Postgraduate Diploma in Management, but present evidence of ability to succeed, require a combination of academic and practical or professional experience:  \n\r\n* a three-year post-secondary school diploma in a related discipline at NZQA Level 7 or equivalent from a recognised tertiary provider, and demonstration of at least three years' equivalent practical or professional experience at a managerial level with at least two written references; or  \n\r\n* demonstration of at least five years' equivalent practical or professional experience at a senior management level, evidence of ability to study at postgraduate level, and three written references (as an employee and of your character). \n\r\nEnglish Language Competency:  Applicants much have an overall International English Language Testing System (IELTS) score of at least 6.5 (Academic) with no band less than 6.0, or equivalent, where English is not the primary spoken language. Where English is the first language, Waiariki may require students to achieve 65 on the Waiariki English Test.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Management is designed for domestic and international students seeking to advance scholarly research and practice-informed management. It will build on previous undergraduate degree, graduate and postgraduate studies and strengthen career aspirations within fields of management, business, health, hospitality, or information technology.  \n\r\nThe advanced standard at which the graduates will operate includes the ability to articulate theory and practice within a management scope. Graduates will engage in independent study demonstrating an advanced level of knowledge and employing discourse analysis and critical enquiry in a relevant management context. \n\r\nThrough work-integrated practice and advancing theoretical knowledge, the graduates will extend management capabilities to generate solutions to complex problems, particularly (but not exclusively) in the areas of business, health, hospitality, or information technology.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of this qualification Graduates will:  \n\r\n* have advanced knowledge and skills relevant to their chosen field to be able to: critically evaluate research methodologies and frameworks and their application within advanced management studies in the New Zealand management context; manage and instigate growth and positive change through the application of advanced bodies of knowledge; engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, critique and problem-solving; develop and implement work-integrated management plans, and potentially evaluate their outcomes; investigate a significant challenge, propose a solution and present findings;  and develop advanced applied research proposals. \n\r\n* have advanced knowledge and skills in their selection of core management areas to be able to: interact and communicate effectively with people of diverse ethnicities and cultures in context; analyse, improve and implement quality management systems in organisations; analyse human and resource management theories, models and systems;  evaluate a range of financial methods and approaches to utilising financial assets reflecting their significance in management roles; and/or evaluate the outcome of work-integrated advanced specialized management activities.  \n\r\n* possess values and attitudes consistent with their management practices.","educationPathway":"Graduates with a graduate diploma at NZQA Level 7 or equivalent, an undergraduate degree, a bachelor's honours degree, or a postgraduate certificate in a relevant endorsement may be admitted into the Postgraduate Diploma programme. Graduates from the Postgraduate Diploma in Management with a B average may be admitted to the Master of Management.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3337"},"3341":{"i":"3341","entryRequirements":"Students must: * Be able to access a relevant workplace; and * Have a Bachelor degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a cognate subject; or * Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies (with or without endorsement) or in cognate subject for entry to the Postgraduate Diploma; or * A combination of academic and practical or professional experience based upon a record of learning (academic transcript), parchment and a curriculum vitae detailing relevant educational achievements work experience and professional achievements as follows: EITHER * completion of a post-secondary school diploma in a related discipline at NZQA level 7 or equivalent from a recognised tertiary provider; and * demonstration of at least two years relevant practical experience with at least two written references (employer and character); or * demonstration of at least five years relevant practical or professional experience at a senior level, evidence of ability to study at postgraduate qualification level and two written references (employer and character); * IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching endorsements; or * IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control endorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies programme will enable learners to further their knowledge and professional practice in their field of practice. Students will be able to apply an advanced body of knowledge in a range of contexts that will compliment their current experience and/or qualifications. This qualification enables professionals in leadership roles to maintain currency and develop their discipline by ongoing professional development.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies, graduates will be able to: * Supervise and mentor others in their field of study; * Communicate effectively in an inter and intracultural environment; * Work across interdisciplinary boundaries; * Critically evaluate existing research; * Use research to solve problems; and * Work as reflective practitioners.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies will be eligible for entry to the Master of Applied Professional Studies programme or further Postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3341"},"3346":{"i":"3346","entryRequirements":"One of the below for admission:\n\r\n1. Bachelor Honours degree or Postgraduate Certificate\n\r\n2. Graduate Diploma at L7\n\r\n3. Undergraduate degree\n\r\n4. Special entry, courses and/or experience\n\r\nAND English language competency where English is not a first language.  All students:\n\r\nEnglish language competency where English is not a first language.\n\r\n* International applicants for whom English is not their first language will be required to show evidence of language competency, issued within the last two years. The level of competency required is:\n\r\no IELTS Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0,\n\r\no or an equivalent as outlined in NZQF-related rules (Rule 18).\n\r\n* For domestic applicants for whom English is not their first language, evidence of language competency may be required.\n\r\nThere are four pathways to admission to the Postgraduate Certificate in Management programme9:\n\r\n1. Bachelor Honours Degree or Postgraduate Certificate.\n\r\n2. A Graduate Diploma at level 710: Graduate Diploma in business or management or endorsement area or equivalent\n\r\n3. An undergraduate degree11: Bachelor in business or management or endorsement area or equivalent.\n\r\n4. Special entry12 - Applicants who do not meet any of the academic requirements may be given special admission if they can provide evidence that they are capable of achieving the programme outcomes through a combination of academic and practical or professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate is designed for domestic and international students seeking to broaden scholarly research and management capabilities. It will build on previous undergraduate degree, graduate studies and/or strengthen career aspirations within fields of management, business, health, hospitality or information technology. The standard at which the graduate will operate includes the ability to conceptualise and evaluate theory and practice within a management scope. Graduates will work towards independent study demonstrating an advanced level of knowledge, applying evidence and enquiry to a relevant management context","graduateProfile":"The aim of Level 8 is to extend and deepen an individual's management knowledge and skills and build on attainment in their endorsement area. The programme contains specific courses that will ensure students are provided with the tools and skills necessary.","educationPathway":"Graduates from the Postgraduate Diploma in Management with a B average may be admitted to the Master of Management.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3346"},"3350":{"i":"3350","entryRequirements":"Students must:\n\r\n* Be able to access a relevant workplace; and\n\r\n* Have a Bachelor degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a cognate subject; or\n\r\n* Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies (with or without endorsement) or in\n\r\ncognate subject for entry to the Postgraduate Diploma; or\n\r\n* A combination of academic and practical or professional experience based upon a record of\n\r\nlearning (academic transcript), parchment and a curriculum vitae detailing relevant\n\r\neducational achievements work experience and professional achievements as follows:\n\r\nEITHER\n\r\n* completion of a post-secondary school diploma in a related discipline at NZQA level 7 or\n\r\nequivalent from a recognised tertiary provider; and\n\r\n* demonstration of at least two years relevant practical experience with at least two written\n\r\nreferences (employer and character); or\n\r\n* demonstration of at least five years relevant practical or professional experience at a\n\r\nsenior level, evidence of ability to study at postgraduate qualification level and two written\n\r\nreferences (employer and character);\n\r\n* IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test\n\r\n65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching\n\r\nendorsements; or\n\r\n* IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test\n\r\n70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control\n\r\nendorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies will enable learners to critically\n\r\nexamine theories and models of continuing development through leadership. Students will have\n\r\nthe opportunity to exhibit advanced knowledge and expertise in professional leadership in the\n\r\ncontext of their specialist field which compliments their current experience and/or qualifications.\n\r\nThis qualification enables professionals in leadership roles to maintain currency and to critique\n\r\ntheir leadership practice.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies,\n\r\ngraduates will be able to:\n\r\n* Develop pedagogical content expertise within their field of study;\n\r\n* Critically evaluate their personal practice;\n\r\n* Critique challenges and issues within their specialist field and use to solve problems;\n\r\n* Operate within their communities of practice;\n\r\n* Advocate for self and others.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Professional Studies will be eligible for entry\n\r\nto the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Professional Studies programme or further Postgraduate\n\r\nstudy.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3350"},"3369":{"i":"3369","entryRequirements":"Brief Entry Requirements:\n\r\nOne of the below for admission:\n\r\n1. Bachelor Honours degree\n\r\n2. Postgraduate Diploma\n\r\n3. Undergraduate degree with experience\n\r\n4. Special circumstances - qualifying courses and experience\n\r\nAND English language competency where English is not a first language\n\r\nAll students:\n\r\nEnglish language competency where English is not a first language.\n\r\n* International applicants for whom English is not their first language will be required to show evidence of language competency, issued within the last two years. The level of competency required is:\n\r\no IELTS Academic score of 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, \n\r\no or an equivalent as outlined in NZQF-related rules (Rule 18).\n\r\n* For domestic applicants for whom English is not their first language, evidence of language competency may be required.\n\n\n\r\nPathway 1: Master of Management by Thesis programme (120cr)\n\r\n* Bachelor Honours Degree or Postgraduate Diploma in business or related field of study .\n\n\n\r\nPathway 2: Master of Management by Coursework programme (180cr)\n\r\n* An Undergraduate Degree with at least a New Zealand B average at Level 7; \n\r\nand at least one year practical or professional experience with at least two written references. \n\r\nOR\n\r\n* Bachelor Honours Degree with a New Zealand B average at Level 7.\n\r\nOR\n\r\n* A Postgraduate Diploma (120 credits at L8).\n\r\nOR \n\r\n* Special entry - Applicants who do not meet the academic requirements may be given special admission if they can provide evidence that they are capable of achieving the programme outcomes. \n\n\n\r\nPathway 3: Master of Management by Coursework and Thesis programme (240cr)\n\r\nAn Undergraduate Degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This qualification is designed for domestic and international students seeking an advanced scholarly research and practice-informed management qualification. It will complement existing postgraduate studies and further career aspirations through mastery within the fields of business, health, hospitality or information technology.\n\r\nThe highly advanced standard at which the graduate will operate, includes the ability to develop and apply new skills and techniques to existing or emerging issues, whilst articulating theory and practice within a management scope.\n\r\nGraduates will work independently at a highly specialised level of knowledge, and they will engage in rigorous critical intellectual analysis and be in a position to assume leadership in a relevant management context.\n\r\nThrough the attainment of advanced work-integrated practice and advanced sophisticated theoretical knowledge the graduates will contribute to high level management particularly (but not exclusively) in the areas of business, health, hospitality, or information technology.\n\r\nThe Kaitiakitanga framework which underpins this qualification reflects the holistic aspirations of Māori, while acknowledgement of Te Tiriti o Waitangi/Treaty of Waitangi ensures an inclusive environment for all learners.","graduateProfile":"Upon successful completion of the Master of Management graduates will have advanced knowledge, skills and attributes relevant to management (and their chosen endorsement) to be able to:\n\r\n1. Demonstrate mastery of sophisticated management theoretical subject matter; \n\r\n2. Understand key management functions as applied in practice;\n\r\n3. Apply in-depth knowledge and understanding of management literature to new and endorsement related situations;\n\r\n4. Engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, critique and problem-solving using evidence;\n\r\n5. Work independently and collaborate with others capitalising on different thinking, experience and skills;\n\r\n6. Apply advanced communication, research, professional, and interpersonal skills to enhance effectiveness and quality outcomes within their professional practice;\n\r\n7. Consider and respond to social, cultural, global, ethical and environmental responsibilities and issues; and\n\r\n8. Critically evaluate research methodologies and undertake advanced applied research projects.\n\n\n\r\nGraduates who successfully complete the 90 credit supervised thesis are also able to:\n\r\n9. Undertake qualitative and quantitative research and apply this knowledge in the context of a major independent work.","educationPathway":"Completion of the 90 credit course to be able to enroll for PhD study.","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3369"},"3474":{"i":"3474","entryRequirements":"1. A completed application form. 2. Original transcripts showing a degree or a Graduate Diploma in a related field from a recognized institution, including full transcripts and grade point average details, or equivalent. A scanned PDF will be sufficient to progress the application, but original documents will be required on arrival at ICL Business School. Failure to provide original documents will result in the cancellation of the enrolment. 3. For international students, IELTS with a minimum score of 6.5 overall (with no band score lower than 6.0), or any other equivalent approved by NZQA. 4. Credit transfer of up to four papers and RPL will be negotiated on a case-by-case basis.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aims of the Post Graduate Diploma in Business (Level 8) are: To take an interdisciplinary approach to study in the fields of international business studies within a single qualification, while retaining the core business disciplines of economics, marketing, project management, organizational behaviour, leadership, and accounting. This is a one-year, full-time programme of study designed for graduates of a first degree in a business-related subject. It is suited for those seeking to: a) bridge the gap between a first degree and a career in business, that requires further qualifications; and b) build a firm foundation for further study at postgraduate level in the business discipline.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this programme will have acquired an advanced-level knowledge of international business theory, assessment and management. Furthermore, students will develop the ability to prepare for and work towards running and managing a business and/or, undertake, mid-level management roles within a variety of industries. Graduates will be suitable in roles, which have prospects of a management career pathway (as identified by ANZSCO as Level 1 skilled employment roles). Graduates of the programme will have acquired the following specialist skills and knowledge: Critically analyze concepts of leadership, teamwork, marketing, finance, and accounting in relation to contemporary organizations Evaluate and apply entrepreneurial activities, quantitative analytical techniques, market research methods and project management processes within a global setting Generate a critical understanding of global economic and political activities Graduates of the programme will have acquired the following general skills: Intellectual rigour: a commitment to excellence in all scholarly and intellectual activities, including critical judgement Creativity: an ability to develop creative and effective responses to intellectual, professional and social challenges Ethical practice: a commitment to sustainability and high ethical standards in social and professional practices Knowledge of a discipline: command of a discipline to enable a smooth transition and contribution to professional and community settings Lifelong learning: the ability to be responsive to change, to be inquiring and reflective in practice, through information literacy and autonomous, self-managed learning Communication and social skills: the ability to communicate and collaborate with individuals, and within teams, in professional and community settings. Cultural competences: an ability to engage with diverse cultural and bi-cultural perspectives in both global and local settings and in the context of the Treaty of Waitangi.","educationPathway":"Graduates will be able to path way into master's programmes.,","developedBy":"ICL Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3474"},"3538":{"i":"3538","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Te Tohu Tītohu mō Te Aka Whakaaroaro/PGDipPP is one of the following*:\n\r\n·\tan NZQF-listed undergraduate degree or graduate diploma (or equivalent) in a socio-cultural field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- (B Minus) average across the final year of study as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system;\n\r\nor\n\r\n·\ta degree or equivalent professional qualification in a different field if the applicant can supply evidence of work experience at degree level or above within a socio-cultural field, subject to an interview and/or the submission of a portfolio of evidence to establish the status and relevance of the applicant's prior learning and experience;\n\r\nor\n\r\n·\tat the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above.\n\r\n* Applicants who does not meet the entry requirements may be provisionally accepted; such students will be expected to pass their first course in the programme in order to progress.\n\r\n4.2.4\tThe academic entry requirement for the Te Tohu Paerua mō Te Aka Whakaaroaro/MPP is one of the following*:\n\r\n·\tan NZQF-listed undergraduate degree or graduate diploma (or equivalent) in a socio-cultural field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- (B Minus) average across the final year of study as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system;\n\r\nor\n\r\n·\tan NZQF-listed postgraduate qualification (Level 8) (or equivalent) in a socio-cultural field with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- (B Minus) average across the final year of study as per the EIT-specified 11-point achievement-based grading system;\n\r\nor\n\r\n·\tcompletion of the Te Tohu Tītohu mō Te Aka Whakaaroaro/PGDipPP with a minimum B- (B Minus) average;\n\r\nor\n\r\n·\ta degree or equivalent professional qualification in a different field if the applicant can supply evidence of work experience at degree level or above within a socio-cultural field, subject to an interview and/or the submission of a portfolio of evidence to establish the status and relevance of the applicant's prior learning and experience;\n\r\nor\n\r\n·\tat the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above.\n\r\n* Applicants who do not meet the entry requirements may be provisionally accepted; such students will be expected to pass their first two courses with a minimum B minus average in order to progress.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The MPP has been designed to enable students to demonstrate a critical awareness of personal and professional self in relation to new and emerging challenges in their professional field; demonstrate rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving; apply advanced knowledge and skills to new o emerging challenges in their practice.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate a critical awareness of personal and professional self in relation to new and emerging challenges in their professional field; demonstrate rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving; research, analyse and argue from evidence; demonstrate excellent communication skills as a change agent in relation to professional practice; work independently and collaboratively with relevant communities to apply specialised knowledge to new or emerging situations in practice.","educationPathway":"PhD study","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3538"},"3539":{"i":"3539","entryRequirements":"Students must: * Be able to access a relevant workplace; and * Have a Bachelor degree or \n\r\nGraduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a cognate subject; or * Postgraduate Certificate\n\r\nin Applied Professional Studies (with or without endorsement) or in cognate subject for entry \n\r\nto the Postgraduate Diploma; or * A combination of academic and practical or professional \n\r\nexperience based upon a record of learning (academic transcript), parchment and a \n\r\ncurriculum vitae detailing relevant educational achievements work experience and \n\r\nprofessional achievements as follows: EITHER * completion of a post-secondary school \n\r\ndiploma in a related discipline at NZQA level 7 or equivalent from a recognised tertiary \n\r\nprovider; and * demonstration of at least two years relevant practical experience with at \n\r\nleast two written references (employer and character); or * demonstration of at least five \n\r\nyears relevant practical or professional experience at a senior level, evidence of ability to \n\r\nstudy at postgraduate qualification level and two written references (employer and character)\n\r\n; * IELTS Academic 6.5 with no band score lower than 6.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English \n\r\nTest 65 with no score lower than 60 for Mentoring and Leadership and Adult Teaching endorsements; or * IELTS Academic 7.0 with no band score lower than 7.0, or equivalent or Waiariki English Test 70 with no score lower than 70 for Vulnerable Peoples, and Infection Prevention and Control endorsements.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of this qualification is to provide an opportunity for students to acquire knowledge and expertise in mentoring \n\r\nand professional leadership in the context of their specialist field which complements their current experience and/or \n\r\nqualifications. This qualification enables professionals in leadership roles to maintain currency and develop their discipline by ongoing professional development.","graduateProfile":"After successful completion of this qualification, students will have the skills and knowledge to be able to: \n\r\n -build on their current underpinning knowledge and skills to further develop their professional practice \n\r\n -demonstrate knowledge of leadership in relation to their field of practice. \n\r\n -develop professional mentoring skills \n\r\n -demonstrate knowledge about theory and practice of professional supervision and mentoring \n\r\n -Solve real world problems in the field of professional leadership and mentoring \n\r\n -analyse relevant legislation that impacts on professional leadership and practice \n\r\n -critically examine the principles of implementing culturally appropriate professional practice \n\r\n -produce, analyse and synthesise empirical data which will contribute to well-informed decision-making \n\r\n -explore best practice through the process of critical thinking and reflection","educationPathway":"Students may move onto further learning in fields relevant to their profession e.g. Masters in Nursing, Masters in \n\r\nEducation, Masters in Social Work","developedBy":"Toi Ohomai Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3539"},"3540":{"i":"3540","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are 1 a Bachelor's degree (or equivalent qualification) in a related discipline with a grade average at level 7/8 of B- or higher, or 2 a combination of academic qualifications and relevant skills and knowledge acquired through work or professional experience that is deemed equivalent to 1 above. 3 International applicants must demonstrate that they have equivalent academic qualifications and experience, and those for whom English is not their first language must provide evidence of English language competence of IELTS academic overall band score of 6.5 with no individual band less than 6.0, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Management will be able to confidently engage with research and its application to a range of disciplines within the applied management context. These graduates are critical thinkers, effective problem solvers, future-focused and apply specialised management and leadership knowledge and capabilities to new situations with the field of business management or business information systems.  This qualification prepares students for further postgraduate study or to advance their careers or enhance their own organisation.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to: \n\r\n* Research, analyse and argue using empirical evidence \n\r\n* Think independently and critically enabling future-focused decision-making in real world situations \n\r\n* Engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and applied problem-solving \n\r\n* Work effectively in multicultural teams and exercise leadership in the workplace \n\r\n* Critically apply specialised management knowledge and capabilities to new situations \n\r\n* Critically assess the impact of organisational practices on society and address related ethical and sustainability issues  \n\r\n* Critically analyse current practitioner literature and applied and conceptual research findings  \n\r\n* Design and complete a piece of applied research to internationally recognised standards \n\r\n* Communicate applied research outcomes effectively \n\r\n* Actively engage in leadership activities in applied management contexts \n\r\n* Critically assess own professional learning and capabilities against Aotearoa New Zealand workplace context.  \n\n\n\r\nThose graduates who complete the 120 credit Research Thesis component will also be able to: \n\r\n* Demonstrate a high order of skill in the planning, execution and completion of a piece of original research or creative scholarly work \n\r\n* Synthesise knowledge and apply this learning to new organisational decision-making situations.  \n\n\n\r\nThose graduates who complete the Business Management major will also be able to: \n\n\n\r\n* Explore, critically evaluate and develop an in-depth appreciation of key business management and leadership roles within effective organisational contexts  \n\r\n* Manage and lead organisational projects, taking into consideration their responsibilities and decision-making from a variety of perspectives, to meet the requirements of an applied business management role.  \n\r\n* Critically evaluate evidence-based business management practices which contribute to the importance of strategic thinking in leadership decision-making \n\n\n\r\nThose graduates who complete the Business Information Systems major will also be able to: \n\n\n\r\n* Explore, critically evaluate and develop an in-depth appreciation of key business information systems management and leadership roles within effective organisational contexts \n\r\n* Manage and lead business information systems projects, taking into consideration their responsibilities and decision-making from a variety of perspectives, to meet the requirements of effective organisations. \n\r\n* Critically evaluate evidence-based business information systems which contribute to the leadership and effective strategic direction and operation of organisations.","educationPathway":"Following successful completion of a bachelors degree, postgraduate certificate and diploma in Applied Management students will then complete the Master of Applied Management.","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3540"},"3541":{"i":"3541","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are   \n\r\n1 a Bachelor's degree (or equivalent qualification) in a related discipline, or   \n\r\n2 a combination of academic qualifications and relevant skills and knowledge acquired through work or professional experience that is deemed equivalent to 1 above.   \n\r\n3 International applicants must demonstrate that they have equivalent academic qualifications and experience, and those for whom English is not their first language, must provide evidence of English language competence of IELTS academic overall band score of 6.5 with no individual band less than 6.0, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management will extend and deepen their knowledge and understanding of research and enquiry methods, current capabilities and issues over a wider range of disciplines within an applied management context. Through experiential learning strategies and reflective practice, students will apply management practices in the field of business management or business information systems. This qualification prepares students for further postgraduate study or to obtain employment, advance their careers or develop their own organisation.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to: \n\r\n-Critically analyse and argue using empirical evidence \n\r\n-Think independently and critically enabling future-focused decision-making in real world situations. \n\r\n-Engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and applied problem-solving. \n\r\nWork effectively in multicultural teams and exercise leadership in the workplace \n\r\n-Critically apply management knowledge and capabilities to new situations \n\r\n-Assess the impact of organisational practices on society and address related ethical and sustainability issues \n\r\n-Critically analyse current practitioner literature and applied and conceptual research findings \n\r\n-Critically evaluate a range of research and enquiry methodologies and undertake applied professional projects \n\r\n-Participate in leadership activities in applied management contexts. \n\r\n-Apply their professional learning and capabilities to be able to live and work in Aotearoa New Zealand. \n\r\nThose graduates who complete the Business Management major will also be able to: \n\r\n-Explore, critically evaluate and develop an in-depth knowledge of key business management and leadership roles within effective organisational contexts \n\r\n-Manage organisational projects, taking into consideration their responsibilities and decision-making from a variety of perspectives, to meet the requirements of an applied business management role. \n\r\nThose graduates who complete the Business Information Systems major will also be able to: \n\r\n-Explore, critically evaluate and develop an in-depth appreciate of key business information systems management and leadership roles within effective organisational contexts \n\r\n-Manage business information systems projects, taking into consideration their responsibilities and decision-making from a variety of perspectives, to meet the requirements of effective organisations.","educationPathway":"Further postgraduate study including the Master of Applied Management","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3541"},"3542":{"i":"3542","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are  \n\r\n1) a Bachelor's degree (or equivalent qualification) in a related discipline, or  \n\r\n2) a combination of academic qualifications and relevant skills and knowledge acquired through work or professional experience that is deemed equivalent to 1 above.  \n\r\n3) International applicants must demonstrate that they have equivalent academic qualifications and experience, and those for whom English is not their first language, must provide evidence of English language competence of IELTS academic overall band score of 6.5 with no individual band less than 6.0, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management will extend and deepen their knowledge and understanding of current management capabilities and issues in a range of applied settings through experiential learning strategies and reflective practice. This qualification prepares students for further postgraduate study, or acquiring additional skills and knowledge for employment in a management-related role.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to: -Critically analyse and argue using empirical evidence -Think independently and critically enabling future-focused decision-making in real world situations -Engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and applied problem-solving -Work effectively in multicultural teams and exercise leadership in the workplace -Critically apply management knowledge and capabilities to new situations -Assess the impact of organisational practices on society and address related ethical and sustainability issues. -Apply their professional learning and capabilities to be able to live and work in Aotearoa New Zealand..","educationPathway":"Following Bachelors degree, Postgraduate Cert in Applied Management leading to Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Management and onto the Master of Applied Management","developedBy":"Otago Polytechnic","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3542"},"3691":{"i":"3691","entryRequirements":"Academic: Applicants must have a Bachelor's degree or a Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a similar subject, OR relevant skills and knowledge acquired through appropriate work or professional experience.\n\r\nAlternative: Applicants who are unable to evidence that they meet Academic Entry Requirements, but who can demonstrate acquired skills for tertiary study gained through study, work and/or life experience, may be approved for alternative entry. This may include Recognition of Prior Learning. \n\r\nEnglish language: If English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency Outcomes Table: IELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.0 in each band). Note: Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact NMIT for an assessment. Note: Applicants who have achieved NCEA Level 3 University Entrance requirements are not required to provide evidence of English language skills.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The logistics and supply chain industry is massive and global. It is an innovative area of business with constantly emerging business processes changes, disruptive technologies, enterprise software, tracking-and-reporting technologies, and business models. The area is fiercely competitive both at the global scale and at the local domestic scale. Companies that can effectively manage procurement, just-in-time delivery, and relationships with third-party suppliers will be able to control their own costs, score win-win solutions with partners, ensure business continuity, and ultimately develop a core competency that underpins competitive advantage and better prices and service for customers. For these reasons, trained and skilled logistics and supply chain managers are in demand in New Zealand, in our major export markets (e.g., India, north Asia, south east Asia), and globally.   \n\r\nThe Programme is designed for people with an educational background in business, management, and/or commerce or with high levels of knowledge in a specialist industry, who may wish to enter the area of logistics and supply chain management. Logistics and supply chain professionals may also wish to receive an academic qualification that recognises their experience and supports their career progression into management or advisory positions.   \n\r\nThe Programme is also designed for people working with businesses that utilise logistics and supply chain processes, and who seek to gain advanced skills and knowledge to apply to their business environment, whether it be domestic or international.   \n\r\nThe purpose of this Programme is to produce graduates who will be well equipped to carry out these roles and aims to produce graduates who will be able to manage complex tasks and strategic challenges in the contemporary, and evolving, logistics and supply chain industry. They will be able to critically evaluate data, qualitative information, and industry trends in order to assess supply chain vulnerabilities and risks, opportunities to reduce cost and improve performance, and to identify, implement, and manage tactics that are innovative and value-adding for their enterprise.   \n\r\nGraduates will be prepared for independent research or to progress to Level 9 study should they elect to move on to study at a higher level.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this qualification will be able to:   \n\r\nAdvanced specialised knowledge and its application   \n\r\nIdentify, implement, and manage innovative and effective strategies for planning logistics and supply chains in national and international business contexts   \n\r\nPlan and carry out effective applied research related to logistics and supply chain management   \n\r\nApplied Business skills   \n\r\nAchieve the right balance of people, systems, contractual arrangements and technologies to control costs and optimise product and service quality   \n\r\nNavigate effectively in a global and multicultural business environment   \n\r\nAnalysis and critical evaluation skills   \n\r\nInterpret, analyse and critically evaluate complex and diverse data and information as it relates to logistics and supply chain management   \n\r\nStrategy/problem solving skills   \n\r\nCritically evaluate strategic opportunities for an enterprise to control costs and improve product and service quality through effective planning of logistics and supply chains   \n\r\nIdentify problems in logistics and supply chain management, propose potential solutions, and mitigate risk   \n\r\nUse specialist knowledge and critical evaluative skills to anticipate future trends in procurement and logistics, assess the strategic implications for an enterprise, adapt, and innovate to optimise an enterprise's market position","educationPathway":"Graduates will have the skills and knowledge to progress to higher level Postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Nelson Marlborough Institute of Technology (NMIT)","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3691"},"3749":{"i":"3749","entryRequirements":"1. A completed application form.  \n\r\n2. Original transcripts showing a Bachelor degree or a Graduate Diploma in a business-related or IT/computing subject from a recognized institution, including full transcripts;  \n\r\nOR  \n\r\nEvidence of acquiring the relevant skills and knowledge through appropriate work or professional experience in business studies or IT/computing related area.  \n\r\nA scanned PDF will be sufficient to progress the application, but original documents will be required on arrival at ICL Graduate Business School. Failure to provide original documents will result in the cancellation of the enrolment.  \n\r\n3. For international students, Academic IELTS with a minimum score of 6.5 overall (with no band score lower than 6.0 and gained within the past two years in one examination), or any other equivalent approved by NZQA.  \n\r\n4. Credit transfer or RPL of up to four papers will be negotiated on a case-by-case basis.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Master of Business Informatics is to take an interdisciplinary approach in informatics and business innovation within a single qualification, including the core disciplines of enterprise innovation, IT service management, information security management, digital transformation, project management and business professionalism. This programme brings together business and IT services in both a New Zealand and global context. This is a 16-month, full-time programme of study designed for graduates with a Bachelor degree, postgraduate or graduate diploma or equivalent in a business-related or IT/computing subject from a recognised institution. It is suited for those seeking to: a) bridge the gap between a first degree and a career in business informatics that requires further qualifications and skills; b) build a firm foundation for further advanced level study towards a doctoral qualification in a similar discipline.","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the Master of Business Informatics is able to: * show evidence of advanced knowledge of business informatics * demonstrate mastery of the theory of business informatics * evaluate critically the findings and discussions in the literature on business informatics * research, analyse and argue from evidence * work independently and apply knowledge to new situations in a business informatics context * engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving","educationPathway":"Doctoral programmes in a related discipline.","developedBy":"ICL Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3749"},"3784":{"i":"3784","entryRequirements":"Academic:  Applicants must have a Bachelor's degree OR relevant skills and knowledge acquired through appropriate work or professional experience. \n\r\nAlternative: Applicants who are unable to evidence that they meet Academic entry requirements, but who can demonstrate acquired skills for postgraduate tertiary study gained through study, work and/or life experience, may be approved for alternative entry by the Curriculum Manager (or delegate) \n\r\nEnglish language: If English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency Outcomes Table: IELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.0 in each band). Note: Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact NMIT for an assessment. IELTS scores used must be taken from a single IELTS Test Report Form and are valid for two years from the date of the test. \n\r\nInterview: Applicants may be interviewed to assess their suitability for the programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The overall strategic purpose of this qualification is to advance management expertise, widen employment opportunities and improve effectiveness in management roles.    \n\r\nThe qualification is unique in that it provides advanced qualifications in applied management, with industry electives or pathways which have been developed to match key labour market needs and characteristics of the Nelson and Marlborough region in particular.    \n\r\nThis combination of practical and applied study, as well as advanced theory and work-based learning is strongly aligned with NMIT's role in providing work-ready graduates and its objective to develop and retain skilled applied management professionals in the regions served by NMIT.    \n\r\nThis qualification is designed to be directly relevant not just to larger private and public organisations, but also to the self-employed, and the smaller organisations and businesses which employ the majority of people in the Nelson and Marlborough regions.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this qualification will be able to:   \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of management issues and design solutions for a contemporary environment or a range of environments.   \n\r\n* Employ innovative management approaches and leadership in complex contexts.   \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of management to problem solving in chosen field of enquiry or professional practice including Logistics and Supply Chain Management, International Business, Aquaculture Management, Healthcare Management or Business Analytics.    \n\r\n* Engage in rigorous analysis and critical thinking about complex management issues in chosen field of enquiry or professional practice.   \n\r\n* Design and complete independent research in management, applying knowledge to new situations in a chosen field of enquiry or professional practice including Logistics and Supply Chain Management, International Business, Aquaculture Management, Healthcare Management, or Business Analytics.","educationPathway":"Graduates will have the skills and knowledge to progress to higher level Doctoral study.","developedBy":"Nelson Marlborough Institute of Technology (NMIT)","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3784"},"3785":{"i":"3785","entryRequirements":"Academic Requirements: \n\r\nA Bachelor's degree \n\r\nOR \n\r\nRelevant skills and knowledge acquired through appropriate work or professional experience. \n\n\n\r\nAlternative Requirements: \n\r\nApplicants who are unable to evidence that they meet Academic entry requirements, but who can demonstrate acquired skills for postgraduate tertiary study gained through study, work and/or life experience, may be approved for alternative entry by the Curriculum Manager (or delegate) \n\n\n\r\nEnglish language Requirements: \n\r\nIf English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency outcomes Table: \n\r\nIELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.0 in each band), \n\r\nNote: Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact NMIT for an assessment \n\r\nIELTS scores used must be taken from a single IELTS Test Report Form and are valid for two years from the date of the test.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The overall strategic purpose of this programme is to advance management expertise, widen employment opportunities and improve effectiveness in management roles.   \n\r\nThe programme is unique in that it provides advanced qualifications in applied management, with industry electives or pathways which have been developed to match key labour market needs and characteristics of the Nelson and Marlborough region in particular.   \n\r\nThis combination of practical and applied study, as well as advanced theory and work-based learning is strongly aligned with NMIT's role in providing work-ready graduates and its objective to develop and retain skilled applied management professionals in the regions served by NMIT.   \n\r\nThis programme is designed to be directly relevant not just to larger private and public organisations, but also to the self-employed, and the smaller organisations and businesses which employ the majority of people in the Nelson and Marlborough regions.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this qualification will be able to:  \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of management issues and design solutions for a contemporary environment or a range of environments.  \n\r\n* Employ innovative management approaches and leadership in complex contexts.  \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of management to problem solving in chosen field of enquiry or professional practice including Logistics and Supply Chain management, International Business, Aquaculture Management, Healthcare Management or Business Analytics.  \n\r\n* Engage in rigorous analysis and critical thinking about complex management issues in chosen field of enquiry or professional practice including Logistics and Supply Chain Management, International Business, Aquaculture Management, Healthcare Management or Business Analytics.","educationPathway":"Graduates will have the skills and knowledge to progress to higher level postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Nelson Marlborough Institute of Technology (NMIT)","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3785"},"3786":{"i":"3786","entryRequirements":"Academic: Applicants must have a Bachelor's degree or a Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in a similar subject, OR relevant skills and knowledge acquired through appropriate work or professional experience.\n\r\nAlternative: Applicants who are unable to evidence that they meet Academic Entry Requirements, but who can demonstrate acquired skills for tertiary study gained through study, work and/or life experience, may be approved for alternative entry. This may include Recognition of Prior Learning. \n\r\nEnglish language: If English is not the applicant's first language, applicants will need to provide a result from a test or qualification on the acceptable alternatives English Proficiency Outcomes Table: IELTS 6.5 Academic (no lower than 6.0 in each band). Note: Applicants who do not have evidence of English language skills and are a New Zealand citizen or permanent resident, may contact NMIT for an assessment.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The overall strategic purpose of this programme is to advance management expertise, widen employment opportunities and improve effectiveness in management roles.  \n\r\nThe programme is unique in that it provides advanced qualifications in applied management, with industry electives or pathways which have been developed to match key labour market needs and characteristics of the Nelson and Marlborough region in particular.  \n\r\nThis combination of practical and applied study, as well as advanced theory and work-based learning is strongly aligned with NMIT's role in providing work-ready graduates and its objective to develop and retain skilled applied management professionals in the regions served by NMIT.  \n\r\nThis programme is designed to be directly relevant not just to larger private and public organisations, but also to the self-employed, and the smaller organisations and businesses which employ the majority of people in the Nelson and Marlborough regions.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this qualification will be able to:  \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of management issues and design solutions for a contemporary environment or a range of environments.  \n\r\n* Employ innovative management approaches and leadership in complex contexts.","educationPathway":"Graduates will have the skills and knowledge to progress to higher level postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Nelson Marlborough Institute of Technology (NMIT)","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3786"},"3808":{"i":"3808","entryRequirements":"1. A completed application form.  \n\r\n2. Original transcripts showing a Bachelor degree or a Graduate Diploma in a business-related or IT/computing subject from a recognised institution, including full transcripts;   \n\r\nOR  \n\r\nEvidence of acquiring the relevant skills and knowledge through appropriate work or professional experience in business studies or IT/computing related area.  \n\n\n\r\nA scanned PDF will be sufficient to progress the application, but original documents will be required on arrival at ICL Graduate Business School. Failure to provide original documents will result in the cancellation of the enrolment.  \n\r\n3. For international students, Academic IELTS with a minimum score of 6.5 overall (with no band score lower than 6.0 and gained within the past two years in one examination), or any other equivalent approved by NZQA.  \n\r\n4. Credit transfer or RPL of up to four papers will be negotiated on a case-by-case basis.  \n\r\n5. ICL Graduate Business School also strongly recommends that a Personal Statement, written by the applicant, is attached to the application explaining why they believe they should study on the programme, their motivations and further aspirations.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of the Postgraduate Diploma of Business Informatics is to take an interdisciplinary approach in informatics and business innovation within a single qualification, including the core disciplines of enterprise innovation, IT service management, information security management, digital transformation, project management and business professionalism. This programme brings together business and IT services in both a New Zealand and global context.   \n\n\n\r\nThis is a 12-month, full-time programme of study designed for graduates with a Bachelor degree, postgraduate or graduate diploma or equivalent in a business-related or IT/computing subject from a recognised institution. It is suited for those seeking to:   \n\r\na) bridge the gap between a first degree and a career in business informatics that requires further qualifications and skills;   \n\r\nb) build a firm foundation for further advanced level study towards a Master's qualification in a similar discipline.","graduateProfile":"A graduate of the Postgraduate Diploma in Business Informatics is able to:  \n\r\n- Show evidence of advanced knowledge of business informatics  \n\r\n- Engage in rigourous intellectual analysis, criticism and problem-solving in the context of business informatics.","educationPathway":"This programme may provide pathways for further academic study at an advanced level leading to a Master's degree. Graduates from this programme may be required to pursue additional study and/or research for provisional or direct entry onto a university Master's/doctoral programme.","developedBy":"ICL Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=3808"},"4116":{"i":"4116","entryRequirements":"19.1.1\tThe academic entry requirement for the Master of Logistics Supply Chain Management (240) is one of the following:\n\r\n*\tan NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent);\n\r\n*\tat the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above.\n\n\n\r\nAll applicants must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in their programme. For international students, ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include the following: \n\r\n* successful study of a programme in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply) \n\r\n* completion of a New Zealand Certificate in English Language (Level 5 with any endorsement) \n\n\n\r\n* IELTS Academic score of 6.5, with no band score lower than 6, achieved in a single test within the two years preceding enrolment \n\r\n* completion of accepted international English language proficiency tests (refer to NZQA English language entry requirements for international students) with scores equivalent to the IELTS scores above. \n\r\nAn international student must be in possession of an appropriate visa for the duration of their programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Logistics and Supply Chain Management (240) is a Level 9 programme of 240 credits at levels 8 and 9 with at least 45 credits at level 9, completed by coursework, or a combination of coursework and either a project or research. It enables students who have completed a bachelor degree in an unrelated field to achieve a master's level qualification in the logistics and supply chain management area.","graduateProfile":"* Apply advanced knowledge of broad conceptual and theoretical elements to improve functional areas of logistics and supply chain management   \n\r\n* Evaluate the impact of social, ethical, cultural and sustainability dimensions in logistics and supply chain contexts   \n\r\n* Lead and execute transformation strategies and decision making processes to solve complex logistics and supply chain problems   \n\r\n* Synthesise information from a range of contemporary sources to inform effective, efficient recommendations to improve business outcomes   \n\r\n* Pursue lifelong learning based on values and attitudes consistent with being responsible citizens and members of professional communities   \n\r\n*Think critically and conduct investigative applied research in a wide range of logistics and supply chain contexts","educationPathway":"Further study in the field of logistics and supply chain management.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4116"},"4117":{"i":"4117","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Master of Logistics and Supply Chain Management (180) is one of the following: * an NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) with a minimum of the equivalent to a B- average (as per the EIT 11 point grading system); or * a Bachelor Honours or Postgraduate qualification in Logistics and Supply Chain field with 120 credits at Level 8; or * at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. [A Master of Logistics and Supply Chain applicant who does not meet the entry criteria above may be admitted to the Postgraduate Certificate in Logistics and Supply Chain Management and, upon successful completion of four courses (with a minimum B average) from the schedule of courses may be admitted to the Master of Logistics and Supply Chain Management.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Logistics and Supply Chain Management (180) is a Level 9 programme of 180 credits at levels 8 and 9 with at least 45 credits at level 9, completed by coursework, or a combination of coursework and either a project or research. It enables students who have completed a bachelor degree in business, or a related discipline, to achieve a master's level qualification in the logistics and supply chain management area.","graduateProfile":"The graduate will: * Apply advanced knowledge of broad conceptual and theoretical elements to improve functional areas of logistics and supply chain management * Evaluate the impact of social, ethical, cultural and sustainability dimensions in logistics and supply chain contexts * Lead and execute transformation strategies and decision making processes to solve complex logistics and supply chain problems * Synthesise information from a range of contemporary sources to inform effective, efficient recommendations to improve business outcomes * Pursue lifelong learning based on values and attitudes consistent with being responsible citizens and members of professional communities * Think critically and conduct investigative applied research in a wide range of logistics and supply chain contexts","educationPathway":"Further studies in the fields of logistics and supply chain management.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4117"},"4119":{"i":"4119","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Postgraduate Certificate and Postgraduate Diploma in Logistics and Supply Chain Management is one of the following: * an NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) in Logistics or Supply Chain field; or * an undergraduate degree in a related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a -B average (as per the EIT 11 point grading system), subject to assessment by the programme coordinator; or * Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. All applicants must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in their programme. For international students, ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include the following: * successful study of a programme in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply) * completion of a New Zealand Certificate in English Language (Level 5 with any endorsement) * IELTS Academic score of 6.5, with no band score lower than 6, achieved in a single test within the two years preceding enrolment * completion of accepted international English language proficiency tests (refer to NZQA English language entry requirements for international students) with scores equivalent to the IELTS scores above.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Logistics and Supply Chain Management is a Level 8 programme of 60 credits, which enables students who have completed a bachelor degree in business, or a related discipline, to achieve a postgraduate level qualification in the logistics and supply chain management area.","graduateProfile":"The graduate will:   \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of broad conceptual and theoretical elements to support functional areas of logistics and supply chain management   \n\r\n* Evaluate the impact of social, ethical, cultural and sustainability dimensions in logistics and supply chain contexts   \n\r\n* Contribute to the execution of transformation strategies and decision making processes to solve complex logistics and supply chain problems   \n\r\n* Synthesise information from a range of contemporary sources to inform effective, efficient recommendations to improve business outcomes   \n\r\n* Possess values and attitudes consistent with being responsible citizens and membersThe graduate will:","educationPathway":"Further studies in the fields of logistics and supply chain management.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4119"},"4121":{"i":"4121","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Master of Applied Management (240) is one of the following: * an NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) with a minimum of a pass (as per the EIT 11 point grading system specified in the ARF); * at the Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. All applicants must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in their programme. For international students, ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include the following: * successful study of a programme in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply) * completion of a New Zealand Certificate in English Language (Level 5 with any endorsement) * IELTS Academic score of 6.5, with no band score lower than 6, achieved in a single test within the two years preceding enrolment * completion of accepted international English language proficiency tests (refer to NZQA English language entry requirements for international students) with scores equivalent to the IELTS scores above. An international student must be in possession of an appropriate visa for the duration of their programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The degree may be taken by coursework, thesis and coursework or thesis. The Master of Applied Management (240) is designed to develop advanced knowledge and skills in the applied management field for students entering the degree from successful study in other disciplines. A student undertaking the Master of Applied Management (240) is required to complete courses across a range of areas of professional competencies as approved by the Programme Coordinator. This requirement ensures that graduates in the Master of Applied Management (240) gain breadth and depth of professional competence in their postgraduate studies consistent with the philosophy of the programmes. Selection of courses will take into account previous experience, individual level of competency, together with the attainment of all graduate attributes.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Management will: * show evidence of advanced knowledge and mastery of sophisticated theoretical subject matter in the areas of professional competence * demonstrate evidence of leadership skills in a business context Graduates will be able to demonstrate the following professional attributes in a business context: Critical thinking and problem solving * apply independent rigorous intellectual analysis to management decisions * critically and effectively diagnose existing and emerging business problems in order to produce optimal solutions Planning and change management skills * work both independently and co-operatively to make, and implement, strategic and operational business plans * apply advanced knowledge to new situations and generate new solutions * adapt to emerging paradigms within the profession Research and informational skills * critically evaluate findings and discussions in applied management literature * apply business and/or management research in industry * research, analyse, and argue from evidence Communication skills * effectively communicate business decisions and information both written and orally * communicate across cultures within a business context.","educationPathway":"Further study in management.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4121"},"4123":{"i":"4123","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Postgraduate Certificate and Postgraduate Diploma in Logistics and Supply Chain Management is one of the following: * an NZQCF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent) in Logistics or Supply Chain field; or * an undergraduate degree in a related field with a minimum of the equivalent to a -B average (as per the EIT 11 point grading system), subject to assessment by the programme coordinator; or * Dean's discretion, where an applicant's situation is compelling but not covered by the requirements listed above. All applicants must demonstrate an acceptable level of English language fluency prior to acceptance in their programme. For international students, ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include the following: * successful study of a programme in which English was the language of instruction (conditions apply) * completion of a New Zealand Certificate in English Language (Level 5 with any endorsement) * IELTS Academic score of 6.5, with no band score lower than 6, achieved in a single test within the two years preceding enrolment * completion of accepted international English language proficiency tests (refer to NZQA English language entry requirements for international students) with scores equivalent to the IELTS scores above.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Logistics and Supply Chain Management is a Level 8 programme of 60 credits, which enables students who have completed a bachelor degree in business, or a related discipline, to achieve a postgraduate level qualification in the logistics and supply chain management area.","graduateProfile":"The graduate will:   \n\r\n* Apply advanced knowledge of broad conceptual and theoretical elements to support functional areas of logistics and supply chain management   \n\r\n* Evaluate the impact of social, ethical, cultural and sustainability dimensions in logistics and supply chain contexts   \n\r\n* Contribute to the execution of transformation strategies and decision making processes to solve complex logistics and supply chain problems   \n\r\n* Synthesise information from a range of contemporary sources to inform effective, efficient recommendations to improve business outcomes   \n\r\n* Possess values and attitudes consistent with being responsible citizens and membersThe graduate will:","educationPathway":"Further studies in the fields of logistics and supply chain management.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4123"},"4208":{"i":"4208","entryRequirements":"Applicants must have a recognised Bachelor's degree (or higher) in a relevant discipline with merit achievement deemed to be a grade \n\r\naverage of B- or higher OR a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to merit achievement in a bachelor degree or equivalent. Applicants must also meet the English Language Admission Requirements.\n\n\n\r\nEntry requirements:\n\r\nGeneral Admission Requirements: Applicants must meet the following requirements:\n\r\na. a recognised Bachelor's degree (or higher) in a relevant discipline with merit achievement deemed to be a grade average of B- or higher; or \n\r\nb. a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to merit achievement in a bachelor degree or equivalent.\n\n\n\r\nEnglish Language Admission Requirements: \n\r\nDomestic applicants must have achieved the minimum requirement to go to a New Zealand University or equivalent. International applicants must also meet the English Language Entry Requirements as stated by the New Zealand \n\r\nQualifications Authority | Mana Tohu Matauranga O Aotearoa.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Business will extend and deepen learner's knowledge and capabilities of a specialised area of study in applied business contexts. This qualification prepares learners for further postgraduate study, or acquiring additional skills and knowledge for employment in a specialist role. The qualification will develop capable and responsible business professionals for careers in Aotearoa / New Zealand's economy.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Applied Business postgraduate qualifications will have the knowledge, skills and capabilities to make highly effective contributions to business practice in their specialisations in both domestic and international organisation contexts.   \n\r\nA graduate of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Business will be able to:   \n\r\n1. Apply specialised knowledge of business theory and practice to enhance organisational outcomes.   \n\r\n2. Critically evaluate business challenges and opportunities to inform decision making.   \n\r\n3. Engage collaboratively with diverse teams and cultures in Aotearoa New Zealand and global contexts.   \n\r\n4. Communicate effectively and professionally with a range of stakeholders.   \n\r\n5. Critically engage with ethically and socially responsible business practices.","educationPathway":"Graduates from the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Business will be able to pathway into further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Manukau Institute of Technology and Unitec - Unitec","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4208"},"4209":{"i":"4209","entryRequirements":"Applicants must have a recognised Bachelor's degree (or higher) in a relevant discipline with merit achievement deemed to be a grade average of B- or higher OR a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to merit achievement in a bachelor degree or equivalent. Applicants must also meet the English \n\r\nLanguage Admission Requirements.\n\n\n\r\nEntry requirements:\n\r\nGeneral Admission Requirements: Applicants must meet the following requirements:\n\r\na. a recognised Bachelor's degree (or higher) in a relevant discipline with merit achievement deemed to be a grade \n\r\naverage of B- or higher; or \n\r\nb. a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to merit achievement in a \n\r\nbachelor degree or equivalent.\n\n\n\r\nEnglish Language Admission Requirements: \n\r\nDomestic applicants must have achieved the minimum requirement to go to a New Zealand University or equivalent. International applicants must also meet the English Language Entry Requirements as stated by the New Zealand Qualifications Authority | Mana Tohu Matauranga O Aotearoa.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Business will extend and deepen learners' knowledge and capabilities in a specialised area of study through research and enquiry methods in an applied business context. Graduates will be able to apply advanced practices in the field of their chosen specialisation. This qualification prepares learners for further postgraduate study or to obtain employment, advance their careers or develop within their own organisation. The qualification will develop capable and responsible business professionals for careers in local and international economies.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Applied Business postgraduate qualifications will have the knowledge, skills and capabilities to make highly effective contributions to business practice in their specialisations in both domestic and international organisation contexts.   \n\r\nA graduate of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Business will be able to:   \n\r\n1. Apply advanced knowledge of business theory and practice to enhance organisational outcomes.   \n\r\n2. Critically evaluate business challenges and opportunities to inform decision making.   \n\r\n3. Engage collaboratively with diverse teams and cultures in Aotearoa New Zealand and global contexts.   \n\r\n4. Communicate effectively and professionally with a range of stakeholders.   \n\r\n5. Critically engage with ethically and socially responsible business practices.","educationPathway":"Graduates from the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Business will be able to pathway into further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Manukau Institute of Technology and Unitec - Unitec","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4209"},"4210":{"i":"4210","entryRequirements":"General Admission Requirements: Applicants must meet the following requirements:\n\r\na. a recognised Bachelor's degree (or higher) in a relevant discipline with merit achievement deemed to be a grade \n\r\naverage of B- or higher; or \n\r\nb. a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to merit achievement in a \n\r\nbachelor degree or equivalent.\n\n\n\r\nDomestic applicants must have achieved the minimum requirement to go to a New Zealand University or equivalent. International applicants must also meet the English Language Entry Requirements as stated by the New Zealand Qualifications Authority | Mana Tohu Matauranga O Aotearoa.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Applied Business will enable learners to apply an advanced body of knowledge in a chosen specialisation and confidently engage in research in an applied business context. Graduates will be able to apply advanced practices in the field of their chosen specialisation. This qualification prepares learners for further postgraduate study or to obtain employment, advance their careers or develop within their own organisation. The qualification will develop capable and responsible business professionals for careers in local and international economies.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Applied Business postgraduate qualifications will have the knowledge, skills and capabilities to make highly effective contributions to business practice in their specialisations in both domestic and international organisation contexts.    \n\r\nA graduate of the Master of Applied Business will be able to:    \n\r\n1. Apply advanced knowledge of business theory and practice to enhance organisational outcomes.    \n\r\n2. Undertake applied research to critically evaluate business challenges and opportunities to inform decision making.    \n\r\n3. Engage collaboratively with diverse teams and cultures in Aotearoa New Zealand and global contexts.    \n\r\n4. Communicate effectively and professionally with a range of stakeholders.    \n\r\n5. Critically engage with ethically and socially responsible business practices.","educationPathway":"Graduates from the Master of Applied Business will be able to pathway into research degrees at the same or higher level, such as Master's with a high research component and / or Professional Doctorates","developedBy":"Manukau Institute of Technology and Unitec - Unitec","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4210"},"4211":{"i":"4211","entryRequirements":"A completed application form. \n\r\nFor study options 1a, 1b, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6: Original transcripts showing a Bachelor's degree or a Graduate Diploma in a business-related subject, or a subject relevant to the specialised strand, from a recognized institution, including full transcripts; \n\r\nOR Evidence of acquiring the relevant skills and knowledge through appropriate work or professional experience in business or an area relevant to the specialised strand. \n\r\nFor study option 1c: Original transcripts showing a Master's degree, Postgraduate Diploma, or other NQF Level 8 qualification in a business-related subject from a recognized institution, including full transcripts; \n\r\nOR Original transcripts showing a Master's degree, Postgraduate Diploma, or other NQF Level 8 qualification in any subject from a recognized institution, including full transcripts, combined with a minimum of 3 years' relevant managerial and practical experience. \n\r\nICL will consider the applicant's academic achievement, work history, and evidence of preparedness for advance study and research at Master's level. \n\r\nA scanned PDF will be sufficient to progress the application, but original documents will be required on arrival at ICL Graduate Business School. Failure to provide original documents will result in the cancellation of the enrollment. \n\r\nFor international students, Academic IELTS with a minimum score of 6.5 overall (with no band score lower than 6.0 and gained within the past two years in one examination), or any other equivalent approved by NZQA. \n\r\nCredit transfer or RPL of up to 50% of the total credits, i.e. up to 90 of the 180 credits, required for the qualification will be negotiated on a case-by-case basis. \n\r\nICL Graduate Business School also strongly recommends that a Personal Statement, written by the applicant, is attached to the application explaining why they believe they should study the programme, their motivations and further aspirations.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The aim of this programme, with specialisations in Marketing, Construction Project Management, Project Management, Supply Chain and Logistics Management and Healthcare Management, is to enable experienced professionals and graduates of these specialisations seeking advanced managerial capability to critically examine management theories and practices and to undertake applied research so that they can:  \n\r\ndevelop advanced strategic leadership and management capabilities to lead organisational transformation in complex and dynamic environments; and  \n\r\ndevelop high-level skills and knowledge for leading, managing and transforming organizations within an environment of ubiquitous and continuous change; and  \n\r\napply this knowledge and these skills to contemporary organizations specialising with particular emphasis in areas of Marketing, Construction Project Management, Project Management, Logistics and Supply Chain and Healthcare Management in Aotearoa New  \n\r\nZealand and internationally.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Management will be able to:  \n\r\n1. Evaluate and apply advanced contemporary management theories to emerging situations in an organization.  \n\r\n2. Create an internal organisation culture with strong employee engagement, collaboration and teamwork, and ongoing learning and development in the changing environment.  \n\r\n3. Analyse, synthesise and communicate information, plans, policies and strategies to enhance business outcomes in an organization.  \n\r\n4. Apply leadership and management skills to improve business performance within an organisation in Aotearoa New Zealand or internationally.  \n\r\n5. Graduates of the Marketing strand will be able to critically evaluate and apply advanced marketing analytics, consumer behaviour theory, and AI-enabled marketing tools to design and implement data-driven marketing strategies in complex organisational contexts.  \n\r\n6. Graduates of the Construction Project Management strand will be able to critically evaluate and apply advanced project planning, risk management, and sustainability frameworks to the delivery of complex construction and infrastructure projects.  \n\r\n7. Graduates of the Project Management strand will be able to plan, lead, and evaluate complex projects and programmes by applying advanced project management methodologies, governance frameworks, and risk management principles to deliver strategic organisational  \n\r\noutcomes in diverse professional contexts.  \n\r\n8. Graduates of the Supply Chain and Logistics strand will be able to analyse, design, and optimise integrated supply chain and logistics systems using advanced analytical tools, sustainability principles, and global best-practice frameworks to enhance operational efficiency, resilience, and value creation.  \n\r\n9. Graduates of the Healthcare strand will be able to apply advanced management and leadership principles within healthcare and health-related organisations, integrating policy, quality improvement, and ethical decision-making to improve service delivery, organisational performance, and patient-centred outcomes.","educationPathway":"Further study in the relevant area","developedBy":"ICL Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4211"},"4287":{"i":"4287","entryRequirements":"Applicants must have a recognised Bachelor's degree (or higher) with merit achievement deemed to be a grade average of B- or higher OR a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to merit achievement in a bachelor degree or equivalent. Applicants must also meet the English Language Admission Requirements specified in Unitec's Admission Requirements Policy.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of the Master of Professional Accounting is to produce highly skilled graduates who can practice as accountants in a range of industries and communities within Aotearoa and overseas. As a conversion Masters, the qualification is aimed at graduates and professionals from diverse disciplines who desire to pursue a career in accounting and provides a pathway to membership with professional accounting bodies. The qualification seeks to meet the needs of small to medium enterprises along with those of larger organisations.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Professional Accounting will have the skills, knowledge and competencies to make highly effective contributions as professional accountants, both domestically and internationally. This includes analytical and decision-making skills, business advisory abilities, and research capabilities, to operate in a variety of business situations relating to the practice of accounting. Graduates will be able to:   \n\r\n1. Apply advanced knowledge of accounting theory and practice to enhance organisational outcomes.   \n\r\n2. Undertake applied research to critically evaluate organisational challenges and opportunities to inform decision making.   \n\r\n3. Engage collaboratively with diverse teams and cultures in Aotearoa New Zealand and global contexts.   \n\r\n4. Communicate effectively and professionally with a range of stakeholders.   \n\r\n5. Critically engage with ethically and socially responsible accounting practices.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this degree may choose to undertake further postgraduate studies in the fields of accounting and business. They will also be able to work towards full membership as a Chartered Accountant or Certified Practicing Accountant within the accounting profession. Graduates will be credited with 9 papers towards their professional membership.","developedBy":"Manukau Institute of Technology and Unitec - Unitec","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4287"},"4315":{"i":"4315","entryRequirements":"The academic entry requirement for the Postgraduate Certificate in Business Analytics is one of the following:*an NZQF-listed undergraduate degree (or equivalent)  in a related discipline or *at  the  Dean's  discretion,  where  an  applicant's  situation  is  compelling  but  not  covered  by  the  requirements listed above.  All  applicants  must  demonstrate  an  acceptable  level  of  English  language  fluency  prior  to  acceptance  in  the  programme. For international students, ways in which English language fluency may be demonstrated include the following:*successful  study  of  a  programme  in  which  English  was  the  language  of  instruction  (subject  to  the  conditions in EIT's Database for English Language Proficiency (DELP))*completion of a New Zealand Certificate in English Language (Level 5 with any endorsement)*IELTS Academic score of 6.5, with no band score lower than 6, achieved in a single test within the two years preceding enrolment*accepted international equivalents to the above IELTS scores, achieved in a single test within the two years preceding enrolment (see equivalency tables in the DELP).An international student must be in possession of an appropriate visa for the duration of their Programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Business Analytics is a Level 8 programme of 60 credits, that will enable students who have completed a Bachelor's  Degree in Business, Information Technology or similar, and/ or suitable work experience to achieve a postgraduate level qualification in the Business Analytics area.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Business Analytics will:1.Have specialised   conceptual   and   theoretical   knowledge, and   advanced   practical skills in Business Analytics2.Be   a   problem   solver   who   can   locate,   evaluate,   manipulate   and   use   information effectively and efficiently to improve organisational outcomes3.Be  able  to  deliver  insights  by  developing  and  interrogating  complex  data  models typically used by contemporary organisations4.Be able to effectively communicate knowledge, ideas, recommendations and decisions to diverse audiences5.Demonstrate a growth mind-set to maintain currency as a professional in the field of Business Analytics.","educationPathway":"Related Masters programmes in logistics, supply chain management, e-business and other related areas.","developedBy":"Eastern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4315"},"4577":{"i":"4577","entryRequirements":"Minimum entry requirements are\n\r\n1 a Bachelor's degree (or equivalent qualification) in a related discipline, or\n\r\n2 a combination of academic qualifications and relevant skills and knowledge acquired \n\r\nthrough work or professional experience that is deemed equivalent to 1 above.\n\r\n3 International applicants must demonstrate that they have equivalent academic \n\r\nqualifications and experience, and those for whom English is not their first language, \n\r\nmust provide evidence of English language competence of IELTS academic overall \n\r\nband score of 6.5 with no individual band less than 6.0, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Management will extend and  \n\r\ndeepen their knowledge and understanding of current management capabilities and issues \n\r\nin a range of applied settings through experiential learning strategies and reflective  \n\r\npractice. This qualification prepares students for further postgraduate study, or acquiring  \n\r\nadditional skills and knowledge for employment in a management-related role.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to: \n\r\n - Critically analyse and argue using empirical evidence \n\r\n - Think independently and critically enabling future-focused decision-making in real  \n\r\nworld situations \n\r\n - Engage in rigorous intellectual analysis, criticism and applied problem-solving \n\r\n - Work effectively in multicultural teams and exercise leadership in the workplace \n\r\n - Critically apply management knowledge and capabilities to new situations \n\r\n - Assess the impact of organisational practices on society and address related ethical and  \n\r\nsustainability issues. \n\r\n - Apply their professional learning and capabilities to be able to live and work in Aotearoa  \n\r\nNew Zealand.","educationPathway":"Further postgraduate study in business management related areas","developedBy":"Future Skills Academy Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4577"},"4597":{"i":"4597","entryRequirements":"To be admitted to the Master of Change and Organisational Resilience, all applicants must: \n\n\n\r\nhave a recognised Bachelor's Degree or Level 7 Graduate Diploma (or higher) AND a minimum of two years relevant industry experience. \n\n\n\r\nOr \n\n\n\r\nhave at least five years professional experience in a relevant industry or community demonstrating through evidence equivalence or higher to the qualification stated above. \n\n\n\r\nNote: Relevant professional industry experience can include paid or voluntary roles within organisations where formal or informal leadership can be evidenced. (for example, management and team leadership roles, elections to Boards, project leadership). Evidence that can be provided includes: professional and or community awards; references; published (or shared) outputs; invitations to represent professions and communities at conferences, by media. \n\n\n\r\nNote: To ensure that the Master of Change and Organisational Resilience is relevant to the applicant, an interview will take place with the applicant and the Programme Lead. The interview will ensure potential students understand the programme, and to allow The Mind Lab to help ensure the programme is a good fit for the applicant. \n\n\n\r\nEnglish Language Admission Requirements \n\r\nApplicants whose first language is not English must provide evidence of English language competence. This evidence may be in the form of: \n\r\n* A formal test of English Language \n\r\no IELTS academic band score of 6.5 (overall), with no individual band less than 6.0. \n\r\no TOEFL - Internet-based (Score of 79 with a minimum writing score of 21) \n\r\no Cambridge Certificate in Advanced English (CAE) Minimum of 176 or Certificate of Proficiency in English (CPE) minimum of 176, with no less than 169 in each skill. \n\r\no Pearson Test of English (PTE) Academic Overall score of 58 with no communicative skills score below 50. \n\r\n* Evidence of an academic qualification at level 7 or above, completed in one of the following countries, New Zealand, Australia, Canada, the Republic of Ireland, South Africa, the United Kingdom and the United States. \n\r\n* For domestic applicants, professional outputs or achievements in English language that can be evidence of competence equivalent to any of the above.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Change and Organisational Resilience (Level 9, 180 credits) aims to enable professionals and practitioners from a range of relevant industries to critically apply knowledge and skills to lead and manage change. The programme is designed to blend theoretical and practical knowledge to enable critical evaluation of the complex intersections of purpose, people, processes and technology which are implicated by change. This Master's programme will support the development of individual and organisational resilience and capability to apply future-focused practices needed to navigate change for sustainable and equitable outcomes in the context of New Zealand industries and communities.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Change and Organisational Resilience will be able to; \n\r\n1. Analyse critical social, cultural, economic, environmental and technological drivers of change that impact organisations. \n\r\n2. Evaluate Indigenous and contemporary practices that can support effective and authentic initiatives to build organisational resilience in the context of change. \n\r\n3. Critically reflect on personal and collective capability to lead sustainable change in practice. \n\r\n4. Apply culturally intelligent practice founded on principles of Te Tiriti o Waitangi to develop equitable and inclusive outcomes of change initiatives.  \n\r\n5. Develop culturally, methodologically and ethically sound organisational change initiatives to advance authentic leadership and management practice. \n\r\n6. Apply relevant knowledge, skills and capabilities to develop change initiatives focused on organisational resilience in the context of local and global disruption. \n\n\n\r\nAND for 90 credits at Level 9; \n\r\n7. Develop and apply new knowledge contributing to professional understandings of the complexity of leading transformational change in organisations.","educationPathway":"Graduates could continue study through a Doctoral pathway (research-based or professional). Entry into a Doctoral programme will be dependent on the regulations and entry requirements of the institution being applied to.","developedBy":"AcademyEx Education Limited Partnership","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4597"},"4705":{"i":"4705","entryRequirements":"To enter the Master of Business Innovation and Leadership and Innovation candidates will: \n\r\n - have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelor's Degree achieved with a B average in the final year, or a Bachelor Honours Degree or a Postgraduate Diploma  \n\r\nOR   \n\r\n - Have been awarded a Bachelor's Degree followed by relevant professional experience  \n\r\nOR \n\r\n - have demonstrated equivalent practical, professional and/or scholarly experience. \n\r\nApplicants whose first language is not English are required to provide satisfactory evidence of proficiency in the English language, such as a minimum score of 625 on the TOEFL test, or 6.5 on the IELTS. \n\r\nInternational students are required to meet the minimum English language requirements for this level programme as detailed on the following NZQA webpages: \n\n\nhere\n \n\r\nand \n\n\nhere","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Business Innovation and Leadership (formally known as Master of Creative Enterprise and Innovation) will enable students to experience a cutting-edge learning journey to identify and develop entrepreneurial characteristics to become leaders of change and impact the entre/intrapreneurial world. As innovators they will pioneer the art of non-linear problem solving to become resilient and risk tolerant as opposed to risk averse.  \n\r\nThe key is 'doing it for real', meaning a hands-on, applied approach to everything during the programme. The programme will open the entrepreneurial door within participants to enable them to recognise new business, social, indigenous or community focused opportunities, develop a minimum viable product (MVP) and approach investors. It is a gateway to create wealth by building a sustainable business or becoming an innovative leader within a large organization, or social or community focused enterprise.  \n\r\nTo succeed, founders and entrepreneurs need critical thinking and analysis skills, problem solving, self-management, working with people and communication. The MBIL programme nurtures these skills, and is a platform for human centred creativity, impacting social, cultural, economic, and environmental outcomes and job creation. The relationship between creativity, enterprise, innovation and leadership will enable graduates to work beyond borders and become global citizens.  \n\r\nThe MBIL programme intentionally builds resilience and confidence alongside the development of the creative, innovative concepts/product by taking an integrated approach, to support a creative, innovative business leaders or founders and those who seek a different direction. This approach is a point of difference for this programme.","graduateProfile":"GPO1: Demonstrate an agile mind-set, communications skills, innovative leadership, and resilience through creative storytelling. GPO2: Apply critical thinking to discern the social, cultural, environmental, and economic impacts of design innovation. GPO3: Create innovative, non-linear solutions to design challenges. GPO4: Establish and monitor realistic goals to transform and actualise a minimum viable produce (MVP) to market readiness. GPO5:  Synthesise strategic business insights, research, and design thinking to generate future-focused creative innovations. GPO6: Evaluate diverse business models, market dynamics, and emerging trends to make executive decisions that deliver on competitive advantages. GPO7: Lead visionary business strategies to launch innovative ventures, cultivate creative ecosystems, and generate sustainable value in market spaces.","educationPathway":"This programme leads to the award of: Master of Business Innovation and Leadership, level 9, 180 credits.  \n\r\nGraduates of this programme may progress to doctoral studies, depending on the entry requirements of the receiving programme.","developedBy":"Whitecliffe Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4705"},"4721":{"i":"4721","entryRequirements":"Applicants must have:- attained the age of 21 years and either:- completed all requirements of a relevant Bachelor Degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in business and/or management from a recognised institution; OR- completed all requirements of a relevant Bachelor Degree or Graduate Certificate or Graduate Diploma in technology from a recognised institution and a minimum of one year's work or professional experience in the fields of business and/or management. Under this criterion, the suitability of the applicant will be decided upon by the Aspire2 Academic Board; OR- acquired the relevant skills and knowledge to gain entry into this programme with a minimum of three years' work or professional experience in the fields of technology, business and/or management. Under this criterion, the suitability of the applicant will be decided upon by the Aspire2 Academic Board. English Language Requirements Candidates with English as a second language must provide evidence of the required English language requirements from an internationally recognised English Proficiency Test. This includes:- IELTS academic test - with a minimum score of 6.5 and no band score lower than 6. (Scores must be taken from a single IELTS Test Report Form)- TOEFL paper-based test (pBT) - with a minimum score of 590 and an essay score 5.5 TWE- TOEFL Internet-based test (iBT) - with a minimum score of 79 and a writing score of 21- Cambridge English Qualifications - with a minimum C1 Advanced or C2 Proficiency with a score of 176 or above and no less than 169 in each skill- OET - with a minimum grade C+ or 300 in all sub-tests- NZCEL - Level 5- Pearson Test of English (Academic) - with a PTE academic score of 58 or above and no band score lower than 50- Language Certificate - with a minimum achievement of C1 Expert IESOL (LRWS) with HIGH PASS and no less than pass in each skill or C2 Mastery IESOL (LRWS) with PASS and no less than pass in each skill- Trinity ISE - ISE III with no less than pass in any band. Results must come from one test conducted in the last 2 years. Application Requirement for All Candidates As part of the entry requirements, all applicants will be required to provide a 500-word statement about their professional goals and rationale for seeking entry into the programme. Suitable candidates will be selected based on the alignment between the applicant's aspirations and by assessing whether the applicant has the pre-requisite skills for successful achievement.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Digital Transformation in Business targets students who have relevant qualifications or experience in technology, business and/or management and enables them to significantly deepen their knowledge and capability to facilitate digital transformation in business. The aim of the programme is to develop business professionals who can think critically and competently facilitate digital transformation in business, both strategy development and implementation.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Digital Transformation in Business will be able to:\n\r\n- Evaluate current and emerging technologies to identify viable opportunities for enhanced business performance.\n\r\n- Evaluate the impact of cultural, social, ethical and sustainability factors on digital business contexts.\n\r\n- Integrate information from a range of sources to propose effective and efficient recommendations to improve business performance.\n\r\n- Develop and facilitate digital transformation strategies to enhance performance in a digital business context.\n\r\n- Integrate the values, attitudes and continuous development approaches consistent with responsible citizenship, professionalism and leadership to improve business performance.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Digital Transformation in Business Level 8 may be able to continue their studies to a more advanced level.","developedBy":"Aspire2 Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=4721"},"5267":{"i":"5267","entryRequirements":"Whare Mairanga Terms and Conditions of Enrolment and any relevant conditions specified by the Ministry of Education, the Education and Training Act 2020 and the Tertiary Commission. Uri should be:\n\r\n- 18 years or older;\n\r\n- A New Zealand citizen (which includes citizens of Cook Island, Niue and Tokelau);\n\r\n- A New Zealand resident currently living in New Zealand;\n\r\n- An Australian citizen currently living in New Zealand;\n\r\n- An Australian permanent resident who has a returning residents visa and is currently living in New Zealand;\n\n\n\r\nUri must meet the following admission criteria to be admitted to the programme:\n\r\n- Proficiency in spoken and written reo Māori.\n\r\n- An undergraduate degree and/or 2 or more years relevant experience in a leadership kaupapa within an educational context or within a community, marae, hapū and/or iwi.\n\r\n- An endorsement or support letter/video from a kura, community organisation, marae, hapū and/or iwi that outlines the ability to complete the programme and any support that can be provided to uri.\n\r\n- Special admission may be granted to uri who do not meet the admission criteria above but can demonstrate sufficient evidence of skills, knowledge and/or education within a mana motuhake leadership context. Any special admission applications will be approved by the Pou Mairanga or delegate.\n\n\n\r\n- Uri granted special admission may be required to meet specific conditions for their continued enrolment. This will be communicated in writing to uri at the time of granting the admission. Conditions may include provisional admission requirement to complete pre- or co-requisites; and/or requirement to maintain a specified level of achievement.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Ko ngā whāinga o te hōtaka nei: \n\r\n- He whakatinana i te tautake o Te Tihi o Angitu hei puna whāngai i te tātāriki mana motuhake, e whakawhanake ai i ngā tātāriki mana motuhake i ngā horopaki ao mātauranga, i ngā horopaki whānui ake rānei. \n\r\n- He whakamahi i ngā mātāpono tauutuutu, e arotake arohaehae ai i ngā tauira whakahaere, i ngā tauira tātāriki a te Māori, a ngā iwi taketake me ētahi tauira tātāriki anō e hāngai ana ki te horopaki tātāriki mana motuhake. \n\r\n- He whaitake te mahi hei tātāriki ara whakamana-uara, e whakatere ai i ngā āhuatanga tuatinitini me ngā wero tukituki o te whāngai rauemi me te ahumoni i waenganui i ngā hapori kanorau. \n\r\n- He whakatinana i ngā hua o te tātāriki hautū ā-Tīpuna, e whakapuāwai ai i te pitomata o ngā hapori kanorau.","graduateProfile":"Ko tā te Manu Pīrere: \n\n\n\r\n1. He huritao arohaehae me te whakamahi i ngā pūkenga tātāriki mana motuhake, te mātauranga me ngā āheinga e tautoko ai i ngā hapori kia whai mana motuhake ai rātou. \n\r\n2. He whakamahi i ngā mātāpono tauutuutu, e arotake arohaehae ai i ngā tauira whakahaere, i ngā tauira tātāriki a te Māori, a ngā iwi taketake me ētahi tauira tātāriki anō e hāngai ana ki te horopaki tātāriki mana motuhake. \n\r\n3. He arotake arohaehae me te whakamahi i ngā uara o te tātāriki mana motuhake e whakatere ai i ngā hononga pāhekoheko tuatinitini, i ngā rauemi me ngā pūnaha ahumoni ki te horopaki mātauranga, ki horopaki kē atu rānei. \n\r\n4. He kōtuitui i ngā hua hautū ā-Tīpuna ki te tātāriki mana motuhake, e whaitake ai ngā rautaki auaha, kia whakapuāwai ai te pitomata o ngā hapori.","educationPathway":"The following education pathways are available for graduates of Te Korowai Tātāriki Mana Motuhake (Kaupae 8): \n\n\n\r\nMasters level programmes at universities and wānanga subject to entry requirements. As Masters' programmes can range from 1 - 2 years in duration, graduates of this programme will have to go through an application process at each university and/or wānanga to determine at which stage of the Master's programme they will be eligible.","developedBy":"Nga Kura a Iwi o Aotearoa Incorporated","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5267"},"5276":{"i":"5276","entryRequirements":"Academic\n\r\nGeneral Admission Requirements: Applicants must meet the following requirements:\n\r\n* Bachelor's degree (or equivalent) in business, management or a related hospitality area, \n\r\nwith at least a B- grade average at level 7 (or higher). \n\r\n* LCBNZ Postgraduate Diploma in Hospitality Management (joint application with this \n\r\nprogramme)\n\r\n* Degrees in other disciplines may be considered if the applicant has at least three years' \n\r\nrelevant hospitality experience at a supervisory level, or equivalent.\n\r\nEnglish Language (for international students)\n\r\nThe minimum entry requirement for international students is IELTS Academic score of 6.5 with no \n\r\nband score lower than 6 (or equivalent). \n\r\nSpecial Entry\n\r\nAn applicant who does not meet all entry requirements may be granted entry where the Head of \n\r\nSchool is satisfied the applicant is capable of undertaking the programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Hospitality Management Applied at Le Cordon Bleu New Zealand is aimed to equip  \n\r\ngraduates with advanced knowledge, skills, and expertise in hospitality management, empowering  \n\r\nthem to create, own, and lead world-class businesses. The programme is termed 'applied' as it  \n\r\nencompasses 'real world' practical experience essential for success in the dynamic and competitive  \n\r\nhospitality industry, including the application of key aspects of te ao Māori that will enable graduates  \n\r\nto work successfully senior leadership roles both within New Zealand's hospitality landscape and  \n\r\noverseas. This programme is aimed and offers an elevated level of study for both hospitality  \n\r\ngraduates and mid-level professionals from New Zealand and abroad.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the MHMA programme will have the knowledge, skills and capabilities to make highly effective contributions to hospitality business practice in both domestic and international organisation contexts. A Graduate of the Master of Hospitality Management Applied programme will be able to: 1. Evaluate and apply highly specialised knowledge and skills to the field of hospitality management. 2. Research, analyse and generate solutions to complex and sometimes unpredictable hospitality management current and emerging problems. 3. Establish and maintain an inclusive workplace culture of ethical and cultural integrity within a hospitality management context. 4. Demonstrate advanced leadership skills and risk management techniques within a hospitality setting.","educationPathway":"Graduates who wish to pursue further study can seek admission to professional doctoral  \n\r\nprogrammes in New Zealand or overseas.","developedBy":"Le Cordon Bleu New Zealand Institute Limited Partnership","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5276"},"5422":{"i":"5422","entryRequirements":"Admission to the programme is subject to applicants meeting the requirements as stated below, and those contained in the Admissions and Enrolment Policy. Applicants must, generally, meet the criteria for a recognised Bachelor's Degree or equivalent, or possess relevant work or professional experience at an appropriate level. Exceptions for discretionary and special admission are available, subject to approval by the Academic Board. There are no age restrictions to admissions.\n\r\nA recognised Bachelor's Degree or Graduate Diploma (or higher) in a relevant discipline with a grade average of B- or higher, and at least two years of work experience in an operational setting relevant to the hotel industry; or \n\r\nA professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to a Bachelor's Degree or equivalent, with the equivalent of a grade average of B- or higher; or \n\r\nAt least five years experience as a director or senior leadership role in a 4 or 5 star hotel. \n\n\n\r\nInternational students that meet the English language requirements as set out in Rule 22 of the NZQF Programme Approval, Recognition and Accreditation Rules 2025, may be eligible for enrolment subject to meeting appropriate academic criteria. In addition, applicants for whom English is not their first language require an Academic IELTS score of 6.5 or equivalent, with no band score lower than 6.0. \n\n\n\r\nDiscretionary admission: Applicants who do not meet the qualification admission requirements defined above may apply for discretionary admission by completion of a relevant programme of learning at NZQF level 7. Applicants who do not meet the work experience admission requirements defined above may apply for permission to undertake operational training and will be required to successfully complete operational training before undertaking the industry placement component of the programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Applied Hotel Management aims to foster advanced expertise and innovation in the complex domain of hotel management, catering to a diverse cohort of learners and to equip students with the capabilities needed to enhance hotel operations, employ advanced marketing and financial strategies, and lead sustainable and innovative projects within the hospitality sector. Learners will be equipped with a toolbox of contemporary academic and industry frameworks that can be applied to deal with real world industry challenges.","graduateProfile":"On successful completion of the programme, graduates will be able to: \n\r\nGPO 1: Apply advanced operational management frameworks and methodologies to optimise efficiency, service quality, and overall performance in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO 2: Apply advanced theories of change management, organisational behaviour, and critical decision-making to drive business growth and transformation in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO 3: Develop data-driven marketing strategies to enhance brand positioning and customer loyalty in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO 4: Apply financial analysis tools, forecasting techniques, and strategic financial decision-making models to effectively manage financial resources in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO 5: Utilise advanced data analytics to enhance operational and strategic outcomes in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO 6: Critically evaluate sustainable business practises to enhance cultural, environmental, economic, and social sustainability within the hotel industry.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Master of Applied Hotel Management (Level 9) may be able to continue onto Doctoral-level studies in management related fields at New Zealand or international universities","developedBy":"Pacific International Hotel Management School Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5422"},"5423":{"i":"5423","entryRequirements":"Admission to the programme is subject to applicants meeting the requirements as stated below, and those contained in the Admissions and Enrolment Policy. Applicants must, generally, meet the criteria for a recognised Bachelor's Degree or equivalent, or possess relevant work or professional experience at an appropriate level. Exceptions for discretionary and special admission are available, subject to approval by the Academic Board. There are no age restrictions to admissions.\n\r\nA recognised Bachelor's Degree or Graduate Diploma (or higher) in a relevant discipline, and at least two years of work experience in an operational setting relevant to the hotel industry; or\n\r\nA professional qualification in a relevant discipline, recognised as being equivalent to a Bachelor's Degree or equivalent.\n\r\nInternational students that meet the English language requirements as set out in Rule 22 of the NZQF Programme Approval, Recognition and Accreditation Rules 2022, may be eligible for enrolment subject to meeting appropriate academic criteria.  In addition, applicants for whom English is not their first language require an Academic IELTS score of 6.5 or equivalent, with no band score lower than 6.0.  \n\r\nDiscretionary admission: Applicants who do not meet the qualification admission requirements defined above may apply for discretionary admission by completion of a relevant programme of learning at NZQF level 7.  Applicants who do not meet the work experience admission requirements defined above may apply for permission to undertake operational training and will be required to successfully complete operational training before undertaking the industry placement component of the programme","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Hotel Management aims to foster advanced expertise and innovation in the complex domain of hotel management, catering to a diverse cohort of learners and equip students with the capabilities needed to enhance hotel operations, employ advanced marketing and financial strategies, and lead sustainable and innovative projects within the hospitality sector. Learners will be equipped with a toolbox of contemporary academic and industry frameworks that can be applied to deal with real world industry challenges.","graduateProfile":"GPO1: Apply advanced operational management strategies and industry best practices to enhance efficiency and performance in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO2: Critically evaluate complex organisational challenges to manage change effectively and make data-driven leadership decisions in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO3: Develop evidence-based marketing strategies that enhance brand loyalty, customer engagement, and competitive positioning in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO4: Apply financial analysis techniques and strategic decision-making frameworks to optimise financial resource management and ensure business sustainability in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO5: Critically evaluate data to influence and enhance management strategies and service delivery in the hotel industry. \n\r\nGPO6: Critically evaluate cultural, environmental, economic, and social sustainability principles to promote responsible and ethical business practises in the hotel industry.","educationPathway":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Hotel Management (Level 8) will be able to continue onto the Master of Applied Hotel Management (Level 9) at PIHMS or to other Master-level studies in management related fields at New Zealand or international universities.","developedBy":"Pacific International Hotel Management School Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5423"},"5544":{"i":"5544","entryRequirements":"5.1 Admission\n\r\nAll applicants will be approved for admission by the Faculty Lead or their delegate. Applicants must fulfil the following requirements for academic admission.\n\r\n5.1.1 Academic Admission category\n\r\nTo be considered for general admission onto the programme, applicants must:\n\r\n*\tHave successfully completed a Bachelor's degree, Graduate Diploma, Bachelor Honours Degree or a Postgraduate Diploma (or equivalent qualification) in a relevant discipline, such as social sciences, IT disciplines, health sector, business sector, commerce, health, construction or another related discipline.\n\r\n*\tInternational ākonga who have successfully completed a bachelor's degree (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university (or similar) and wish to undertake further study with a view to employment in a management position within Aotearoa |New Zealand.\n\n\n\r\nĀkonga who do not meet the above criteria but have industry experience and wish to further develop their knowledge, skills and application may be considered on a case-by-case basis by the Faculty Lead.  Entry will be dependent on an assessment of the applicant's level of achievement in their undergraduate programme or other prior study and/or experimental work-related learning, their potential for success on the programme, and/or their industry experience and portfolio.\n\r\nApplicants for whom English is a second language \n\r\n*\tmust demonstrate English language proficiency equivalent to an IELTS Academic score of 6.5 overall, with no individual band below 6.0. All English language test results must be dated within two years before the programme start date.\n\r\n*\tĀkonga who have completed at least five  years of full-time study in an approved English-medium secondary or tertiary qualification in certain countries (e.g., USA, UK, Australia, Canada, New Zealand) may be exempt from submitting an English language test score. Their qualification must be approved by NZQA or meet their criteria for English-medium instruction.\n\n\n\r\nWhen required, the Faculty Lead or their delegate may interview applicants to determine their eligibility for admission.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The MMgmt programme aims to empower ākonga from a range of academic and professional backgrounds-including, but not limited to, social sciences, information technology, health, business, commerce, and construction-to develop advanced management capabilities that are required to succeed in today's digital and global business environments. Through a strong integration of applied knowledge and practical skills, the programme builds on prior experience and fosters innovative thinking and agile management practices. Ākonga will develop in-depth knowledge of contemporary management trends and the skills that enable them to respond effectively to the evolving demands of dynamic, fast-paced organisational settings. \n\r\nThe programme is designed to prepare graduates for leadership and management roles in national and international contexts. It also addresses emerging global business challenges such as digital transformation, cross-cultural collaboration, and sustainability, equipping ākonga to lead future-focused and socially responsible business practices.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Master of Management programme will be able to: \n\r\n - Critique advanced knowledge and skills and apply these in a business and management context to achieve organisational goals. \n\r\n - Analyse local and global challenges when working with national and multinational organisations and elaborate on the application of well-thought-through solutions. \n\r\n - Critically evaluate business and management theories and practices to inform strategic decision-making in diverse organisational contexts. \n\r\n - Using appropriate tools, technologies, and formats, confidently communicate complex management ideas clearly and persuasively to a range of audiences,  \n\r\n - Evaluate legal and ethical considerations that will impact any risk identification from an organisation's perspective","educationPathway":"Graduates of this programme may be eligible to enrol in higher-level programmes offered across the sector, such as:  \n\r\n - Doctoral level study in Business or Management, or other related fields.  Ākonga will be advised that they may need to complete additional research or courses to gain entry to a doctoral programme, with any decision on progression and admission being subject to the requirements of the receiving institution.","developedBy":"Yoobee Colleges Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5544"},"5612":{"i":"5612","entryRequirements":"Admission Criteria:\n\r\nThe minimum entry qualification for this Postgraduate Certificate is:\n\r\n-\tA Bachelor's degree or a Graduate Diploma or a Graduate Certificate in a related discipline OR\n\r\n-\tA combination of academic qualifications and relevant skills and knowledge acquired through work or professional experience that is deemed equivalent to the above.\n\r\nDocumentary evidence of the applicant's ability to undertake postgraduate study is required, including an official transcript of the qualification(s) achieved.\n\n\n\r\nEnglish Language Entry Requirements: \n\r\n-\tApplicants must have sufficient competence in the English language to undertake the Programme which is taught and assessed in English AND\n\r\n-\tInternational learners must meet the English Proficiency Outcomes for International learners as set out in Appendix 1 of the NZQCF Programme Approval and Accreditation Rules. These can be accessed at https://www2.nzqa.govt.nz/\n\n\n\r\nVisa and Insurance:\n\r\nInternational learners require a valid visa and insurance to study on the programme. The type of visa will determine the mode of delivery.\n\n\n\r\nSelection:\n\r\nApplicants will be selected in order of successful application. This programme of study is open to those who have met the entrance requirements and programme admission regulations. Applicants may be interviewed in person or via a suitable digital platform.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Business Intelligence equips learners with theoretical knowledge and advanced skills in business analysis to benefit organisational transformation and business decision-making in SMEs, global corporations, NGOs, and local communities. The programme offers a comprehensive and well-rounded curriculum to allow for career progression and higher education. \n\n\n\r\nLearners, with an undergraduate qualification or professional work experience in a relevant discipline, will gain an advanced body of knowledge and may progress into higher level positions in Aotearoa New Zealand or overseas.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will be able to: \n\r\n- Apply advanced discipline-specific theories, techniques, and concepts to critically and professionally evaluate business intelligence strategies, change management processes, and emerging technologies that drive strategic organisational performance and data-driven decision making in contemporary professional practice. \n\r\n- Appraise literature and theories of ethical practices, legal requirements and sustainable business approaches to inform organisational management and strategic decision-making specific to business intelligence and relevant applications in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural society.","educationPathway":"Graduates may be able to pathway into the Master of Business Analytics.","developedBy":"New Zealand School of Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5612"},"5613":{"i":"5613","entryRequirements":"The minimum entry qualification for this Master's degree is:\n\r\n-\tBachelor's degree or Postgraduate Diploma or Postgraduate Certificate in a related discipline OR\n\r\n-\tGraduate Diploma in a related discipline with an average grade of B- OR\n\r\n-\tA combination of academic qualifications and relevant skills and knowledge acquired through work or professional experience (min. 2 ½ years in the last 6 years) that is deemed equivalent to the above.\n\r\nDocumentary evidence of the applicant's ability to undertake postgraduate study is required, including an official transcript of the qualification(s) achieved.\n\n\n\r\nEnglish Language Entry Requirements: \n\r\n-\tApplicants must have sufficient competence in the English language to undertake the Programme which is taught and assessed in English AND\n\r\n-\tInternational learners must meet the English Proficiency Outcomes for International learners as set out in Appendix 1 of the NZQCF Programme Approval and Accreditation Rules. These can be accessed at https://www2.nzqa.govt.nz/\n\n\n\r\nVisa and Insurance:\n\r\nInternational learners require a valid visa and insurance to study on the programme. The type of visa will determine the mode of delivery.\n\n\n\r\nSelection:\n\r\nApplicants will be selected in order of successful application. This programme of study is open to those who have met the entrance requirements and programme admission regulations. Applicants may be interviewed in person or via a suitable digital platform.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Business Intelligence equips learners with a strong understanding of descriptive and diagnostic analytics, utilising advanced professional skills to focus on business performance whilst improving organisations' operational efficiency and supporting ethical business decision-making. Graduates of this Master's degree will  be capable of generating and applying actionable insights that drive operational optimisation and give organisations a decisive competitive advantage. The programme is aimed for graduates with prior study in related disciplines who aspire to progress into senior roles in business environments in Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. \n\n\n\r\nGraduates will be equipped with advanced business knowledge and skills to deliver practical solutions and create value across diverse sectors and industries, contributing meaningfully to organisations, local communities, and the global economy.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of this Master's Degree will be able to meet the following programme outcomes.  \n\n\n\r\nGPO1: Apply advanced discipline-specific theories, techniques and concepts to critically and professionally evaluate business intelligence strategies, change management processes, and emerging technologies that drive strategic organisational performance and data driven decision making in professional practice. \n\r\nGPO2: Appraise literature and theories of ethical practices, legal requirements and sustainable business approaches to inform organisational management and strategic decision-making specific to business intelligence and relevant applications in Aotearoa New Zealand's bicultural society. \n\r\nGPO3: Synthesise advanced analytical frameworks and emerging technologies to drive strategic business optimisation, entrepreneurial innovation, and sustainable digital transformation that enhances organisational performance and competitive advantage in contemporary business environments.  \n\r\nGPO4: Critically evaluate ethical leadership, cultural responsiveness, professional conduct and governance in relation to the strategic use of business intelligence for addressing complex challenges in diverse organisational contexts in Aotearoa New Zealand.  \n\n\n\r\n(Coursework only)  \n\r\nGPO5: Design and lead ethically grounded, business intelligence strategies that integrate innovation, security, interdisciplinary and cultural responsiveness in global and local organisational contexts. \n\n\n\r\n(Capstone Project) \n\r\nGPO6: Apply advanced proficiency in data-driven decision-making to generate actionable insights that effectively address complex, real-world challenges through independent analysis and strategic communication to diverse stakeholders.  \n\r\nGPO7: Design and lead ethically grounded, business intelligence strategies that integrate innovation, security, interdisciplinary and/or cultural responsiveness in global and local organisational contexts.","educationPathway":"Graduates of this Master's degree will have achieved study output to an advanced standard including a research component and may be considered for admission to a programme of advanced study and/or original industry research.","developedBy":"New Zealand School of Education Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=5613"},"110044":{"i":"110044","entryRequirements":"Applicants must have a degree or a minimum of five years full-time equivalent work experience, which includes relevant experience, as determined by the Director, USQ Australian Graduate School of Business. International candidates for admission must demonstrate appropriate English language ability through English as a first language; at least two years of prior successful full-time study in which English was the language of education; or an IELTS (Academic) grade 6.5 (or better (no component lower than 6.0).","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Business Project is a practical project work requiring students to investigate a particular aspect of an organisation's business or management practices. Students will be required to spend some time on the organisation's premises. This may range from as little as 10 hours up to 50 hours, depending upon the project's scope. \n\n\n\r\n- Discuss and apply the basic theories and skills of modern management. \n\r\n- Demonstrate competence in a range of areas relevant to management practice at senior levels. \n\r\n- Communicate and interact effectively with other people within an organisation. \n\r\n- Comprehend, analyse and evaluate internal and external environmental forces, and develop strategy for the management of change. \n\r\n- Analyse developments in a chosen area of management, and to critically evaluate the relationships between such developments and contemporary theory and practice. \n\r\n- Further enhance their managerial skills through a commitment to ongoing managerial development. \n\r\n- Apply their knowledge of current behavioural, policy and strategic issues to their experience of organisations so as to improve organisational efficiency. \n\r\n- Integrate a thorough understanding of the relevant political, cultural and business environment, and of the ethical standards in modern business to improve organisational practice.","graduateProfile":"This programme will give you the edge in a competitive work environment by helping you to understand and make critical decisions about change. You will learn about sustainability across global markets and contexts and contemporary business management.","developedBy":"UUNZ Institute of Business Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=110044"},"111515":{"i":"111515","entryRequirements":"Applicants must have a degree or a minimum of five years full-time equivalent work experience, which includes relevant experience, as determined by the Director, USQ Australian Graduate School of Business. International candidates for admission must demonstrate appropriate English language ability through English as a first language; at least two years of prior successful full-time study in which English was the language of education; or an IELTS (Academic) grade 6.5 (or better (no component lower than 6.0).","strategicPurposeStatement":"This is an advanced cross disciplinary academic programme that aims to build and extend business related skills in two specialised areas. It provides students with the ability to match their specialisations with their career goals. \n\n\n\r\n- Discuss and apply the basic theories and skills of modern management. \n\r\n- Demonstrate competence in a range of areas relevant to management practice at senior levels. \n\r\n- Communicate and interact effectively with other people within an organisation. \n\r\n- Comprehend, analyse and evaluate internal and external environmental forces, and develop strategy for the management of change. \n\r\n- Analyse developments in a chosen area of management, and to critically evaluate the relationships between such developments and contemporary theory and practice. \n\r\n- Further enhance their managerial skills through a commitment to ongoing managerial development. \n\r\n- Apply theories and skills of management practice in the international business environment \n\r\n- Demonstrate competence in a range of areas relevant to management practice at senior levels in internationally-focused businesses.","graduateProfile":"You will be able to choose two specialisations that will broaden your knowledge, enhance your expertise and complement your career ambitions.  \n\r\n         *   Big Data and Visualisation \n\r\n          *   Digital Transformation \n\r\n          *   Enterprise Leadership \n\r\n          *   Finance \n\r\n          *   International Business   \n\n\n\r\nThe third component of your studies will be a research project which will expand your knowledge in innovative business and entrepreneurship. This degree emphasizes collaboration with other specialities to prepare you for decision making for the future ensuring you are well equipped for this era in innovation.","developedBy":"UUNZ Institute of Business Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=111515"},"112634":{"i":"112634","entryRequirements":"Admission normally requires a tertiary qualification at a bachelor degree or equivalent from a recognised institution, and a minimum of two years full-time equivalent relevant and appropriate work experience. Candidates who do not hold an undergraduate degree will be considered for admission if they have had a minimum of five years full-time equivalent and appropriate work experience. Applicants must demonstrate appropriate English language ability through English as a first language, prior education in English, and IELTS grade 6.5 or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to understand selected theories and skills associated with a limited number of management discipline areas; apply acquired knowledge associated with their studies to their work environments; synthesise selected areas of managerial knowledge to produce meaningful assignments/reports; display competencies in a limited number of postgraduate discipline areas.","developedBy":"UUNZ Institute of Business Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"Quality Assurance Division, NZQA","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=112634"},"AK1096":{"i":"AK1096","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent.  Relevant professional experience approved as equivalent to a bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Diploma in Human Performance Leadership, who complete all four Level 8 courses will demonstrate advanced knowledge across human performance optimisation, leadership psychology, team dynamics, and innovative leadership. They will critically apply psychological, physiological, and relational principles, and critically apply communication and interpersonal strategies to build psychologically safe, high-trust performance cultures. They will also demonstrate cultural fluency by engaging respectfully with Maori and other Indigenous knowledge systems. Graduates are prepared for leadership, coaching, or performance-support roles and for progression to the Master of Human Performance Leadership.","graduateProfile":"Video-based tasks, scenario-based analysis, reflective journals, and applied problem-solving activities.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1096"},"WI0967":{"i":"WI0967","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree with at least a B- grade average across the 300 level papers, or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This Masters degree will give students the skills, knowledge and abilities that will enable graduates to advance professional practice in their subject.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0967"},"AK1065":{"i":"AK1065","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree with a minimum of a B- grade average in papers at Level 7, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The main goal of the Master of Global Business is to develop the knowledge, understanding and skills of non-international business graduates in order to prepare them for professional roles in international business. By adding value and building capabilities on top of a prior undergraduate degree, the Master of Global Business degree will enhance these graduates career opportunities and employment prospects.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1065"},"AU5720":{"i":"AU5720","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree, a Postgraduate Diploma in Business (with a minimum GPA), or a professional qualification in a relevant subject, and three years relevant leadership/management experience. References and an interview may also be required.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertLdGov graduates will know and understand the core tenets of leadership and governance especially as applied to a New Zealand context. They will be critical, reflective and confident practitioners able to build their own leadership and governance practice in service of their personal and professional goals.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5720"},"AU1004":{"i":"AU1004","entryRequirements":"A relevant degree or a relevant professional qualification, and at least two years of relevant work experience, or five years of relevant work experience. Tests of academic aptitude and or interviews may be required.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipBus graduates will have acquired the knowledge and skills in specialist fields of business essential for them to perform at a high personal level. They will have the capability to analyse complex business situations, integrate contemporary theory with best business practice and have demonstrated problem solving skills as individuals and as part of a team.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU1004"},"AK1077":{"i":"AK1077","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with a B grade average in courses at level 7, or equivalent and at least three years of relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MDTL graduates will have advanced strategic and applied leadership capabilities essential for navigating and driving digital transformation. They will be critical thinkers, equipped to bridge technological opportunities with organisational goals and contribute to innovation. Graduates will be prepared for roles leading digital change such as Transformation Lead, Digital Strategist, and Innovation Manager, contributing to the digital maturity and success of organisations and communities.","graduateProfile":"Reports, projects, reflective journals/portfolios, case studies, proposals, presentations.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1077"},"AK3748":{"i":"AK3748","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertIHM graduates will demonstrate an advanced level of understanding of international hospitality management and issues and will be competent and reflective practitioners.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3748"},"WI0948":{"i":"WI0948","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Bachelor of Business with Honours (BBus(Hons)) is a one-year postgraduate qualification that develops advanced professional knowledge and an introduction to the research literature in a subject area that has been taken as a major in an undergraduate business degree.  It includes a requirement for independent research.  This qualification may also be taken as the first stage of a programme leading to higher level qualification such as a master degree or PhD.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0948"},"VI00D4":{"i":"VI00D4","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or Certificate in Management Studies; three years of relevant work experience; and acceptance by the Programme Director as capable of proceeding with the proposed course of study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained a broad-based management education programme, focusing on strategic issues.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00D4"},"AU5664":{"i":"AU5664","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertBusDev graduates will have attained a set of capabilities in areas of study related to business management. They will be equipped to enter career pathways related to business management within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5664"},"LI0111":{"i":"LI0111","entryRequirements":"A relevant undergraduate degree with an average of B+ or higher in 300 level subjects.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the BTM(Hons) will have enhanced research skills and aptitudes in tourism management and tourism policy, planning and development.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0111"},"LI7205":{"i":"LI7205","entryRequirements":"An undergraduate qualification in a relevant field achieved at an above average level, usually a B+","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will significantly progress their understanding of the components that make up agribusiness systems and will know how to strategically use components and appropriate methods to leverage innovative systems, products and environments in inter- and trans- disciplinary contexts and settings.  They'll understand the role of management in the integration of these components and will be able to utilise appropriate skills to provide relevant management and leadership to assist in the operation of sustainable agribusinesses.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7205"},"AU5759":{"i":"AU5759","entryRequirements":"Completed a relevant Bachelors or Bachelors Honours degree with a minimum GPA and MATHS 108 or STATS 108 or the equivalent, or the Postgraduate Diploma in Business in Administration or Business Management with a minimum GPA and 15 relevant course points and completed 15 points from BUSADMIN 763, BUSMAN 707, MATHS 108, STATS 108, or the equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertAppFin graduates will demonstrate the technical knowledge and skills in financial analysis and financial management required for entry into careers as financial analysts.","graduateProfile":"Assignments, group and individual projects, cases and tests.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5759"},"AK1056":{"i":"AK1056","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Finance graduates will have advanced their knowledge and skills within the area of finance, and have advanced their personal and professional capabilities.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1056"},"OO0495":{"i":"OO0495","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have a wide range of opportunities in commercial and investment banks, brokerage and investment firms, insurance companies, treasury departments of non-financial corporations, regulatory agencies, consulting and accounting firms, and further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0495"},"AU5661":{"i":"AU5661","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree or attained an equivalent qualification or equivalent professional experience of an appropriate kind.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertSCM graduates will demonstrate a set of capabilities in areas of study related to supply chain management. They will be equipped to enter career pathways related to supply chain management within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5661"},"MY0361":{"i":"MY0361","entryRequirements":"Admission to the Master of Health Service Management requires that the candidate will: \n\n\n\r\n(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and will have \n\n\n\r\n(b) been awarded or qualified for a relevant Bachelor's degree, having achieved a grade average of at least a B- in the highest level courses, or equivalent; or \n\n\n\r\n(c) been awarded or qualified for a Postgraduate Diploma in Health Service Management with a B- grade average, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Health Service Management  (Professional Practice pathway) should be able to: \n\r\n - Apply management, leadership and informatics skills in Health Services Management practice \n\r\nEngage with and critically evaluate contemporary issues that challenge Health Services Management practice \n\r\nCommunicate effectively using a range of modalities with stakeholders in an organisation \n\r\nWork effectively in independent and team roles within an organisation \n\r\nEngage reflective practice with critical application of knowledge to organisational problem-solving \n\r\n - Graduates of the Master of Health Service Management (Research pathway) should be able to: \n\r\n - Apply management, leadership and informatics skills in Health Services Management practice \n\r\nEngage with and critically evaluate contemporary issues that challenge Health Services Management practice \n\r\nCommunicate effectively using a range of modalities with stakeholders in an organisation \n\r\nWork effectively in independent and team roles within an organisation \n\r\nCritically evaluate research and theory in an area of Health Services management and demonstrate an understanding of a research process.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0361"},"WI0933":{"i":"WI0933","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the skills and understanding required for effective management incorporating their particular chosen field of specialisation. They will have a well-grounded understanding of general management and a chosen discipline or specialisation that includes key concepts of the discipline, the analysis of case studies and the ability to engage with business and management in this area.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0933"},"LI7772":{"i":"LI7772","entryRequirements":"Qualify for the award of an undergraduate degree in New Zealand, with a B average or higher; be admitted with equivalent status (ad eundem statum).","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will have a coherent understanding of advanced investment analysis and portfolio management skills; be able to evaluate, apply and modify finance theory to finance sector, and communicate effectively.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7772"},"VI00Z8":{"i":"VI00Z8","strategicPurposeStatement":"Within their discipline, graduates will demonstrate a command of the published international scholarly research; have an expert understanding of the predominant research methods used in the published international scholarly research; and be able to design and implement a substantial piece of independent research. The MCom replaced the MCA degree (VI0034) in 2013.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Z8"},"AK3717":{"i":"AK3717","entryRequirements":"A Bachelors degree, or a graduate diploma, or a professional qualification in a relevant discipline, and relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be practising managers and professionals aspiring to future managerial careers. They will have received a general grounding in all functional business and management areas in order to develop knowledge, confidence and skills for emerging and middle level managers. They will be able to operate at a senior organisational level, providing overall leadership.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3717"},"MY0439":{"i":"MY0439","entryRequirements":"A bachelor degree with at least a B average in majoring papers at levels 6 and 7.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate competence in accountancy and finance such that they will be eligible to pursue membership of both domestic and international accountancy and finance professional bodies.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0439"},"AU0259":{"i":"AU0259","entryRequirements":"A relevant Masters degree and passed any prerequisite requirements for the intended subject with a minimum GPA, or have completed at least 30 points towards the Master of Commerce, and been recommended for admission by the Dean or nominee.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipCom graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills in business essential for them to be able to pursue personal professional goals and postgraduate study. The emphasis placed on integrating theory and practice will enhance problem solving and analytical skills developed at undergraduate level.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0259"},"CN0466":{"i":"CN0466","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the skills, knowledge and competencies to undertake entry-level Information Systems related roles within an organization, and a good foundation for developing further and moving into more advanced roles in IT management which contribute to the strategic development of organizations through technology both in New Zealand and internationally. They will have had the opportunity to apply knowledge gained to real work problems and situations to prove their skill in Information Systems/Information and Communications Technology-related areas and business competencies and to interact with external stakeholders in a professional manner and an industry relevant environment.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0466"},"LI0390":{"i":"LI0390","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree with appropriate grades.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced skills and knowledge in commerce subjects through postgraduate coursework and research.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0390"},"AK1020":{"i":"AK1020","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree or a graduate diploma or professional experience and relevant experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Business is designed for those students who wish to undertake a postgraduate programme of one to two years. Students may complete a Postgraduate Certificate qualification then take a break before continuing on to the Postgraduate Diploma programme at a later date. This may suit students who wish to try out a shorter postgraduate programme before they commit to completing the Master of Business.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1020"},"MY1078":{"i":"MY1078","entryRequirements":"Graduate Diploma in Emergency Management or Graduate Certificate in Emergency Management. Minimum Grade Point Average (5.0)(B average) required for entry.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an advanced understanding of natural hazards, disaster psychology, and emergency management.","graduateProfile":"Not provided","educationPathway":"Not provided","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1078"},"OO0527":{"i":"OO0527","entryRequirements":"It is not normally possible to enrol for the Postgraduate Certificate in Maori and Indigenous Business. Instead, it is available only as an exit qualification for students who withdraw, voluntarily or otherwise, from a programme of study for the degree of Master of Maori and Indigenous Business or for the Postgraduate Diploma in Maori and Indigenous Business.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have critical understanding and knowledge of core business concepts combined with, and enriched by, an understanding of Maori and Indigenous approaches both to business theory and business practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0527"},"OO0494":{"i":"OO0494","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have developed an advanced knowledge of business data science. They will understand how data analysis can be used in business, be able to identify opportunities to use data, be aware of ethical and privacy issues and possible mitigations, and be able to select appropriate means of presenting the results of analysis. They will also be able to select and apply techniques to manage large collections of data, and to analyse data.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0494"},"MY0363":{"i":"MY0363","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0363"},"CN0426":{"i":"CN0426","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or extensive practical, professional or scholarly experience of an appropriate kind.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this executive qualification will develop leadership skills, and the ability to become entrepreneurs and intrapreneurs who can operate in multi-functional roles in small to medium sized companies, with a strong corporate awareness and abilities in strategic management.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0426"},"AU4054":{"i":"AU4054","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree, and a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"MMgt graduates will demonstrate advanced level skill, knowledge and understanding in a critical mix of practical and theoretical areas of study related to their business specialisation and will be well equipped to become practitioners in their specialist fields.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4054"},"CN0627":{"i":"CN0627","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will: have in-depth knowledge and understanding of current theoretical concepts and frameworks within Financial Engineering, an ability to apply scientific principles and concepts to solve problems in this field, independently solve problems through the application of scientific knowledge and methods, be able to apply their in-depth knowledge of mathematics and finance to practical real-world problems, be able to think independently, demonstrate understanding from a multidisciplinary perspective and show an awareness of ethical issues.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0627"},"VI00M2":{"i":"VI00M2","entryRequirements":"New Zealand bachelor's degree and two years of relevant work experience or extensive practical, professional or scholarly experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an advanced understanding of public management relevant to employment in the public sector.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00M2"},"AU5642":{"i":"AU5642","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree or a professional qualification in a relevant subject.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertBusDev graduates will have attained a set of capabilities in areas of study related to the processes that underpin the growth and success of business. They will be equipped to enter career pathways related to business development within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5642"},"PC9123":{"i":"PC9123","entryRequirements":"A candidate for admission to this programme of study shall: \n\r\n(a) (i) hold an undergraduate (at least equivalent to New Zealand pass  \n\r\nstandard) or postgraduate degree awarded by a tertiary institution  \n\r\napproved by the Academic Board; or \n\r\n(ii) possess a qualification awarded by a recognised tertiary or  \n\r\nprofessional organisation as approved by the Academic Board as  \n\r\nbeing of an appropriate standard either for direct entry, or for entry  \n\r\nconditional upon satisfactory completion of a prescribed bridging  \n\r\nprogramme of study;  \n\r\nand \n\r\n(b) have completed a minimum of two years equivalent full-time relevant work  \n\r\nexperience as approved by the Academic Board;  \n\r\nand \n\r\n(c) have an English level equivalent to IELTS (Academic) 6.5 (with no band less  \n\r\nthan 6.0) / TOEFL iBT 79 (with a writing score of 21) / PToE academic score of  \n\r\n58 with no band lower than 50 / NZCEL (Level 5) / AIS Test of English  \n\r\nProficiency (TEP) 56/80 (with no band less than 13) (eligible students only); \n\r\nor \n\r\n(d) gain approval under Admission Regulation 1.3: Special Admission","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Business Administration provides graduates with applied skills in the core business disciplines at a managerial level. The programme combines theoretical and applied components in an environment that imitates real-world business settings, to enhance managerial competencies and enable overall personal growth.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will have a broad knowledge of a range of business subjects in the basic core. Increased managerial competencies gained will include research and investigation, problem solving, acting proactively, applying new ideas and thinking strategically; providing sound corporate values, professional skills and overall personal growth. Graduates will be expected \n\r\nto advance their careers in supervisory management roles.","educationPathway":"Graduates will be able to continue to further postgraduate studies in business and management.","developedBy":"Auckland Institute of Studies Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=PC9123"},"AK3411":{"i":"AK3411","entryRequirements":"Must have a bachelor's degree with a B- grade average or higher in courses at level 7, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of the MPA is to provide a pathway of postgraduate study which develops practical and theoretical knowledge, skills and expertise to produce literate and analytical accounting professionals. The emphasis will be on a programme of learning which covers all functional accounting and the research capability framework so as to develop knowledge, confidence and skills for aspiring accountants. Academic maturity gained from the completion of an undergraduate degree will enable students to make connections between research, theory and professional practice.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3411"},"CN0486":{"i":"CN0486","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Successful completion of this qualification will make graduates employment ready as effective digital marketers. They will be able to plan and carry out independent research, investigation and analysis.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including marked electronic quizzes, tests, assignments and projects.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0486"},"CN0494":{"i":"CN0494","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or extensive practical, professional or scholarly experience of an appropriate kind.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have focused on the core aspects of business administration. They may be able to transfer to the Master of Business Administration.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0494"},"AU5705":{"i":"AU5705","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or an approved alternative. Must meet entry requirements of each component degree. Selection criteria apply.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BAdvSci(Hons)/BC graduates will demonstrate knowledge and understanding of the content and application of elements of both Communication and Advanced Science disciplines.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5705"},"VI002P":{"i":"VI002P","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or an equivalent qualification, completed with a B- grade average or higher.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to secure marketing roles in medium to large organisations, both in New Zealand and overseas. They will understand complex situations in an environment of high uncertainty, and they will be able to provide solutions to marketing problems at a global strategic level. Graduates will have good oral and written communication skills and will be facilitators of change within organisations. Some graduates will be able, with appropriate further research preparation, to progress to a research-based master's degree or possibly a PhD.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002P"},"WI1015":{"i":"WI1015","entryRequirements":"Candidates for the Postgraduate Diploma would normally have qualified for the award of a Master of Professional Accounting","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Professional Accounting will enable graduates to complete the academic and professional requirements of the Chartered Accountants of Australia + New Zealand (CAANZ)","graduateProfile":"Examination or internal assessment","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1015"},"OO0065":{"i":"OO0065","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Commerce degree or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides advanced study plus an introduction to research in a chosen commerce subject. Recipients are capable of self-directed learning and intellectual independence, and can proceed to further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0065"},"VI004X":{"i":"VI004X","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree or Graduate Diploma with an average grade of B+ or better in the relevant subjects, with a major in Actuarial Science, Finance, Statistics or a related field.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MActSc graduates will be able to apply advanced actuarial techniques, including stochastic processes, generalized linear models, big data analysis and asset/liability modelling. They will have a professional-level knowledge of the Actuarial Control Cycle and corporate risk management strategies as well as additional advanced skills in finance and statistics. Graduates will be prepared to continue into a PhD programme in Actuarial Science. Graduates will be well prepared to take leadership roles in the actuarial or related fields.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004X"},"VI00V3":{"i":"VI00V3","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree in any discipline and the postgraduate English language requirements of the University.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an introductory knowledge of accounting which will assist them in clerical jobs in accounting or business. They may continue on to the Postgraduate Diploma in Professional Accounting (VI00V4) and the Master of Professional Accounting (VI00U8). The PGCertPA also acts as a stand-alone qualifications for students who choose to exit the PGDipPA or MPA programme.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00V3"},"OO0251":{"i":"OO0251","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Commerce degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will be able to: demonstrate advanced knowledge of their chosen business discipline; solve unstructured problems; undertake independent applied research; successfully interact with individuals and groups in a business context; and demonstrate an understanding of ethical issues in business.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0251"},"CN0476":{"i":"CN0476","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to: reflect critically on contemporary issues in accounting and finance, synthesize and analyze theory, research and practice in accounting and finance; undertake and communicate independent research related to accounting and finance.  They will have the knowledge and skills required to be a business analyst, investment analyst and cost//management accountant.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0476"},"CN0407":{"i":"CN0407","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"An MBus graduate will be able to: \n\r\n* demonstrate in-depth knowledge and understanding of current theoretical concepts, frameworks and industry practice within the broader fields of business and also within their chosen major;\n\r\n* think logically, analytically and critically with respect to the academic and professional literature within the fields of business and their chosen major; and\n\r\n* plan and carry out independent research and analysis that demonstrates critical awareness of academic and professional issues in the fields of business and their chosen major; and  \n\r\n* synthesise academic and professional literature and effectively communicate findings to a range of audiences in both written and oral formats; and  \n\r\n* demonstrate understanding of their major in the context of a bicultural Aotearoa New Zealand and multicultural world.   \n\r\nGraduates will be well suited to work in a range of roles including business analyst, management trainee, operations manager or specialist roles in areas such as human resource management, marketing or supply chain management. They will be able to work in a range of organisations.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0407"},"VI00M3":{"i":"VI00M3","entryRequirements":"New Zealand bachelor's degree and two years of relevant work experience or extensive practical, professional or scholarly experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained an enhanced understanding of management relevant to employment in the public sector.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00M3"},"MY0342":{"i":"MY0342","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree or equivalent. Professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have knowledge and skill on Logistics and Supply Chain Management to be able to apply a variety of techniques in a range of relevant situations at strategic level. They will be able to apply research skills in an ethical manner and effectively communicate the results at all levels in an organisation.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0342"},"VI004W":{"i":"VI004W","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with at least an average grade of B, and at least two years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertBus(Prof) provides a depth of specific applied business skill to knowledgeable, work experienced people who wish to upskill and will provide students with a technical toolkit in their chosen area of specialisation. Graduates will develop skills in one specific area of applied business knowledge to support a change of track and/or advancement in their career.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004W"},"WI1020":{"i":"WI1020","entryRequirements":"Candidates for the Postgraduate Certificate would normally have qualified for the award of a Bachelors Degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Management enables graduates from a wide range of disciplines to have a mastery of management concepts and applied research which they will be able to apply in their chosen occupation","graduateProfile":"Examination or internal assessment","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1020"},"MY0151":{"i":"MY0151","entryRequirements":"Undergraduate degree and postgraduate admission.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate scholarly achievement, or practical and professional experience, of an acceptable standard in an area or areas relevant to the qualification.       Graduates possess advanced knowledge, including a mastery of sophisticated abstract concepts, and can apply that knowledge in unfamiliar circumstances.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0151"},"MY0387":{"i":"MY0387","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate scholarly achievement, or practical and professional experience, of an acceptable standard in an area or areas relevant to the qualification. They can critically evaluate and summarise knowledge claims in their discipline and possess advanced knowledge, including a mastery of sophisticated abstract concepts, in a business discipline and can apply that knowledge in unfamiliar circumstances. Graduates can convey theories, propositions, research designs, results, and conclusions effectively in English using a variety of oral and written communication modes. They have knowledge of and can, with guidance, employ the principal research methods in their discipline and undertake supervised research in their discipline to internationally recognized standards.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0387"},"OO0485":{"i":"OO0485","entryRequirements":"An applicant must have held a degree for at least five years, and must normally be a graduate of the University of Otago.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have achieved recognition for publishing original contributions of special excellence in an area of commerce.","graduateProfile":"Not Provided","educationPathway":"Not Provided","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0485"},"MY0384":{"i":"MY0384","entryRequirements":"a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and  b) have been awarded or qualified for a relevant Bachelor's degree, or equivalent; and  c) have completed at least two years of relevant practical experience at management level;  d) have been selected into the programme on the basis of a selection process which may include a written application, interview and practical exercises.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate scholarly achievement, or practical and professional experience, of an acceptable standard in an area or areas relevant to the qualification.  They can critically evaluate and summarise knowledge claims in business administration.     Graduates can demonstrate professional knowledge, including a mastery of theory employed in business administration, and can integrate and apply that knowledge in a variety of organisational situations. They can effectively communicate analysis, synthesis, and recommendations orally and in writing.    Graduates display social and emotional intelligence in leadership, communication, interpersonal relationships and teamwork. They are able to undertake independent applied research directed at the enhancement of organisational performance.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0384"},"VI00Z5":{"i":"VI00Z5","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have sound analytical and research skills suitable for carrying out research at a Master's level, and will have consolidated and advanced the knowledge obtained in their undergraduate degree in one of a range of subjects in commerce. They may be able to enter at higher levels the jobs listed under the Bachelor of Commerce (VI00Z4), and may also find employment as auditors and tax consultants, business advisers, investigations officers, industrial relations consultants, systems consultants, strategic analysts, change management analysts, human resources advisors, product managers, market research and sales executives, investment researchers, financial advisors, sharebrokers, and advisory and parliamentary officers.  Graduates who achieve above-average performance will be able to continue to a Master of Commerce (VI00Z8).","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Z5"},"CN0304":{"i":"CN0304","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree plus a minimum of five years practical or professional work experience, preferably in a management position.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have in-depth knowledge of the tasks and skills required for effective, strategic leadership and the national and global context within which the role of the manager is located. They will understand the need for, and the practice of sustainable and responsible leadership and will be proficient at setting direction, building teams, engaging people and leading change in complex organisational environments. They will understand the personal foundations of strategic leadership, particularly those relating to emotional intelligence, spiritual intelligence, resilience and character. Graduates will have high levels of awareness of their capability as leaders, including a clear sense of direction and a comprehensive plan for their future learning and development.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0304"},"VI004Y":{"i":"VI004Y","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree or Graduate Diploma with an average grade of B+ or better in the relevant subjects, with a major in Actuarial Science, Finance, Statistics or a related field.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipActSc graduates will be able to apply advanced actuarial techniques, including stochastic processes, generalized linear models, big data analysis and asset/liability modelling. They will have a professional-level knowledge of the Actuarial Control Cycle and corporate risk management strategies. High performing graduates will be able to proceed to the Master of Actuarial Science. Graduates will be well prepared to take leadership roles in the actuarial field.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004Y"},"WI0852":{"i":"WI0852","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Business and Management prepares graduates from any discipline for entry to a career in management.  It provides a comprehensive training in the core areas required for effective management, develops an understanding of the business environment and builds the skills required for leadership or to be an entrepreneur. For many graduates it will be possible to select a position that requires management ability, but also draws on the knowledge and skills obtained in the undergraduate degree.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0852"},"CN0416":{"i":"CN0416","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained the skills, knowledge and competencies to be a highly effective contributing accountant to organisations both domestically and internationally. They will have the required qualifications to gain provisional membership into NZICA's College of Chartered Accountants and CPA Australia. They will be able to demonstrate knowledge and understanding of current theoretical concepts, frameworks and industry practice within the fields of accounting and business and will be able to think logically, analytically and critically with respect to the academic literature and professional journals within the field of accounting and business. They will be able to plan and carry out research that demonstrates critical awareness of academic and professional issues and will be able to synthesise academic and professional literature and effectively communicate this information and research findings both orally and in written form to a range of audiences.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0416"},"LI0720":{"i":"LI0720","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will gain the advanced skills and aptitudes required in tourism policy, planning and development and tourism management.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0720"},"AK1019":{"i":"AK1019","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent and relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipBA graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills in business essential for them to be able to pursue personal professional goals and further postgraduate study. The emphasis placed on integrating theory and practice will enhance problem solving and analytical skills developed at undergraduate level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1019"},"OO0501":{"i":"OO0501","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have advanced academic skills and research abilities within the discipline of accountancy.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0501"},"MY0436":{"i":"MY0436","entryRequirements":"Industry experience and a Postgraduate Diploma in Emergency Management. Minimum Grade Point Average (5.0)(B average) required for entry.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MEmergMgt graduates will have an advanced understanding of leadership in crisis environments, disaster psychology, decision-making and comprehensive emergency management or undertake significant supervised research in an emergency management topic.","graduateProfile":"Not provided","educationPathway":"Not provided","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0436"},"WI0943":{"i":"WI0943","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent, completed at a specified minimum level of attainment, management experience and academic aptitude and/or interviews.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma graduates will have the essential knowledge and skills in business required to contribute fully to decision making at management level in a Maori or other business context.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0943"},"MY0246":{"i":"MY0246","entryRequirements":"1. Admission to the Postgraduate Diploma in Agribusiness requires that the candidate will:    (a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and    (b) have been awarded or qualified for an agricultural or business-related Bachelor's degree, or equivalent; or    (c) have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelor's degree or equivalent and have completed at least three years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the PGDipAgribusiness will demonstrate the following attributes and skills:    Communicate effectively in various modes.  Apply advanced knowledge of agribusiness to effective solution of agribusiness issues.  Recognise and assess new agribusiness opportunities.  Identify cultural, ethical and regulatory issues in agribusiness, including the social and environmental effects of agribusiness decisions, and provide reasoned alternatives for their resolution.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0246"},"WI0963":{"i":"WI0963","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent, completed at a specified minimum level of attainment.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have the ability to use basic financial analysis and tools to develop lines of argument and make valuation, financing, investment management and banking decisions.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0963"},"OO0526":{"i":"OO0526","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in a relevant subject, two years' relevant management experience, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have critical understanding and knowledge of core business concepts combined with, and enriched by, an understanding of Maori and Indigenous approaches both to business theory and business practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0526"},"WI0942":{"i":"WI0942","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent, management experience, academic aptitude tests and/or interviews.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Certificate graduates will have knowledge and skills in Maori and Indigenous Business and have a platform from which they can either seek opportunities to further their studies in Business or perform generic non-specialist roles in Business.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0942"},"PC9688":{"i":"PC9688","entryRequirements":"A candidate for admission to this programme of study shall: i. have an English level equivalent to IELTS 6.5 (with no band less than 6.0) / TOEFL iBT 79 (with a writing score of 21) / PToE academic score, of 58 / AIS Test of English Proficiency (TEP) 56/80 (with no band less than 13); and ii. hold an undergraduate degree (at least equivalent to New Zealand pass standard) or a graduate diploma, bachelor honours degree, postgraduate diploma or postgraduate degree, awarded by a tertiary institution approved by the Academic Board; or possess a qualification awarded by a recognised tertiary or professional organisation as approved by the Academic Board as being of an appropriate standard either for direct entry, or for entry conditional upon satisfactory completion of a prescribed bridging programme of study; and iii. have completed a minimum of two years equivalent full-time relevant work experience as approved by the Academic Board; or hold an undergraduate degree (at least equivalent to New Zealand pass standard) or a graduate diploma, bachelor honours degree or postgraduate diploma in cognate discipline areas awarded by a tertiary institution approved by the Academic Board, reside in New Zealand, and include the module 4.798 in their programme of studies; or iv. gain approval under Admission Regulation 1.3: Special Admission.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Business Administration provides graduates with applied skills in the core business disciplines at a managerial level, and in-depth knowledge and applied skills in a chosen area of specialisation. The programme combines theoretical, applied and research components in an environment that imitates real-world business settings, to enhance managerial competencies and enable overall personal growth.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will have a broad knowledge of the range of business subjects in the basic core, and will have more in-depth knowledge and skills in subjects relevant to the specialisation of their choice. Increased managerial competencies gained will include research and investigation, problem solving, acting proactively, applying new ideas and thinking strategically;     \n\r\nproviding sound corporate values, professional skills and overall personal growth. Graduates will be expected to advance their careers in successively more senior management roles.","educationPathway":"Graduates will be able to continue to further postgraduate studies in business and management.","developedBy":"Auckland Institute of Studies Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=PC9688"},"VI00E3":{"i":"VI00E3","entryRequirements":"An appropriate Bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification, or extensive appropriate professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have developed a conceptual understanding and operational skills for use in the international world of deregulated and volatile financial markets.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00E3"},"OO0067":{"i":"OO0067","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's or other degree, or an acceptable professional qualification; plus acceptable experience in management or administration; plus a satisfactory result in the Graduate Management Admission Test.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the MBA programme will have the skills required to successfully lead teams and businesses in a globalised business environment.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0067"},"AU5514":{"i":"AU5514","entryRequirements":"A four year bachelor's or honours degree or a three year bachelor's degree and a postgraduate diploma or relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Postgraduate Certificate in Commercialisation and Entrepreneurship will have the core knowledge and skills essential to moving scientific and technological research and innovation from the lab to the market place through commercialisation processes and understand what is required to build a successful entrepreneurial venture.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5514"},"AU4060":{"i":"AU4060","entryRequirements":"All requirements for BProp with a B grade or better average in Part III.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BProp(Hons) graduates will have undertaken advanced studies in key concepts and theories underpinning property processes. They will be critical, reflective practitioners able to pursue personal professional goals and will have demonstrated capacity to undertake postgraduate studies.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4060"},"OO0419":{"i":"OO0419","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree or other acceptable qualification; or equivalent experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This certificate provides training in business administration and management.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0419"},"MY0403":{"i":"MY0403","entryRequirements":"(a) meet the University admission requirements as specified;  (b) have been awarded or qualified for a relevant Bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification, having achieved a grade average of at least a B- in the highest level papers.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate scholarly achievement, or practical and professional experience, of an acceptable standard in an area or areas relevant to the qualification.   They can critically evaluate and summarise knowledge claims in their discipline.     Graduates possess advanced knowledge, including a mastery of sophisticated abstract concepts, in a business discipline and can work independently and apply knowledge to new situations.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0403"},"VI0042":{"i":"VI0042","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree. Five years of relevant work experience strongly recommended.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates enter as experienced managers and are provided with a solid foundation in management and related subject areas, effective interpersonal skills, strategic vision and leadership and an international perspective.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI0042"},"WI0140":{"i":"WI0140","entryRequirements":"Entry by invitation based on results of second and third years of Bachelor of Management Studies","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an understanding of a broad range of management theories and competency in developing, evaluating and critiquing management presentations and reports. They will be able to engage in management activities in both structured and unstructured environments and to self manage, co-manage and accept directed management tasks.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0140"},"MY0231":{"i":"MY0231","entryRequirements":"A Bachelors degree with a major in Supply Chain Management or equivalent, with a minimum B- average over the qualifying 300-level courses, and have completed at least two years of relevant professional experience; or a Graduate Diploma in Logistics and Supply Chain Management or equivalent qualification with a minimum B- average, ; or demonstrated at least five years relevant professional experience, including completion of appropriate professional qualifications or equivalent via a portfolio and an interview at the discretion of the University.","strategicPurposeStatement":"A graduate of the PGDip in Supply Chain Management will demonstrate the following attributes and skills:    Critical Analysis - Take a reflective, evaluative approach to critically analyse a problem context, current norms, methodologies and potential solutions.  Systems Thinking - Take a holistic approach to framing problems, evaluate interface trade-offs and consider cause and effects throughout an entire system.  Analytical Modelling - Demonstrate numerical proficiency in scenario modelling. Demonstrate competency in a range of financial and operational analytical techniques to maximise value provision.  Commercial Context - Apply best practice techniques and skills to commercial problems.  Life-Long Learning - Continually develop intellectual skills and knowledge through experience and life-long learning.  Communication - Use effective communication skills to convincingly facilitate understanding and improvement in a range of organisational, technical and social contexts.  Teamwork - Develop a collaborative approach when working with a range of stakeholders and team members in order to build consensus and find acceptable compromises.  Logical Arguments - Construct logical arguments based on sound reasoning to solve organisational problems.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0231"},"OO0522":{"i":"OO0522","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent. No applicant will be admitted who has previously been awarded an Honours degree or Postgraduate Diploma in Marketing.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have an extensive knowledge of marketing theory and practice, and the ability to integrate this knowledge to address applied and academic research.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0522"},"VI00N3":{"i":"VI00N3","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates enter as experienced managers and are provided with a solid foundation in management and related subject areas, effective interpersonal skills, strategic vision and leadership and an international perspective.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00N3"},"AK1079":{"i":"AK1079","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent. Relevant professional experience approved as equivalent to a bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgCertDTL graduates will have foundational knowledge and skills in digital transformation, enabling them to understand and support digital change activities. They will have demonstrated analytical skills in relation to digital concepts. Graduates are prepared for further postgraduate study, specifically for entry into the Postgraduate Diploma or Master of Digital Transformation Leadership. Graduates will apply their understanding to contribute more effectively within digitally changing work environments and support transformation efforts at a foundational level.","graduateProfile":"Reports, projects, reflective journals/portfolios, case studies, proposals, presentations.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1079"},"AU5660":{"i":"AU5660","entryRequirements":"This is an exit qualification:  In order to be admitted to this diploma a student must have:  been enrolled in the Degree of Master of Supply Chain Management and passed at least 30 points for that qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipSCM graduates will be able to demonstrate advanced knowledge in business and supply chain management and apply this effectively in a range of contexts. They will be equipped to progress careers in supply chain management within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5660"},"WI0941":{"i":"WI0941","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent, completed at a specified minimum level of attainment, at least 3 years management experience and academic aptitude and/or interviews.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Maori and Indigenous Business is a post-experience Masters programme. It will equip Maori and those involved in Maori and Indigenous business for senior leadership roles.  Master of Maori and Indigenous Business graduates will demonstrate advanced level skill, knowledge and understanding in a critical mix of practical and theoretical areas of study related to Maori and Indigenous business and will be well equipped to occupy positions of significant responsibility within local and global business. Graduates will contribute to the burgeoning Maori economy and be able to stimulate local, national and international business growth.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0941"},"VI002O":{"i":"VI002O","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification, completed with a B- grade average or higher.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to secure management roles in medium to large organisations, both in New Zealand and overseas. They will understand complex situations in an environment of high uncertainty, and they will be able to provide solutions to management problems at a global strategic level. Graduates will have good written and oral communication skills and will be facilitators of change within organisations. Some graduates will be able, with appropriate further research preparation, to progress to a research-based master's degree or possibly a PhD.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002O"},"VI00Z7":{"i":"VI00Z7","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Commerce (or Bachelor of Commerce and Administration), or another approved degree; or demonstrated ability or professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have developed sound analytical and research skills, and consolidated and advanced the knowledge obtained in their undergraduate degree to a postgraduate level in one of a range of subjects in commerce, to a greater degree than in the Graduate Certificate in Commerce (VI00V6). They will be able to advance their career in their chosen speciality or progress to the Master of Commerce (VI00Z8), if they achieve above-average performance and include the required research preparation courses.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Z7"},"MY0149":{"i":"MY0149","entryRequirements":"Undergrad, degree, ad eundem and experience in banking.","strategicPurposeStatement":"For students who whish to keep up with developments in their professional field of banking.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0149"},"CN0456":{"i":"CN0456","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate in-depth knowledge and understanding of current theoretical concepts and frameworks within finance and economics. They will be able to think logically, analytically and critically wtih respect to the academic literature in finance and economics and explain how this literature applies to real work problems. They will be able to synthesise academic or professional literature effectively and communicate the results of their independent study orally and in written form. They will be able to apply their in-depth knowledge of finance and economics to practical real world problems.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0456"},"AK3747":{"i":"AK3747","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipIHM graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills in international hospitality management essential for them to be able to pursue personal professional goals and further postgraduate study. The emphasis placed on integrating theory and practice will enhance problem solving and analytical skills developed at undergraduate level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3747"},"OO0242":{"i":"OO0242","entryRequirements":"A three-year bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have a detailed and high-level critical understanding of tourism as both an industry and a social phenomenon. They will be aware of how tourism is situated in a broad social, environmental, and economic context. Graduates will demonstrate a strong commitment to independent and lifelong learning that is grounded in critical thinking. Their research and presentation skills will enable them to actively participate in the tourism industry, associated governmental and non-governmental institutions, and or academia.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0242"},"CN0406":{"i":"CN0406","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree including specified prerequisites.","strategicPurposeStatement":"A postgraduate course which refines and augments undergraduate knowledge in business and economics. The thesis component strengthens research skills and creates valuable new research for industrial and educational purposes. Students can continue to the Doctorate of Philosophy programme.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0406"},"CN0425":{"i":"CN0425","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Successful completion of this programme will make graduates employment ready as effective digital marketers.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessment will be used including marked electronic quizzes, tests, assignments and projects.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0425"},"AK1095":{"i":"AK1095","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with a B grade average in courses at level 7, or equivalent and at least three years of relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MHPL graduates will have advanced knowledge of ethical leadership, coaching, and performance science, with the ability to integrate psychological, physiological, relational, and cultural principles to enhance human performance in complex applied settings. They will be culturally fluent leaders who engage respectfully with Maori and Indigenous frameworks and who apply insights from human performance technologies, analytics, and artificial intelligence to make data informed decisions and support behavioural change. Graduates will be prepared for advanced roles such as performance lead, coaching director, human performance strategist, or leadership advisor in sport, defence, emergency services, and other high-performance domains.?","graduateProfile":"Video-based tasks, scenario-based analysis, reflective journals, and applied problem-solving activities, project.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1095"},"AK3742":{"i":"AK3742","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgCertBus graduates will have specialist skills in a chosen field of business essential to perform at a high professional level. They will be able to apply contemporary theory to current practice and have demonstrated analytical and problem solving skills and be prepared for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3742"},"AU5763":{"i":"AU5763","entryRequirements":"Completed a relevant Bachelors or Bachelors Honours degree with a minimum GPA and MATHS 108 or STATS 108 or equivalent, or a relevant Bachelors degree and 90 points in the Postgraduate Diploma in Applied Finance or 60 points in the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Finance, or the Postgraduate Diploma in Administration or Business Management with a minimum GPA and 15 relevant course points and completed 15 points from BUSADMIN 763, BUSMAN 707, MATHS 108, STATS 108, or the equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MAppFin graduates will demonstrate advanced capabilities in a critical mix of theoretical and applied areas of study related to finance and will be equipped to progress careers as financial analysts, treasury analysts and financial consultants within local and global business.","graduateProfile":"Assignments, group and individual projects, cases and tests.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5763"},"OO0559":{"i":"OO0559","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree with a minimum average grade of B","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the programme will be equipped with an understanding of the nature of business through advanced knowledge in at least one major subject area; and the ability to integrate and use their knowledge to make informed business decisions.","graduateProfile":"Internal assessment, examinations.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0559"},"AU5563":{"i":"AU5563","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a Bachelors degree, or equivalent qualification and two year's management experience relevant to the degree;   Further information is available from www.auckland.ac.nz","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate advanced level skill, knowledge and understanding in a critical mix of practical and theoretical areas of study related to Maori and Indigenous business and will be well equipped to occupy positions of significant responsibility within local and global business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5563"},"MY0179":{"i":"MY0179","entryRequirements":"a) meet the University admission requirements as specified, and:  b) have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelor's degree or equivalent, and:  c) be working in the health and/or disability sectors.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders will have advanced knowledge and skills in the area of health service management.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0179"},"VI00D8":{"i":"VI00D8","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or Certificate in Management Studies; three years of relevant work experience; and acceptance by the Programme Director as capable of proceeding with the proposed course of study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained a broad-based management education programme, focusing on human resource management.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00D8"},"CN1416":{"i":"CN1416","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be employment ready for accounting roles.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including electronic quizzes, tests, assignments and projects.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN1416"},"AU5632":{"i":"AU5632","entryRequirements":"Completed the requirements for a relevant Bachelors degree, Bachelor (Honours) degree or  the Postgradute Diploma in Business Administration  with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA) and  passed any specified prerequisite courses.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to participate competitively anywhere in the world. They will have skills and knowledge in business and supply chain management that will enable them to continue developing personally and professionally in careers in supply chain management.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5632"},"MY0385":{"i":"MY0385","entryRequirements":"Relevant Bachelors degree with B- GPA in the highest level courses, or equivalent and at least three years of relevant postgraduate practical experience and a selection process applies.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MBA graduates will have the strategic thinking, leadership skills and cultural competence to enhance their organisations, emphasising integrity and responsibility.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0385"},"CN0447":{"i":"CN0447","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will possess the knowledge and skills to select and apply relevant business management theories and frameworks, critically analyse outcomes, and effectively communicate findings through written reports and presentations","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including assignments, group projects, presentations, self-directed online modules, tests and exams.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0447"},"AK1300":{"i":"AK1300","entryRequirements":"A four-year bachelor's degree or a three-year bachelor's degree and one year of advanced study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MArtsMgmt graduates will have advanced knowledge and understanding of the cultural and creative industry sectors. They will have management and research skills in business strategy, entrepreneurship, and creative practice within the context of the creative and cultural industries. They will be prepared for careers as arts managers, writers, curators, directors and project managers within the cultural and creative industry sector.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1300"},"LIO592":{"i":"LIO592","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will gain advanced skills and knowledge in an area of commerce including: accounting, agribusiness, business management, computing, economics, finance, farm management, hotel and institutional management, human resource management, marketing, property valuation.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LIO592"},"PC9797":{"i":"PC9797","entryRequirements":"A candidate for admission to this programme of study shall: i. have an English level equivalent to IELTS 6.5 (with no band less than 6.0) / TOEFL iBT 79 (with a writing score of 21) / PToE academic score of 58 / AIS Test of English Proficiency (TEP) 56/80 (with no band less than 13); and ii. hold an undergraduate degree (at least equivalent to New Zealand pass standard) or a graduate diploma, bachelor honours degree, postgraduate diploma or postgraduate degree, awarded by a tertiary institution approved by the Academic Board; or possess a qualification awarded by a recognised tertiary or professional organisation as approved by the Academic Board as being of an appropriate standard either for direct entry, or for entry conditional upon satisfactory completion of a prescribed bridging programme of study; and iii. have completed a minimum of two years equivalent full-time relevant work experience as approved by the Academic Board; or hold an undergraduate degree (at least equivalent to New Zealand pass standard","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Business Administration provides graduates with applied skills in the core business disciplines at a managerial level. The programme combines theoretical and applied components in an environment that imitates real-world business settings, to enhance managerial competencies and enable overall personal growth.","graduateProfile":"Graduates will have broad knowledge of a range of business subjects with a basic core and may extend this broad range or specialise in their choice of electives. Managerial competencies gained will include problem solving, acting proactively, applying new ideas and thinking strategically; providing sound corporate values, professional skills and overall personal growth.","educationPathway":"-Graduates will be able to continue to master's level study in the field of business.","developedBy":"Auckland Institute of Studies Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=PC9797"},"MY0174":{"i":"MY0174","entryRequirements":"1. been awarded or qualified for an undergraduate degree and have at least two years of relevant industry or professional experience, or equivalent; or  \n\r\n2. been awarded or qualified for the GradCertEmergMgt having achieved at least a B grade average, or equivalent; or \n\r\n3. been awarded or qualified for a GradDipEmergMgt having achieved at least a B grade average, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Massey University Postgraduate Certificate in Emergency Management will have knowledge of core subjects, including evaluation research practices and contemporary and holistic risk based emergency management concepts to enhance reduction, readiness, response and recovery practice.\n\n\n\r\nPersonal capabilities  \n\r\n* Consider historical emergency management contexts, while engaging with current emergency management issues at community, individual, local and global levels.  \n\r\n* Critically evaluate research and scholarly material while competently applying it to solutions in emergency management settings.   Personal capabilities  \n\r\n* Demonstrate initiative, self-discipline, and an ability to plan, reflect on, and achieve personal and professional goals.   \n\r\n* Ability to interpret and evaluate research in emergency management.  \n\r\n* Apply critical analysis skills at a suitable level.   \n\n\n\r\nDiscipline specific competencies  \n\r\n* Consider historical emergency management contexts, while engaging with current emergency management issues at community, individual, local and global levels.  \n\r\n* Understand the theory of risk, readiness, reduction, response and recovery as it applies to comprehensive emergency management.   \n\r\n* Critically evaluate research and scholarly material while competently applying it to emergency management settings.   Professional attributes  \n\r\n* Value ongoing professional development in the area of emergency management.  \n\r\n* Demonstrate practiced computer technology skills and value the importance of digital technologies within the emergency management field.   \n\n\n\r\nEthical and social attributes  \n\r\n* Value diversity and act ethically with a range of individuals, groups, cultures and ethnicities.  \n\r\n* Communicate effectively in a variety of forums to specialist and non-specialist audiences.  \n\r\n* Interact within a research environment with integrity and in an ethical and professional manner.","graduateProfile":"Graduates of the Massey University Postgraduate Certificate in Emergency Management will have knowledge of core subjects, including evaluation research practices and contemporary and holistic risk based emergency management concepts to enhance reduction, readiness, response and recovery practice.\n\n\n\r\nPersonal capabilities  \n\r\n* Consider historical emergency management contexts, while engaging with current emergency management issues at community, individual, local and global levels.  \n\r\n* Critically evaluate research and scholarly material while competently applying it to solutions in emergency management settings.   Personal capabilities  \n\r\n* Demonstrate initiative, self-discipline, and an ability to plan, reflect on, and achieve personal and professional goals.   \n\r\n* Ability to interpret and evaluate research in emergency management.  \n\r\n* Apply critical analysis skills at a suitable level.   \n\n\n\r\nDiscipline specific competencies  \n\r\n* Consider historical emergency management contexts, while engaging with current emergency management issues at community, individual, local and global levels.  \n\r\n* Understand the theory of risk, readiness, reduction, response and recovery as it applies to comprehensive emergency management.   \n\r\n* Critically evaluate research and scholarly material while competently applying it to emergency management settings.   Professional attributes  \n\r\n* Value ongoing professional development in the area of emergency management.  \n\r\n* Demonstrate practiced computer technology skills and value the importance of digital technologies within the emergency management field.   \n\n\n\r\nEthical and social attributes  \n\r\n* Value diversity and act ethically with a range of individuals, groups, cultures and ethnicities.  \n\r\n* Communicate effectively in a variety of forums to specialist and non-specialist audiences.  \n\r\n* Interact within a research environment with integrity and in an ethical and professional manner.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0174"},"VI00H9":{"i":"VI00H9","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Tourism Management or Bachelor of Tourism  Management with Honours or similar degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a high level of understanding of the complex phenomenon of tourism, and be able to demonstrate critical thinking, analytical skills and research expertise.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00H9"},"LI7770":{"i":"LI7770","entryRequirements":"An undergraduate qualification in a relevant field achieved at an above average level, usually a B or better.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an advanced understanding of the key aspects of commercial activity and value creation, and a mastery of analytic techniques within the field of Global Management and Marketing, to enable them to move seamlessly from study to career.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7770"},"MY0348":{"i":"MY0348","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced theoretical and practical knowledge and skills in the areas of quality control, assurance, management and strategy. They will be able to synthesise a variety of analytical tools in analysing their business, to continuously improve industrial processes and systems to achieve sustainable ongoing improvement in manufacturing or service delivery capability with a goal of six sigma capability. They will have a critical understanding of systems thinking and its application to organisational quality and its management. Graduates will be able to communicate effectively, work independently and in teams, be able to learn effectively and seek appropriate information to further their knowledge and solve organisational problems. They will be able to undertake self directed, advanced research utilising appropriate information sources.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0348"},"CN0446":{"i":"CN0446","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to demonstrate in-depth knowledge and understanding of current theoretical concepts, frameworks and industry practice within the fields of business and management. They will be able to think logically, analytically and critically with respect to the academic and professional literature within the fields of business and management. They will have the skills, knowledge and competencies to engage and actively participate in business and commerce. They will be able to challenge existing practice and position themselves as the future leaders in business.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0446"},"OO0549":{"i":"OO0549","entryRequirements":"Qualification proposed as exit award only and students will not normally be able to enrol.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will demonstrate skills in the definition, management and communication of applied research in their chosen area of business.","graduateProfile":"x","educationPathway":"x","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0549"},"AK1058":{"i":"AK1058","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree completed to a merit standard.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MIHM graduates will be prepared to assume or enhance management roles within the global hospitality industry. They will demonstrate advanced knowledge and skills in the field of international hospitality management, be able to undertake research, and have presented the results by way of an applied project, dissertation or thesis. Those who graduate may apply for further study at doctoral level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1058"},"VI004I":{"i":"VI004I","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification, completed with a B grade average or higher, and 5 years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Enables graduates to step up into a position in senior management with an executive qualification that strengthens their analytical rigour and strategic acumen.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004I"},"WI0909":{"i":"WI0909","entryRequirements":"Completion of a bachelors degree in a relevant field or equivalent. Those students who have an honours degree in a relevant field, may take 120 credits to complete the MPM.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Professional Management provides the skills, knowledge and abilities that will enable graduates to advance professional practice in their field. In each of the fields in which it is offered this degree provides a specialised programme that includes core competencies and skills, advanced research-led knowledge relevant to professional practice, professional experience and the ability to undertake applied research.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0909"},"VI00K8":{"i":"VI00K8","entryRequirements":"A degree of Victoria University of Wellington, or a degree of another university, gained at least 5 years prior to candidacy for the DCom.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of the degree have been recognised for major achievements in a field of commerce.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00K8"},"WI0842":{"i":"WI0842","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent. Entry to the honours programme is by invitation based on results of second and third years of Bachelor of Management Studies","strategicPurposeStatement":"This conjoint degree gives students the opportunity to complete the requirements of two Bachelors degrees over a reduced period of time. Graduates will have knowledge and skills from both management and social sciences disciplines which gives them a good grounding for careers in many areas. The BMS will be awarded with honours only where the students grades in the final year justify the award.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0842"},"AU5531":{"i":"AU5531","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Professional Accounting graduates will have an advanced set of skills and knowledge in business, accounting, finance, commercial law and taxation and have the ability to undertake any additional professional study and practical work experience required to become recognised as a chartered accountant/chartered professional accountant.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5531"},"CN0474":{"i":"CN0474","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of the postgraduate diploma will have the skills, knowledge and competencies to undertake entry-level Information Systems related roles within an organisation, and a good foundation for developing further and moving into more advanced roles in IT management which contribute to the strategic development of organisations through technology both in New Zealand and internationally.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0474"},"OO0516":{"i":"OO0516","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's honours degree, a postgraduate diploma or a master's degree in a business discipline, or an acceptable equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have achieved recognition for publishing original contributions of special excellence in an area of business.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0516"},"OO0480":{"i":"OO0480","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The PGCertTechEntr provides a practically-focused introduction to technology businesses, innovation and commercialisation. It fosters the knowledge, skills and behaviours needed to be a successful entrepreneur in the technology industry","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0480"},"OO0066":{"i":"OO0066","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's or other degree requiring 4 years of study; or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree involves supervised research in a chosen commerce subject. Graduates will have advanced knowledge in the field, and the ability to study independently and to carry out original research to internationally recognised standards.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0066"},"VI00V4":{"i":"VI00V4","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree in any discipline and the postgraduate English language requirements of the University.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a solid foundation in professional accounting and may apply their knowledge to jobs in the commercial, government or not-for-profit sectors. They may continue to the Master of Professional Accounting. The PGDipPA also acts as a stand-alone qualification for students who choose to exit the MPA programme.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00V4"},"WI0803":{"i":"WI0803","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Tourism or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an informed knowledge of the aspects of one of the streams in the degree coupled with the  acquisition of research and related skills that enable independent critical analysis and commentary and enhance professional practice.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0803"},"WI1009":{"i":"WI1009","entryRequirements":"Candidates for the Postgraduate Certificate would normally have qualified for the award of a Master of Professional Accounting","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Certificate in Professional Accounting will enable graduates to complete the academic and professional requirements of the Chartered Accountants of Australia + New Zealand (CAANZ)","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1009"},"OO0064":{"i":"OO0064","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Commerce degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study; or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree programme provides in-depth knowledge, plus an introduction to research, in a chosen commerce subject or subjects. Graduates are able to pursue personal professional goals and further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0064"},"WI0135":{"i":"WI0135","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This conjoint degree gives students the opportunity to complete the requirements of two Bachelors degrees over a reduced period of time. Graduates will have knowledge and skills from both law and management disciplines which gives them a good grounding for careers in many areas.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0135"},"AK1060":{"i":"AK1060","entryRequirements":"The Bachelor of Business or the Graduate Diploma in Business, with level 7 papers in the selected subject area for this degree having a B grade average or higher.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MBus graduates will have advanced knowledge and understanding in their chosen field of business. They will be critical and reflective, with strong applied research capability. They will have demonstrated the ability to engage in a sustained period of research, and may progress to further study at doctoral level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1060"},"AU5129":{"i":"AU5129","entryRequirements":"A relevant degree, or a relevant professional qualification and at least two years of relevant work experience, or five years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertBus graduates will understand the importance of information for patient-centred care and will have developed the information management and technology skills needed to enhance the planning, quality and accessibility of New Zealand healthcare","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5129"},"CN0435":{"i":"CN0435","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree plus five years professional project management experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to apply core project management principles, tools, and techniques to the planning and delivery of projects within defined parameters. They will demonstrate a solid understanding of foundational project management processes, including project initiation, stakeholder engagement, scheduling, team leadership, and project closeout. Graduates will be capable of managing small to medium-sized projects, working both independently and collaboratively, while upholding ethical standards. They will demonstrate foundational bicultural competence in Aotearoa New Zealand, with awareness of te ao Maori and Te Tiriti o Waitangi, and will communicate clearly and appropriately for a range of project contexts.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including individual tests and examinations, individual and group essays, assignments and reports, individual journals, incorporating reflective practices, group and individual presentations, literature reviews and project monitoring and evaluation (progress) reports.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0435"},"AU5513":{"i":"AU5513","entryRequirements":"A four-year bachelor's or honours degree or a three-year bachelor's degree and a postgraduate diploma or relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Commercialisation and Entrepreneurship programme will have both the core knowledge and skills essential to moving scientific and technological research and innovation from the lab to the market place through commercialisation processes and understand what is required to build a successful entrepreneurial venture. They also will have deepened and broadened their understanding, practical knowledge and skills through additional coursework or through practical hands-on experience by completing a serious commercialisation project.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5513"},"LI0285":{"i":"LI0285","entryRequirements":"An appropriate bachelors degree plus at least two years relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained advanced-level executive management training and development with an industry-specific focus.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0285"},"LI0248":{"i":"LI0248","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will gain advanced skills and knowledge in an area of commerce including: accounting, agribusiness, business management, computing, economics, finance, farm management, hotel and institutional management, human resource management, marketing, property valuation.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0248"},"AK1055":{"i":"AK1055","strategicPurposeStatement":"The main goal of the Master of Applied Finance is to develop the knowledge, understanding and skills of non-finance graduates in order to prepare them for professional roles in the financial services sector. By adding value and building capabilities on top of a prior undergraduate degree, the Master of Applied Finance degree will enhance these graduates' career opportunities and employment prospects.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1055"},"AU5663":{"i":"AU5663","entryRequirements":"This is an Exit qualification; a student must have been enrolled in the Degree of Master of Business Management and  passed at least 30 points for that qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipBusDev graduates will have attained a set of advanced capabilities in a mix of practical and theoretical areas of study related to their area of specialisation in business and management and demonstrate a strong set of professional competencies. They will be equipped to progress careers in business management within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5663"},"WI0053":{"i":"WI0053","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a detailed and advanced knowledge of a specialised subject area within management studies.  They will have the opportunity to develop critical thinking skills, oral and communications skills, self-directed learning skills and more specific skills relevant to their subject area.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0053"},"VI00B4":{"i":"VI00B4","entryRequirements":"New Zealand Bachelor's degree and two years' relevant work experience or extensive practical, professional or scholarly experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will enhance their understanding of the theory and practice of public management and their performance as a manager, and develop ways of improving practice in their organisations.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00B4"},"AK1072":{"i":"AK1072","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgCertITM graduates will have an advanced knowledge and understanding of tourism. They will demonstrate critical thinking, in depth analytical skills and intellectual independence. The programme will extend graduates' professional skills and prepare them for further study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1072"},"AK1070":{"i":"AK1070","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The main goal of the Postgraduate Certificate in Business Studies is to provide a sound foundation in business studies at Level 8 from a range of subjects including finance, international business, marketing, accounting, business statistics, management and economics.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1070"},"LI0336":{"i":"LI0336","entryRequirements":"Entry to the programme will be limited to students with a prior undergraduate qualification in a related discipline. Students will be expected to have achieved at least a 'B' average in the final year of their undergraduate qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will have a broad understanding of the tourism system. They will be able to focus on particular areas of interest, taking advantage of the interdisciplinary nature of Lincoln University. Graduates will have a deep understanding of tourism processes, their application and their implications. Master of Tourism Management graduates will be able to create new knowledge, critically evaluate information and communicate effectively. They will have quantitative or qualitative analytic skills, or both, that will allow them to solve a range of both theoretical and practical problems. Graduates will have acquired the ability to work both independently and within groups, and, be able to analyse data appropriately. They will also appreciate the benefits of commitments to professional standards and be familiar with gender, ethnicity, equity and environmental issues.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0336"},"LI7761":{"i":"LI7761","entryRequirements":"Qualify for the award of a bachelor's degree in New Zealand, with a B average or higher; and meet the requirements of CPA Australia for eligibility for admission to the CPA Program.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the Master of Professional Accounting (CPA) will have a coherent understanding of accounting, operational and strategic issues; apply strategic thinking and business leadership in an ethical and professional manner; identify and critically analyse accounting issues and their implications on business activities and the accounting professions; sound communication, negotiation and people management skills.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7761"},"MY1062":{"i":"MY1062","entryRequirements":"a) meet the University admission requirements as specified, and:  b) have been awarded or qualified for a Bachelor's degree having achieved at least a B- grade average in the highest level papers, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate scholarly achievement, or practical and professional experience, of an acceptable standard in an area or areas relevant to the qualification.    Graduates possess advanced knowledge in a business discipline and can apply that knowledge in unfamiliar circumstances.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY1062"},"AK3712":{"i":"AK3712","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree completed to a merit standard.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BBus(Hons) graduates will have a broad range of research skills together with sound analytical thinking skills which will enable them to critically evaluate and apply relevant literature and research in their arts discipline. They will be prepared for further postgraduate study at master's or doctoral level.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3712"},"OO0551":{"i":"OO0551","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree majoring in Accounting with a second major or minor in Finance (having achieved an average grade of B+ in the papers satisfying the final-year major subject requirements for the degree). Or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will be equipped with advanced industry knowledge and skills relevant to accountancy and financial management.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0551"},"WI0817":{"i":"WI0817","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Business Analysis or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have developed knowledge of the research literature in accounting, economics or finance, and its application. They will have rigorous and advanced analytical and research skills and demonstrate ability in the presentation of research results. This qualification may also be taken as the first stage of a programme leading to a masters degree in accounting, economics, or finance.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0817"},"AK3611":{"i":"AK3611","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"The purpose of the MPA is to provide a pathway of postgraduate study which develops practical and theoretical knowledge, skills and expertise to produce literate and analytical accounting professionals. The emphasis will be on a programme of learning which covers all functional accounting and the research capability framework so as to develop knowledge, confidence and skills for aspiring accountants. Academic maturity gained from the completion of an undergraduate degree will enable students to make connections between research, theory and professional practice.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3611"},"LI0350":{"i":"LI0350","entryRequirements":"An appropriate bachelors degree plus at least two years' relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced level executive management training and development with a focus on property studies.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0350"},"AU5529":{"i":"AU5529","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA).","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Management graduates will have the essential core knowledge and skills in business required to enter a first-level position in their specialist field.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5529"},"AK3741":{"i":"AK3741","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipBus graduates will have an advanced knowledge and understanding of business. They will demonstrate critical thinking, in depth analytical skills and intellectual independence. The programme will extend graduates' professional skills and prepare them for further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3741"},"VI004J":{"i":"VI004J","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification and 5 years of relevant work experience","strategicPurposeStatement":"Enables graduates to step up into a position in senior management with an executive qualification that strengthens their analytical rigour and strategic acumen.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004J"},"AK3711":{"i":"AK3711","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of the PgDipPA will have integrated a range of accounting and business skills while undertaking advanced level study and research in accounting, which will have provided them with an awareness of the context in which financial and management accounting reports are prepared. They may progress to the Master of Professional Accounting degree.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3711"},"AK3811":{"i":"AK3811","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Holders of the PgCertPA will have a foundation for advanced-level study in accounting and the necessary grounding to interpret financial and management accounting reports.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK3811"},"OO0550":{"i":"OO0550","entryRequirements":"Qualification proposed as exit award only and students will not normally be able to enrol.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will demonstrate highly developed skills in the definition, management and communication of applied research in their chosen area of business.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0550"},"VI004V":{"i":"VI004V","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with at least an average grade of B, and at least two years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipBus(Prof) provides a depth of specific applied business skill to knowledgeable, work experienced people who wish to upskill and will provide students with a technical toolkit in their chosen area of specialisation. Graduates will integrate a grounding in business studies knowledge with skills and expertise in one specialist area to support a change of track and/or advancement in their career.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004V"},"VI00Z6":{"i":"VI00Z6","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Commerce (or Bachelor of Commerce and Administration), or another approved degree; or demonstrated ability or professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have developed sound analytical skills, and consolidated and advanced the knowledge obtained in their undergraduate degree to a postgraduate level in one of a range of subjects in commerce. They will be able to advance their career in their chosen speciality or progress to further study in the Postgraduate Diploma of Commerce (VI00Z7).","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00Z6"},"WI0250":{"i":"WI0250","entryRequirements":"Bachelors degree, or Bachelor of Management Studies with Honours with second class honours, or Postgraduate Diploma in Management Studies, and relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates have the personal and business skills required for effective management and leadership. The programme provides a comprehensive training in the core areas of management and administration, and places emphasis on the managers role in: providing inspirational leadership, ensuring sustainable success, creating value and building international connectedness.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0250"},"OO0560":{"i":"OO0560","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree with a minimum average grade of B","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the programme will be equipped with a developing understanding of the nature of business through advanced knowledge in one major subject area; and a developing ability to integrate and use their knowledge to make informed business decisions.","graduateProfile":"Internal assessment, examinations.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0560"},"WI0880":{"i":"WI0880","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This conjoint degree gives students the opportunity to complete the requirements of two Bachelors degrees over a reduced period of time. Graduates will have knowledge and skills from both management and law disciplines which gives them a good grounding for careers in many areas.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0880"},"MY0430":{"i":"MY0430","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or equivalent, with good grades.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates can demonstrate scholarly achievement of an acceptable standard in the major subject areas of finance. They possess advanced knowledge, including mastery of sophisticated abstract concepts in finance, and can apply that knowledge in unfamiliar circumstances. Graduates can critically evaluate and summarise knowledge claims, and can undertake supervised research in their finance discipline.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0430"},"AU4063":{"i":"AU4063","strategicPurposeStatement":"MIntBus graduates will demonstrate advanced level skills, knowledge and understanding in a critical mix of practical and theoretical areas of study in international business and strategy and will be well equipped to become professional practitioners in their specialist field.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4063"},"MY0344":{"i":"MY0344","entryRequirements":"1. Admission to the Degree of Master of Agribusiness requires that the candidate will:    (a) meet the University admission requirements as specified; and shall have been:    (b) awarded or qualified for an agricultural or business-related Bachelor's degree having achieved a B+ grade average or higher over the 300-level courses, or equivalent; or    (c) awarded or qualified for a Bachelor's degree or equivalent having achieved a B+ grade average or higher over the 300-level courses and have completed at least three years of relevant work experience; or    (d) awarded or qualified for a Bachelor of AgriCommerce with Honours having achieved Second Class Honours, Division I or higher or a Postgraduate Diploma in Agribusiness having achieved a B+ grade average or higher, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Agribusiness graduates will possess the following skills and attributes that enable them to:    Demonstrate mastery of advanced theoretical subject matter and conduct research in the field of agribusiness and agri-food value chains.    Use appropriate methods, tools and processes to investigate and innovatively tackle complex real world issues.    Communicate clearly and concisely with colleagues, clients and other professionals in the agribusiness domain using appropriate modes in a range of academic, organisational, technical and social contexts.    Identify relevant ethical, socio-cultural, sustainability and environment?issues in research and practice of agribusiness and agri-food value chains.    Participate and collaborate as valued peers with colleagues in the wider domain of agribusiness.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0344"},"LI0391":{"i":"LI0391","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree with appropriate grades.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced skills and knowledge in the applications of commerce to agriculture through postgraduate coursework and research.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0391"},"AK1066":{"i":"AK1066","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Global Business graduates will have advanced their knowledge and skills within the area of international business, and have advanced their personal and professional capabilities.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1066"},"VI00M5":{"i":"VI00M5","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree and at least five years relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced their understanding and skills in management and policy analysis for high-level work in public administration.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00M5"},"WI0881":{"i":"WI0881","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand University Entrance qualification or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"This conjoint degree gives students the opportunity to complete the requirements of two Bachelors degrees over a reduced period of time. Graduates will have knowledge and skills from both management and law disciplines which gives them a good grounding for careers in many areas.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0881"},"VI00J5":{"i":"VI00J5","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree or extensive practical, professional or scholarly experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have an operational and instrumental perspective on the conceptual study of finance and financial management.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00J5"},"AU4061":{"i":"AU4061","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Property or approved equivalent qualification","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipProp graduates will have enhanced their understanding of concepts in Valuation or Property Administration","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4061"},"WI0351":{"i":"WI0351","entryRequirements":"BECom degree or equivalent. Those students who have an honours degree in a relevant field, may take 120 credits to complete the MECom.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a detailed knowledge and understanding of the ecommerce environment in their particular area of interest. They will also have an understanding of the research methodologies appropriate to undertake major research studies in this field and have experience and confidence in the electronic commerce area.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0351"},"VI00U8":{"i":"VI00U8","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree in any discipline and the postgraduate English language requirements of the University.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to reflect critically on philosophical issues in accounting; synthesise and analyse different theoretical approaches to accounting topics; and carry out and communicate independent research on projects relevant to accounting. The MPA meets the academic requirements for pursuing membership of the New Zealand Institute of Chartered Accountants (NZICA) and CPA Australia. Graduates may work in chartered accounting firms, smaller accountancy practices, government organisations, not-for-profit organisations, and commercial enterprises including those offering banking and financial services.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00U8"},"VI004P":{"i":"VI004P","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with at least an average grade of B, and at least two years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MBus(Prof) provides a depth of specific applied business skill to knowledgeable, work experienced people who wish to upskill and will provide students with a technical toolkit in their chosen areas of specialisation. Graduates will integrate a grounding in business studies knowledge with skills and expertise in chosen specialist areas to support a change of track and/or advancement in their career. Some graduates will be able, with appropriate further research preparation, to progress to research-based master's degree or a PhD.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004P"},"OO0502":{"i":"OO0502","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This degree programme will equip students to be practitioners in the profession of accountancy, with accreditation by CAANZ and CPA Australia. In particular, students will: * develop analytical and decision-making skills relating to the discipline of accounting; * develop business advisory abilities; * gain investigative skills in unstructured business situations; and * understand the nature of applied research.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0502"},"VI002Q":{"i":"VI002Q","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or an equivalent qualification, completed with a B- grade average or higher.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a general understanding of core concepts of marketing and management. They will be able to engage in discussion regarding developments in the international business environment, use accounting information for managerial decision-making, communicate complex ideas effectively and accurately, and work effectively and ethically in cross-cultural teams. Graduates may progress to the Master of Global Management (VI002O) or Master of Global Marketing (VI002P); the Postgraduate Certificate in Global Business also acts as an exit qualification from these two degrees.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI002Q"},"VI00E2":{"i":"VI00E2","entryRequirements":"A degree or postgraduate diploma, or extensive appropriate professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will attain strong operational and instrumental perspectives on the subject area of finance; demonstrate critical thinking through their application of financial problem solving and decision making skills; communicate financial information demonstrating sound analytical and technology skills; and have a global perspective with respect to financial issues.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00E2"},"VI004Z":{"i":"VI004Z","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree or Graduate Diploma with an average grade of B+ or better in the relevant subjects, with a major in Actuarial Science, Finance, Statistics or a related field.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGCertActSc graduates will be able to apply advanced actuarial techniques, including big data analysis and asset/liability modelling. They will have a professional-level knowledge of the Actuarial Control Cycle and corporate risk management strategies. Graduates will be well prepared to undertake additional postgraduate study in Actuarial Science. Graduates will be well prepared for professional roles in the actuarial or related fields.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004Z"},"MY0624":{"i":"MY0624","entryRequirements":"Bachelors (Hons) or Masters degree with First Class or Second Class Honours (Division 1) and a sufficient background in senior management.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates have experience and expertise in reflective professional practice. They have the knowledge to conduct original applied research and critical inquiry directed towards the improvement of business and administration. Graduates can independently conduct and present applied research that makes an original contribution to knowledge directed towards the improvement of business and administration.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0624"},"AK1283":{"i":"AK1283","entryRequirements":"An undergraduate degree or a professional qualification equivalent to an undergraduate degree or professional experience equivalent to an undergraduate degree or recognised professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Tourism Studies aims to produce high-calibre graduates who can meet the current and future management demands of the tourism industry and related sectors.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1283"},"AU5725":{"i":"AU5725","entryRequirements":"A relevant Masters degree and passed any prerequisite requirements for the subject intended for this postgraduate certificate with a minimum GPA.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Accounting, Business Analytics, Commercial Law, Economics, Finance, Global Management and Innovation, Information Systems, International Business, Marketing, Management, Operations Management","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5725"},"AK1078":{"i":"AK1078","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent. Relevant professional experience approved as equivalent to a bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PgDipDTL graduates will have comprehensive skills in key aspects of digital transformation and leadership essential for contributing effectively to digital initiatives. They will be able to apply contemporary concepts to drive change within their professional context. Graduates are prepared for further postgraduate study, specifically for entry into the Master of Digital Transformation Leadership. Graduates may contribute to leading digital projects, managing IT functions with a strategic lens, or advising on digital adoption within their sectors.","graduateProfile":"Reports, projects, reflective journals/portfolios, case studies, proposals, presentations.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1078"},"MY0255":{"i":"MY0255","entryRequirements":"Appropriate degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have advanced theoretical and practical knowledge and skills in the areas of quality control, assurance and management. They will be able to apply a variety of analytical tools to analyse business, control quality and improve industrial processes and systems to achieve significant improvement in manufacturing or service delivery capability. They will have a critical awareness of systems thinking and its application to organisational quality and its management. Graduates will be able to communicate effectively, work independently and in teams, and be able to learn effectively and seek appropriate information to further their knowledge and solve organisational problems.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0255"},"AU0429":{"i":"AU0429","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Commerce (Honours), Bachelor of Laws, Bachelor of Laws (Honours), Postgraduate Diploma in Business(Taxation) or an approved equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MTaxS graduates will demonstrate an advanced level of understanding of Taxation and Commercial Law enabling them to specialise in taxation and pursue a career as tax advisors or tax specialists.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0429"},"OO0472":{"i":"OO0472","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's Degree or other acceptable qualification; or equivalent experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides training in business administration and management.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0472"},"AK1091":{"i":"AK1091","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Business Management graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills within the area of business management, and advanced personal and professional capabilities. Graduates from the postgraduate diploma will have the confidence and ability to apply theory to practice, undertake further study in this field and/or to make valuable contributions to business, industry and the community.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1091"},"CN0402":{"i":"CN0402","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree including specified prerequisites.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates with this degree will have advanced analytical, research and communication skills in a chosen commerce subject or subjects. Graduates are well prepared for professional occupations in accounting, finance, information systems, market research, human resource management, economics, consulting; or to pursue further postgraduate study.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0402"},"MY0141":{"i":"MY0141","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Accountancy, with a minimum a B average in the highest level courses, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Accountancy  is an advanced programme of professional education in specialist accounting topics. It gives students the opportunity to hone their research skills, giving the ability to go into a more research-focused qualification such as a master's.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0141"},"MY0355":{"i":"MY0355","entryRequirements":"For post graduate study, information will be sought through the application form supplemented by interview and testing, if necessary, for example, where an applicant has extensive managerial experience but lacks a bachelor degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates from the Massey University Master of Advanced Leadership Practice will develop knowledge, understanding, skills, and other attributes as follows:\n\n\n\r\n1. Demonstrate knowledge and understanding of established and emerging concepts, principles, theories, and philosophies underpinning the broad area of leadership at an individual, team and organisational level. \n\n\n\r\n2. Critically evaluate leadership behaviours, issues and traits, relating these to complex, practical, organisational contexts. \n\n\n\r\n3. Integrate theoretical knowledge informed by current research with in-company leadership behaviours and experiences. \n\n\n\r\n4. Assess the relevance of, and critically reflect on, the application of a range of personal leadership skills in an unfamiliar organisational setting (CSR project). \n\n\n\r\n5. Analyse, critique and reason organisational recommendations in the light of competing theories and current developments relating to leadership development.\n\n\n\r\n6. Make informed judgements from the synthesis of behavioural data and information (both qualitative and quantitative) derived from a diversity of sources, primary and secondary, with a view to enhancing leadership success in an organisational context. \n\n\n\r\n7. Deal creatively with complex, challenging and often ill-defined leadership problems and issues, applying appropriate skills and behaviours. \n\n\n\r\n8. Reflect critically on learning on a continuing basis, integrating academic study and leadership experience, in the light of the organisational context. \n\n\n\r\n9. Synthesise and present arguments and communicate effectively (using both verbal and written mediums) with subject experts: both academics and practising leaders. \n\n\n\r\n10. Work effectively with peers and academic supervisors developing and demonstrating leadership skills in a variety of contexts within their organisation/department or area of work.","developedBy":"Massey University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=MY0355"},"OO0520":{"i":"OO0520","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have advanced academic skills and research abilities within the discipline of international business.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0520"},"CN0437":{"i":"CN0437","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree plus least three years of relevant professional experience in a projectised environment.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will demonstrate mastery of advanced project management principles and practices, synthesising technical, strategic, and contextual knowledge to design, lead, and evaluate complex projects in dynamic environments. They will apply independent, research-informed judgement and advanced analytical methods to manage uncertainty, innovation, and change. Graduates will lead diverse project teams with integrity, communicate effectively for multiple audiences, and engage with stakeholders in culturally responsive ways. They will demonstrate advanced bicultural competence grounded in te ao Maori and Te Tiriti o Waitangi, and contribute to professional practice through critical reflection, ethical leadership, and continuous improvement.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including online quizzes, individual tests and examinations, individual and group essays, assignments and reports, individual journals, incorporating reflective practices, group and individual presentations, literature reviews        and project monitoring and evaluation (progress) reports.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0437"},"AU4027":{"i":"AU4027","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Commerce or an approved equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"BCom(Hons) graduates will have an advanced understanding of business related concepts and will have the ability to analyse and apply these in practical and theoretical settings.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU4027"},"OO0525":{"i":"OO0525","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B- in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have critical understanding and knowledge of core business concepts combined with, and enriched by, an understanding of Maori and Indigenous approaches both to business theory and business practice.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0525"},"VI00D7":{"i":"VI00D7","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or Certificate in Management Studies; three years of relevant work experience; and acceptance by the Programme Director as capable of proceeding with the proposed course of study.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have gained a broad-based management education programme, focusing on marketing management and strategy.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00D7"},"WI1019":{"i":"WI1019","entryRequirements":"Candidates for the Postgraduate Certificate would normally have qualified for the award of a Bachelors Degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Management enables graduates from a wide range of disciplines to have a mastery of management concepts and applied research which they will be able to apply in their chosen occupation","graduateProfile":"Examination or internal assessment","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI1019"},"AK1090":{"i":"AK1090","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree with a B- grade average in papers at level 7 or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Business Management graduates will have integrated theoretical knowledge, research skills and values that will prepare them for management careers within a variety of different organisational settings. This programme will build on a prior undergraduate degree from any discipline and equip graduates with practice interventions to give them the confidence and ability to make meaningful contributions within their respective fields.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1090"},"VI00H8":{"i":"VI00H8","entryRequirements":"Bachelor of Tourism Management or similar degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will have a high level of understanding of the complex phenomenon of tourism, and be able to demonstrate critical thinking, analytical skills and research expertise.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI00H8"},"AU5761":{"i":"AU5761","entryRequirements":"Completed a relevant Bachelors or Bachelors Honours degree with a minimum GPA and MATHS 108 or STATS 108 or equivalent, or a relevant Bachelors degree and 60 points in the Postgraduate Certificate in Applied Finance, or the Postgraduate Diploma in Business in Administration or Business Management with a minimum GPA and 15 relevant course points and completed 15 points from BUSADMIN 763, BUSMAN 707, MATHS 108, STATS 108, or the equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipAppFin graduates will demonstrate advanced capabilities in financial analysis and financial management, and be equipped to progress careers as financial analysts.","graduateProfile":"Assignments, group and individual projects, cases and tests.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5761"},"AU5576":{"i":"AU5576","strategicPurposeStatement":"MHRM graduates will have an advanced set of skills and knowledge in business management and human resource management and have the ability to advance a career in the human resource management profession.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5576"},"LI0121":{"i":"LI0121","entryRequirements":"A relevant undergraduate degree with an average of B+ or higher in 300 level subjects.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the BCom (Honours) will be able to apply advanced business concepts and principles to real world situations.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI0121"},"OO0420":{"i":"OO0420","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree or professional qualification or acceptable training and experience in management.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have the skills and behaviours needed to be a successful international entrepreneur.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0420"},"VI004K":{"i":"VI004K","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or equivalent qualification, completed with a B grade average or higher.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to secure business roles in medium to large organisations, both in New Zealand and overseas. They will understand complex situations in an environment of high uncertainty, and they will be able to provide solutions to business problems at a global strategic level. Graduates will have good oral and written communication skills and will be facilitators of change within organisations. Some graduates will be able, with appropriate further research preparation, to progress to a research-based master's degree or possibly a PhD.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI004K"},"WI0811":{"i":"WI0811","entryRequirements":"A New Zealand university entrance qualification or equivalent","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the BMS(Hons)/ BSc conjoint degree will have knowledge and skills from both management and science disciplines. They will have an understanding of a broad range of management theories and competency in developing, evaluating and critiquing management presentations and reports. They will also have advanced technical ability relevant to their area of specialisation and a depth and breadth of knowledge of science and technology with a capacity to think innovatively and to solve problems.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0811"},"ST4965":{"i":"ST4965","entryRequirements":"Application Criteria Application by Academic Qualification Applicants in this category will have: a) graduated with a degree or honours degree in any discipline from a New Zealand tertiary institution accredited to offer qualifications at this level; o","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Postgraduate Diploma in Business Enterprise aims to produce graduates who will have the ability to deal with issues logically, using knowledge, evaluative skills, resources and available literature as necessary and appropriate. They will be able to: critically evaluate and apply key management principles to the business enterprise sector; source, analyse and evaluate complex information and statistical data; identify, analyse and solve theoretical and practical business problems which impact upon the viability of a product or service; implement highly developed communication skills in compiling effective research papers, reports and business plans; and engage in product and process development at a high level of strategic and operational planning.","developedBy":"Southern Institute of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=ST4965"},"LI7206":{"i":"LI7206","entryRequirements":"An undergraduate qualification in a relevant field achieved at an above average level, usually a B+","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will significantly progress their understanding of the components that make up agricultural systems and how to strategically use components and appropriate methods to leverage innovative systems, products and environments in inter- and trans-disciplinary contexts and settings.  They will understand the role of management in the integration of these components and will be able to utilise appropriate skills to provide relevant advice to agricultural systems practitioners to assist in the operation of sustainable agricultural systems.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7206"},"CN0427":{"i":"CN0427","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or a minimum of five years of practical, professional or scholarly experience of an appropriate kind and a high proficiency in English.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be leaders capable of growing organisations with purpose and impact. They will embrace bicultural competence and a global mindset to lead in an era where digital transformation of organisations underpinned through data leverage, innovation and technology have become core capabilities. They will be creative in generating new ideas, solutions and plans to deliver customer value and where possible activate on entrepreneurial opportunities.  In doing so, these individuals will also demonstrate a consciousness that drives sustainability, whilst being inclusive of the community in which they serve.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0427"},"CN0417":{"i":"CN0417","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will be well-positioned to work in a variety of roles, including financial analyst, investment manager, portfolio manager and risk analyst. They will be well prepared for the subsequent Chartered Financial Analyst [CFA] designation that graduates can choose to apply to complete.  They will have a comprehensive education in financial analysis, portfolio management, equity investments, risk management, ESG considerations and other key areas covered by the CFA curriculum. They will have gained both theoretical and practical knowledge to apply what they learn in real-world settings.","graduateProfile":"A range of assessments will be used including assignments, group projects, presentations, self-directed online modules, tests and exams.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0417"},"AK1045":{"i":"AK1045","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree with a minimum of a B- grade average in papers at Level 7, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The main goal of the Master of Marketing is to develop the knowledge, understanding and skills of non-marketing graduates in order to prepare them for professional marketing roles in business. By adding value and building capabilities on top of a prior undergraduate degree, the proposed Master of Marketing degree will enhance these graduates career opportunities and employment prospects.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1045"},"AU0389":{"i":"AU0389","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor of Commerce or approved equivalent qualification.  Students who have completed a BCom(Hons) or approved equivalent or a PGDipCom may gain admission to the second (thesis) year and take 120 credits to complete this programme.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MCom graduates will have the skills and ability to undertake specialist positions in commerce in the public and private sectors.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0389"},"CN0415":{"i":"CN0415","entryRequirements":"An approved Bachelor's degree","strategicPurposeStatement":"Students completing this qualification will be equipped with generalist knowledge and skills in business management which will enable them to understand the connections between the various disciplines in commerce and apply this knowledge to practice. They will be able to provide academically sound and practically relevant solutions to a range of issues that organisations face.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0415"},"OO0521":{"i":"OO0521","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree with an average grade of at least B+ in the final year of study, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this degree programme will have advanced academic skills and research abilities within the discipline of sustainable business.","graduateProfile":"NA","educationPathway":"NA","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0521"},"LI7771":{"i":"LI7771","entryRequirements":"An undergraduate qualification in a relevant field achieved at an above average level, usually a B or better.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the program will have an advanced understanding of the key aspects of commercial activity and value creation, and a mastery of analytic techniques within the field of Accounting and Finance, to enable them to move seamlessly from study to career.","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7771"},"WI0924":{"i":"WI0924","strategicPurposeStatement":"The Master of Professional Accounting provides the skills, knowledge and competencies that will enable graduates to advance in a professional career in accounting. This degree provides a specialised programme that includes core competencies and skills, advanced research-led knowledge relevant to professional practice and the opportunity for students to become effective contributing professionals to organisations nationally and internationally. Students who complete the programme will obtain the required qualification to gain provisional membership into NZICA, CPA Australia and ACCA.","developedBy":"University of Waikato","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=WI0924"},"PC3424":{"i":"PC3424","entryRequirements":"Applicants require an appropriate Bachelor Level 7 degree in either business, management or a related hospitality area.  Degrees in other disciplines may be considered if the applicant has 2 - 3 years relevant hospitality experience at a supervisory level, or equivalent.  In addition, applicants for whom English is not their first language will have an IELTS score of 6.0, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"The successful graduates will demonstrate advanced knowledge and skills in the fields of business planning, financial management, and product development as related to the Hospitality Industry, and principally the Hotel sector. The graduate will have knowledge and skill in operations planning, human resource management, accountancy, logistics and production management, marketing and communications.","developedBy":"Pacific International Hotel Management School Limited","qualityAssuredBy":"New Zealand Qualifications Authority","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=PC3424"},"AK1046":{"i":"AK1046","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree with a minimum of a B- grade average in papers at Level 7, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Marketing graduates will have advanced their knowledge and skills within the area of marketing, and have advanced their personal and professional capabilities.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1046"},"AU5641":{"i":"AU5641","entryRequirements":"This is an exit qualification. Students must have been enrolled in the Degree of Master of Business Development and passed at least 30 points for that degree and been recommended for admission by the Dean or nominee.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipBusDev graduates will have attained a set of advanced capabilities in a mix of practical and theoretical areas of study related to the processes that underpin the growth and success of business. They will be equipped to progress careers in business development within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5641"},"VI001E":{"i":"VI001E","entryRequirements":"A bachelors degree and at least two years of relevant work experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates will be able to understand, critically analyse, manage and design transformational e-Government initiatives in different institutional settings, apply multidisciplinary e-Government concepts, models, perspectives, frameworks, strategies and policies, and transfer e-Government knowledge across institutional contexts to achieve better government in a particular public management context. They will be qualified to work for governments building e-Government capability or in public management generally. This qualification could lead on to PhD study, but it is likely that most graduates will return to government employment.","developedBy":"Victoria University of Wellington","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=VI001E"},"CN0424":{"i":"CN0424","entryRequirements":"A Bachelor's degree.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of this programme will be equipped with generalist knowledge and skills in business management which will enable them to understand the connections between the various disciplines in commerce and apply this knowledge to practice. They will be able to provide academically sound and practically relevant solutions to a range of issues that organisations face.","developedBy":"University of Canterbury","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=CN0424"},"AU5153":{"i":"AU5153","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree or approved equivalent qualification.","strategicPurposeStatement":"PGDipIntBus graduates will understand the complexities of the environment in which international business takes place.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5153"},"AU0384":{"i":"AU0384","entryRequirements":"Bachelor's degree and two years' experience; or a professional qualification and five years' experience; or eight years' professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MBA graduates will have developed high level managerial skills and abilities enabling them to participate in the local, national and global marketplace","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU0384"},"AK1086":{"i":"AK1086","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Diploma in Supply Chain Management graduates will have advanced knowledge and skills within the area of supply chain management, and advanced personal and professional capabilities. Graduates from the postgraduate diploma will have the confidence and ability to apply industry best practices, undertake further study in this field and/or to make valuable contributions to business, industry and the community.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1086"},"OO0210":{"i":"OO0210","entryRequirements":"A bachelor's degree or other acceptable qualification; or equivalent experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"This part-time executive education programme allows busy professionals to improve their business knowledge and skills, enabling them to successfully lead teams and businesses in a globalised business environment.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0210"},"AU5662":{"i":"AU5662","entryRequirements":"A relevant Bachelors degree with a minimum GPA or a relevant Bachelors degree and passed 60 points in the Postgraduate Certificate in Business Management with a minimum GPA (180-point pathway) or a Bachelor of Commerce (Honours) degree with a minimum GPA or the Postgraduate Diploma in Business in Administration, Business Management or Maori Business Development with a minimum GPA (120-point pathway).","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates of the MBM will demonstrate advanced capabilities in a critical mix of practical and theoretical areas of study related to their area of specialisation in business and management, and be able to apply their analytical and solution-seeking skills to organisational challenges. They will be equipped to progress business management careers within local and international business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5662"},"AK1057":{"i":"AK1057","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelor's degree completed to a merit standard.","strategicPurposeStatement":"MITM graduates will meet the current and future management demands of the tourism industry and related sectors. They will be able to engage analytically, critically and reflectively in their chosen area and progress to doctoral study.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1057"},"AU5530":{"i":"AU5530","entryRequirements":"A relevant bachelors degree with a minimum Grade Point Average (GPA), or an approved equivalent qualification, or relevant professional experience.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Postgraduate Certificate in Management graduates will have a core of knowledge and skills in Business and have a platform from which they can either seek opportunities to further their studies in Business or enter an entry-level position in a generic non-specialist role in Business.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5530"},"AU5533":{"i":"AU5533","strategicPurposeStatement":"Graduates with a Master of Marketing will have an advanced set of skills and knowledge in business and marketing and have the ability to advance a career in the marketing industry.","developedBy":"University of Auckland","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AU5533"},"OO0319":{"i":"OO0319","entryRequirements":"Degree or a professional qualification requiring at least 3 years tertiary study","strategicPurposeStatement":"This diploma provides skills in Health management for clinical leaders who may find themselves involved in determining the strategic direction and general management of large health organisations.","developedBy":"University of Otago","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=OO0319"},"LI7345":{"i":"LI7345","developedBy":"Lincoln University","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=LI7345"},"AK1085":{"i":"AK1085","entryRequirements":"Must have completed a bachelor's degree with a minimum B- grade average in papers at level 7, or equivalent.","strategicPurposeStatement":"Master of Supply Chain Management graduates will have integrated theoretical knowledge, in-depth understanding of industry best practices and values that will prepare them for supply chain management careers within a variety of different organisational settings. This programme will build on a prior undergraduate degree from any discipline and equip graduates with principles, knowledge, techniques, philosophy and practice interventions to give them the confidence and ability to make meaningful contributions within the field of supply chain management.","developedBy":"Auckland University of Technology","qualityAssuredBy":"Committee on University Academic Programmes","nzqaLink":"https://www.nzqa.govt.nz/nzqf/search/viewQualification.do?selectedItemKey=AK1085"}};
